1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:03,433
(The men's first-impression picks
on the first night)

2
00:00:03,827 --> 00:00:05,027
Ye In?

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,294
(In Joong chose Ye In for a date.)

4
00:00:07,394 --> 00:00:08,594
We'll be right back.

5
00:00:08,678 --> 00:00:09,660
In 10 minutes.

6
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,227
Would you like to join me, Yu Ra?

7
00:00:11,294 --> 00:00:13,060
(Dong Su chose Yu Ra.)

8
00:00:13,827 --> 00:00:15,060
Min Seo?

9
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,460
(Jin Sung chose Min Seo.)

10
00:00:16,527 --> 00:00:17,727
Shall we go, Ye In?

11
00:00:17,827 --> 00:00:19,760
(Ji Hwan chose Ye In.)

12
00:00:20,994 --> 00:00:26,694
(One person stayed seated
until everyone made their picks.)

13
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,794
(No one chose Jwa Hyeon.)

14
00:00:33,527 --> 00:00:40,360
I knew I might not get chosen
in first-impression picks,

15
00:00:40,727 --> 00:00:42,627
but the moment I got zero votes,

16
00:00:43,594 --> 00:00:44,960
I saw my brother.

17
00:00:45,527 --> 00:00:47,794
He told me there was a chance...

18
00:00:47,927 --> 00:00:51,294
I might not get any votes.

19
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:54,194
So I thought he'd smirk at me.

20
00:00:54,694 --> 00:00:56,459
Maybe like this.

21
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:57,827
But...

22
00:00:59,527 --> 00:01:02,494
How should I put it?

23
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,194
He looked so uncomfortable.

24
00:01:17,227 --> 00:01:19,527
(Who could Jwa Hyeon's
uncomfortable sibling be?)

25
00:01:23,694 --> 00:01:27,127
I was walking up the stairs,
and someone tapped my back.

26
00:01:28,827 --> 00:01:30,160
I turned back,

27
00:01:30,994 --> 00:01:32,127
and it was my brother.

28
00:01:33,027 --> 00:01:34,427
He said, "It's okay."

29
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:38,494
Really?

30
00:01:38,594 --> 00:01:40,127
That would make her tear up!

31
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:43,059
Oh, my. He told her it's okay.

32
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:44,626
- She'd probably cry.
- It'd mean so much to her.

33
00:01:44,627 --> 00:01:45,627
I guess she was hurt.

34
00:01:45,927 --> 00:01:48,159
Usually, unlike at home,

35
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:50,127
- they're on your side on the outside.
- Exactly.

36
00:01:50,827 --> 00:01:52,126
That was touching.

37
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:53,194
I'm tearing up.

38
00:01:54,027 --> 00:01:57,094
The fact that he cared about me...

39
00:01:57,194 --> 00:01:58,327
really moved me.

40
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,294
I honestly thought he'd make fun of me.

41
00:02:03,327 --> 00:02:04,960
So I thought, "Look at him!"

42
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:08,160
"My brother is such a sweetheart."

43
00:02:10,827 --> 00:02:12,027
I didn't expect that!

44
00:02:13,427 --> 00:02:16,560
But his kindness really got to me.

45
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:19,459
I guess he was looking out for you.

46
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,527
Yes, I think so too.
So I was really touched.

47
00:02:22,727 --> 00:02:29,494
I'm actually moved
by my own brother, of all people.

48
00:02:32,827 --> 00:02:37,227
(Who's the sibling
that brought Jwa Hyeon to tears?)

49
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,160
I wonder who.

50
00:02:39,194 --> 00:02:40,560
My guess is Jin Sung.

51
00:02:40,627 --> 00:02:42,994
I also think it's Jin Sung,

52
00:02:43,027 --> 00:02:45,194
judging by how he comforted her.

53
00:02:45,227 --> 00:02:47,427
That does sound like Jin Sung,
comforting her from behind.

54
00:02:47,494 --> 00:02:50,893
The guy who'd tap gently
and say something sweet...

55
00:02:50,894 --> 00:02:52,327
- Who is it?
- might be Ji Hwan for me.

56
00:02:52,894 --> 00:02:56,127
If Ji Hwan tries to comfort her
from behind,

57
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,594
- she'd have already left.
- I get it!

58
00:02:59,494 --> 00:03:00,994
- I see it.
- Give me a break!

59
00:03:01,027 --> 00:03:02,694
He can only do it face-to-face.

60
00:03:02,727 --> 00:03:06,360
No one looks like Jwa Hyeon,
but it has to be one of them.

61
00:03:06,427 --> 00:03:09,060
- For Season Two, I'm just stumped.
- I have no idea!

62
00:03:09,094 --> 00:03:11,060
How can a brother be that sweet?

63
00:03:11,448 --> 00:03:14,327
(After the 10-minute chats in the cabin,)

64
00:03:18,764 --> 00:03:21,894
(Jwa Hyeon heads upstairs.)

65
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,727
- Here it comes!
- For real?

66
00:03:31,260 --> 00:03:33,094
- I told you!
- You're right!

67
00:03:33,127 --> 00:03:34,894
I told you it was him!

68
00:03:35,427 --> 00:03:37,626
He must've felt even worse,

69
00:03:37,627 --> 00:03:39,394
- since he got all the votes.
- I know.

70
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,260
One has zero votes,
while the other is a popular guy.

71
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,327
I feel...

72
00:03:49,460 --> 00:03:50,460
(Sighing)

73
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:52,260
Seriously.

74
00:03:52,261 --> 00:03:53,294
Just as I expected.

75
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,260
I honestly didn't see that coming.

76
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:00,127
(Jwa Hyeon's brother is Ji Hwan.)

77
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:05,327
Do you think I treated them...

78
00:04:06,294 --> 00:04:07,560
more like a friend?

79
00:04:08,094 --> 00:04:09,760
Don't think that way.

80
00:04:10,227 --> 00:04:11,927
I think I was more like an emcee.

81
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:13,427
It was just a first impression.

82
00:04:15,994 --> 00:04:17,627
I acted way too much like an emcee!

83
00:04:18,860 --> 00:04:20,394
I'm always like this.

84
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:24,827
It's always the same, I swear.

85
00:04:33,194 --> 00:04:37,760
The Jwa Hyeon I know is
a really devoted person.

86
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:39,894
And she gets hurt so easily.

87
00:04:40,194 --> 00:04:42,927
She didn't use to be like that,

88
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:45,227
but she gets hurt whenever she dates.

89
00:04:45,394 --> 00:04:47,259
She may seem tough on the outside,

90
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:49,527
but deep down,

91
00:04:49,727 --> 00:04:51,094
she's very soft-hearted.

92
00:04:52,327 --> 00:04:56,460
When I was young,
my sister treated me like her own son.

93
00:04:57,227 --> 00:04:59,627
Then gradually,

94
00:05:01,294 --> 00:05:04,394
we became more like friends at some point.

95
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:09,494
I thought I should be there for her now.

96
00:05:10,094 --> 00:05:13,160
Maybe I could help her too.

97
00:05:13,227 --> 00:05:16,759
Wow, I can't believe
there's a brother like him!

98
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:19,260
I know. Why are they all so sweet?

99
00:05:19,327 --> 00:05:21,760
- He's straight out of a fairytale.
- Exactly.

100
00:05:23,994 --> 00:05:29,227
(Little Jwa Hyeon looked after Ji Hwan.)

101
00:05:32,527 --> 00:05:38,060
(They've grown up
to be there for each other.)

102
00:05:44,694 --> 00:05:47,627
I'm the eldest,
and I have one younger sister too.

103
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:48,694
Ji Hwan is the youngest.

104
00:05:49,494 --> 00:05:51,527
The three of you, stay like that.

105
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:52,960
Here?

106
00:05:56,427 --> 00:05:58,660
He's a newborn angel!

107
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,394
Our little angel!

108
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,560
What are you doing, angel?

109
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:09,294
That's dangerous, angel.

110
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:21,794
What kind of person is your sibling?

111
00:06:23,001 --> 00:06:27,727
He's really thoughtful, kind,
and diligent.

112
00:06:27,827 --> 00:06:30,327
But he's no fun.

113
00:06:31,194 --> 00:06:32,260
For sure.

114
00:06:32,627 --> 00:06:34,827
Ji Hwan is handsome,

115
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:36,860
but that doesn't give him an advantage.

116
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,694
You can't depend on your looks alone,

117
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:42,727
but he's been relying
on his looks way too much.

118
00:06:42,794 --> 00:06:44,494
He's good-looking, that's why.

119
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,027
However,

120
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:47,559
that's not how dating works.

121
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:50,660
I try my absolute best
to make someone laugh.

122
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:54,222
So I told him he should learn
how to be funny too,

123
00:06:54,223 --> 00:06:55,556
but he ignored me right away.

124
00:06:55,623 --> 00:06:57,423
Has he always been popular?

125
00:06:58,056 --> 00:06:59,123
Ji Hwan?

126
00:06:59,223 --> 00:07:00,923
I bet he's never dated anyone.

127
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:03,723
He barely has any experience for his age.

128
00:07:04,323 --> 00:07:07,923
And he's not the type to go out,
unless he gets an opportunity like this.

129
00:07:08,056 --> 00:07:09,656
He was never really popular.

130
00:07:10,923 --> 00:07:13,156
He's not really quick-witted.

131
00:07:13,190 --> 00:07:14,556
Maybe he is when he's dating.

132
00:07:15,244 --> 00:07:16,056
Him?

133
00:07:16,584 --> 00:07:17,890
He could quickly go
after his love interest.

134
00:07:17,923 --> 00:07:19,190
I swear.

135
00:07:19,223 --> 00:07:22,156
What I want to see most on this show is...

136
00:07:22,256 --> 00:07:25,756
my brother quickly spotting
the girl he's interested in,

137
00:07:25,923 --> 00:07:27,923
making a move first,
and even getting rejected.

138
00:07:28,023 --> 00:07:30,256
If a woman is interested in him,

139
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:32,723
that's when he finally finds out.

140
00:07:32,756 --> 00:07:35,890
I've never seen him like someone first.

141
00:07:36,356 --> 00:07:39,556
I've only been in two relationships.

142
00:07:39,623 --> 00:07:42,223
- When was the last time you dated?
- Four years ago?

143
00:07:42,923 --> 00:07:46,890
If we're counting brief relationships,
it was four years ago.

144
00:07:46,990 --> 00:07:49,589
Or maybe six.

145
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:50,789
(It was actually six years ago.)

146
00:07:50,790 --> 00:07:53,990
I wouldn't have come here
if I were going to date the way I do.

147
00:07:54,356 --> 00:07:58,923
I thought I'd never date anyone
if it weren't for this opportunity,

148
00:07:58,956 --> 00:08:01,489
so if I become interested in someone,

149
00:08:01,490 --> 00:08:05,589
I'm going to make the first move
without a second thought.

150
00:08:05,590 --> 00:08:07,490
Have you ever met
one of your sister's exes?

151
00:08:07,823 --> 00:08:08,823
Yes.

152
00:08:09,356 --> 00:08:10,356
But well...

153
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:12,623
I was a little...

154
00:08:14,990 --> 00:08:16,623
Maybe it's my personality,

155
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:20,523
but I don't really like
wild and flashy guys,

156
00:08:20,556 --> 00:08:23,123
especially when it comes
to my sister's boyfriend.

157
00:08:24,123 --> 00:08:26,190
First impressions are crucial, right?

158
00:08:27,023 --> 00:08:31,490
But after talking to him a little,
I feel like something is off about him.

159
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:34,656
Still, I trust that Jwa Hyeon knows
what she's doing.

160
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:37,990
But I strongly believe
Ji Hwan takes a lot after our dad.

161
00:08:38,056 --> 00:08:40,323
Our dad was an athlete,
and Ji Hwan is one too.

162
00:08:40,456 --> 00:08:42,356
He told him he must watch how he behaves.

163
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:44,256
If he acted badly,

164
00:08:44,323 --> 00:08:48,190
people would judge all athletes
the same way,

165
00:08:48,223 --> 00:08:50,089
so he had to be careful.

166
00:08:50,090 --> 00:08:51,090
Right.

167
00:08:51,091 --> 00:08:53,256
- I had to wear my school tie properly.
- Yes.

168
00:08:53,290 --> 00:08:55,490
My jacket had to be buttoned,
even when it was hot.

169
00:08:55,590 --> 00:08:56,855
I also had to mind table manners...

170
00:08:56,856 --> 00:08:58,723
- and use chopsticks correctly.
- Right.

171
00:08:58,756 --> 00:09:01,856
He said, "You're an athlete,
so once you step out of line,"

172
00:09:02,090 --> 00:09:03,456
"you'll be seen as a thug."

173
00:09:03,556 --> 00:09:04,655
Yes. It's true.

174
00:09:04,656 --> 00:09:07,423
(How he learned to spot thugs)

175
00:09:08,423 --> 00:09:12,190
He may be too uptight and a bit boring,

176
00:09:12,223 --> 00:09:13,956
but he's very reliable.

177
00:09:14,156 --> 00:09:16,156
He's not the type to betray anyone.

178
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:19,523
If he teases someone,
despite his personality,

179
00:09:19,656 --> 00:09:21,256
even if it's subtle and boring,

180
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:23,590
it'd be super obvious to me.

181
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:25,590
Ji Hwan is working up the courage.

182
00:09:27,090 --> 00:09:28,356
Make her laugh.

183
00:09:28,590 --> 00:09:30,023
You just have to be funny.

184
00:09:30,256 --> 00:09:34,389
Once you click with Jwa Hyeon,
everything falls into place.

185
00:09:34,390 --> 00:09:35,823
I'm sure he'll do great.

186
00:09:36,623 --> 00:09:37,690
I'm right here.

187
00:09:52,156 --> 00:09:54,256
You should've held me!

188
00:09:54,474 --> 00:09:55,356
No!

189
00:09:58,987 --> 00:09:59,856
No!

190
00:09:59,857 --> 00:10:01,323
Run, hurry!

191
00:10:01,956 --> 00:10:02,990
Like Dad.

192
00:10:03,056 --> 00:10:04,056
Dad.

193
00:10:08,890 --> 00:10:10,423
You really are Dad's daughter.

194
00:10:11,323 --> 00:10:14,323
(Kim Jwa Hyeon)

195
00:10:16,590 --> 00:10:19,623
(Kim Ji Hwan)

196
00:10:20,123 --> 00:10:21,623
Why am I so thrilled over this?

197
00:10:21,647 --> 00:10:23,414
Just like Dad.

198
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:25,610
(Men's first-impression picks tonight)

199
00:10:25,611 --> 00:10:26,478
Later.

200
00:10:27,046 --> 00:10:27,879
Min Seo?

201
00:10:28,347 --> 00:10:31,249
(No one picked Jwa Hyeon.)

202
00:10:32,585 --> 00:10:34,819
(Ji Hwan watched his sister.)

203
00:10:36,689 --> 00:10:38,390
I went last.

204
00:10:39,225 --> 00:10:42,461
My sister still hadn't been picked,

205
00:10:42,462 --> 00:10:44,062
even after the third guy went.

206
00:10:45,064 --> 00:10:48,566
It was hard to keep a straight face.

207
00:10:52,405 --> 00:10:54,373
I couldn't pick my own sister.

208
00:10:55,108 --> 00:10:59,744
I was pretty upset and angry about it.

209
00:11:02,148 --> 00:11:03,081
I put it on the right.

210
00:11:06,019 --> 00:11:08,420
I saw it happen right in front of me.

211
00:11:09,755 --> 00:11:10,922
How is this happening?

212
00:11:11,024 --> 00:11:13,592
"Why isn't anyone picking my sister?"

213
00:11:16,829 --> 00:11:20,198
Dating has always come easy to her.

214
00:11:20,365 --> 00:11:23,635
I've always seen her as popular and cool.

215
00:11:26,672 --> 00:11:28,539
I didn't get it, and it made me mad.

216
00:11:30,376 --> 00:11:31,776
Really,

217
00:11:33,079 --> 00:11:36,314
she might've cried if she'd been alone.

218
00:11:38,684 --> 00:11:42,587
(Their first night in the house ends.)

219
00:11:43,089 --> 00:11:45,157
They're saying the same things
as in Season One.

220
00:11:45,191 --> 00:11:46,758
It's exactly the same.

221
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:47,759
That's so sweet.

222
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,128
- But it's only been a day, right?
- Right.

223
00:11:57,937 --> 00:12:00,171
(In Joong)

224
00:12:03,309 --> 00:12:05,410
(Min Seo)

225
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,447
(Yu Ra)

226
00:12:12,652 --> 00:12:14,252
(Ji Hwan)

227
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:19,057
(Ye In)

228
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:23,261
(Jwa Hyeon)

229
00:12:26,299 --> 00:12:28,100
(Dong Su)

230
00:12:30,670 --> 00:12:32,971
(Jin Sung)

231
00:12:41,414 --> 00:12:46,118
(My Sibling's Romance 2)

232
00:12:47,153 --> 00:12:51,189
(Episode 2: No one picked you.)

233
00:12:52,658 --> 00:12:54,425
(The next morning)

234
00:12:57,930 --> 00:13:00,365
(The women's room on the third floor)

235
00:13:01,033 --> 00:13:03,835
(Jwa Hyeon wakes up.)

236
00:13:05,371 --> 00:13:06,538
I need to get up.

237
00:13:09,185 --> 00:13:11,109
Ye In is such a sleepy baby.

238
00:13:11,110 --> 00:13:12,244
(Ye In wakes up.)

239
00:13:13,346 --> 00:13:15,748
(Min Seo wakes up.)

240
00:13:15,749 --> 00:13:16,815
You're sleepy, right?

241
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:19,218
(Yu Ra's bed)

242
00:13:19,219 --> 00:13:20,452
Is Yu Ra back?

243
00:13:20,453 --> 00:13:22,154
(Shaking her head)

244
00:13:22,888 --> 00:13:23,754
(At the Love Hideout)

245
00:13:23,755 --> 00:13:24,622
Ever played guitar?

246
00:13:26,926 --> 00:13:28,460
I bought one a while back.

247
00:13:28,661 --> 00:13:31,963
I messed around with it for a month.

248
00:13:34,734 --> 00:13:35,634
No way.

249
00:13:36,636 --> 00:13:38,103
- Sounds fun.
- I'm jealous.

250
00:13:38,337 --> 00:13:39,437
That's fun.

251
00:13:40,606 --> 00:13:41,773
I'll tease them later.

252
00:13:42,276 --> 00:13:43,341
Seriously.

253
00:13:43,776 --> 00:13:46,811
(Men's room on the third floor)

254
00:13:49,016 --> 00:13:51,416
(Reducing puffiness)

255
00:13:52,818 --> 00:13:55,253
(Patting on lotion)

256
00:13:56,856 --> 00:13:58,990
(Applying some hair serum)

257
00:14:04,887 --> 00:14:08,900
(A busy morning for the two men)

258
00:14:09,435 --> 00:14:12,437
Men, it's time
for your first-impression picks.

259
00:14:12,638 --> 00:14:14,539
(In Joong picked Ye In.)

260
00:14:15,875 --> 00:14:18,977
(Ji Hwan picked Ye In too.)

261
00:14:19,279 --> 00:14:20,345
We are not allowed to talk.

262
00:14:21,747 --> 00:14:23,081
Did you bulk up at the gym?

263
00:14:23,949 --> 00:14:24,815
I did.

264
00:14:25,619 --> 00:14:27,553
So it's not just your natural build?

265
00:14:27,554 --> 00:14:29,755
You've got a naturally wide frame.

266
00:14:30,189 --> 00:14:32,023
I'm always grateful to my parents.

267
00:14:34,494 --> 00:14:36,695
They're all rivals, but if I had to pick,

268
00:14:37,563 --> 00:14:38,496
I'd say, Ji Hwan.

269
00:14:39,398 --> 00:14:40,732
Ji Hwan is the coolest.

270
00:14:41,135 --> 00:14:44,269
He's soft-spoken. His words carry weight.

271
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:46,805
And Ye In is pretty laid-back.

272
00:14:47,273 --> 00:14:50,375
She'd feel most at ease with Ji Hwan.

273
00:14:50,710 --> 00:14:51,609
He's my competition.

274
00:14:52,111 --> 00:14:53,611
(Which guy is your biggest rival?)

275
00:14:53,612 --> 00:14:54,679
In Joong.

276
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,948
- They're rivals.
- They both.

277
00:14:56,949 --> 00:14:59,684
- They both see each other as rivals.
- They do.

278
00:15:00,086 --> 00:15:01,153
In Joong.

279
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,354
He's got a strong presence.

280
00:15:03,355 --> 00:15:07,091
But he's also got
this warm way of talking...

281
00:15:07,092 --> 00:15:08,693
and a quick wit.

282
00:15:08,694 --> 00:15:11,796
The women will pick up on that too.

283
00:15:12,331 --> 00:15:13,731
I'm keeping an eye on him.

284
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:16,101
Should we take a photo?

285
00:15:16,435 --> 00:15:17,635
I'll get one of each of you.

286
00:15:17,803 --> 00:15:19,570
- Me?
- That looked good.

287
00:15:20,773 --> 00:15:21,740
Is it my turn?

288
00:15:21,741 --> 00:15:23,475
(Taking a photo of his rival)

289
00:15:23,476 --> 00:15:24,909
One, two, three.

290
00:15:25,945 --> 00:15:27,279
(Posing for his rival)

291
00:15:27,280 --> 00:15:28,213
KANU Coffee.

292
00:15:33,386 --> 00:15:35,320
We've gotta talk politely again now.

293
00:15:35,688 --> 00:15:36,621
Right.

294
00:15:36,789 --> 00:15:39,090
And what happened here stays between us.

295
00:15:39,525 --> 00:15:41,693
I like that. It's our own little secret.

296
00:15:41,861 --> 00:15:42,927
I like it too.

297
00:15:43,596 --> 00:15:46,130
We're the only ones who've been here.

298
00:15:46,131 --> 00:15:47,398
Only we know how it looks.

299
00:15:47,399 --> 00:15:48,433
(First Hideout guests)

300
00:15:48,434 --> 00:15:49,334
Right.

301
00:15:49,702 --> 00:15:51,169
Casual speech makes a difference.

302
00:15:51,503 --> 00:15:53,004
- You get close fast, right?
- Right.

303
00:15:53,706 --> 00:15:55,640
I guess the code changes every day.

304
00:15:56,008 --> 00:15:56,941
- Really?
- Yes.

305
00:15:57,676 --> 00:15:59,477
- It's so nice out.
- It is.

306
00:16:00,413 --> 00:16:01,646
Two seconds per move.

307
00:16:01,647 --> 00:16:02,881
- Two seconds? Sure.
- One.

308
00:16:02,882 --> 00:16:03,849
- Should be fun.
- Two.

309
00:16:03,850 --> 00:16:05,117
- One, two.
- Two.

310
00:16:06,419 --> 00:16:07,352
Two. What?

311
00:16:07,353 --> 00:16:08,220
(Peeking in)

312
00:16:08,221 --> 00:16:09,354
- Oh.
- Why are you here?

313
00:16:10,056 --> 00:16:12,290
- How was it?
- You stayed out this long?

314
00:16:12,291 --> 00:16:13,625
So it was just you two?

315
00:16:13,626 --> 00:16:15,960
Turns out there was a checkout time.

316
00:16:16,228 --> 00:16:18,729
We were gonna storm in
if you weren't back by noon.

317
00:16:18,730 --> 00:16:20,397
- It took you ages.
- We were about to go.

318
00:16:20,398 --> 00:16:21,831
You wouldn't have gotten in.

319
00:16:21,832 --> 00:16:22,900
They had a guard.

320
00:16:22,901 --> 00:16:25,937
I'm going to grab some clothes.

321
00:16:27,006 --> 00:16:28,807
- No one's in here, right?
- Right.

322
00:16:30,277 --> 00:16:31,910
You had drinks.

323
00:16:32,211 --> 00:16:33,211
No.

324
00:16:35,047 --> 00:16:36,314
How was it?

325
00:16:37,082 --> 00:16:38,816
I bet they had good food, right?

326
00:16:39,985 --> 00:16:41,118
I can't tell you that.

327
00:16:41,821 --> 00:16:42,821
It's all a secret?

328
00:16:42,822 --> 00:16:43,440
(Top secret)

329
00:16:44,256 --> 00:16:46,224
You had grilled meat, didn't you?

330
00:16:46,225 --> 00:16:47,191
What?

331
00:16:47,593 --> 00:16:49,394
Well...

332
00:16:49,395 --> 00:16:50,261
- I don't know.
- Sashimi?

333
00:16:51,831 --> 00:16:54,533
I'm dying to know
how Dong Su's night went.

334
00:16:54,534 --> 00:16:56,568
He went to bed at 2 a.m.
and got up at 4 a.m.

335
00:16:56,569 --> 00:16:57,736
Really?

336
00:16:57,737 --> 00:16:59,171
(Word starts getting around.)

337
00:17:00,272 --> 00:17:01,739
(In walks the man himself.)

338
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,140
Did everyone sleep well?

339
00:17:03,141 --> 00:17:05,009
I heard you didn't sleep much, Dong Su.

340
00:17:05,110 --> 00:17:06,243
- Yes.
- Really?

341
00:17:06,812 --> 00:17:08,446
Did you have a good time?

342
00:17:11,951 --> 00:17:13,251
That's a shy smile.

343
00:17:14,887 --> 00:17:17,021
There were upsides and downsides, I think.

344
00:17:17,022 --> 00:17:19,057
It's physically tiring, for sure.

345
00:17:19,959 --> 00:17:22,227
What's it like? Is it nice in there?

346
00:17:22,862 --> 00:17:26,097
(All ears)

347
00:17:26,098 --> 00:17:27,265
They said to keep it a secret.

348
00:17:28,133 --> 00:17:30,034
- Really?
- Of course it's a secret.

349
00:17:30,269 --> 00:17:34,138
Is the bed like the ones in our room?

350
00:17:34,406 --> 00:17:36,708
Really? It wasn't just a mattress topper?

351
00:17:36,709 --> 00:17:38,309
Was there a bed frame?

352
00:17:38,310 --> 00:17:40,144
Come on, that's a secret.

353
00:17:40,145 --> 00:17:41,112
It's a secret.

354
00:17:41,914 --> 00:17:44,983
We losers should just sit quietly.

355
00:17:45,618 --> 00:17:47,618
- Right.
- I'd recommend going.

356
00:17:49,321 --> 00:17:51,155
I had no makeup on the whole time.

357
00:17:51,691 --> 00:17:52,591
You went barefaced?

358
00:17:53,192 --> 00:17:55,594
(Whimpering)

359
00:17:55,595 --> 00:17:57,862
- You did?
- I didn't want to either.

360
00:17:58,998 --> 00:18:01,132
Do I look better with or without contacts?

361
00:18:02,935 --> 00:18:04,369
(Looking closely)

362
00:18:04,370 --> 00:18:05,570
- With.
- With them in?

363
00:18:06,839 --> 00:18:08,575
This morning, Min Seo asked me,

364
00:18:08,576 --> 00:18:10,376
"Should I put my contacts in?"

365
00:18:10,377 --> 00:18:12,343
So I took a good look at her.

366
00:18:12,344 --> 00:18:13,812
Wait.

367
00:18:13,813 --> 00:18:14,746
Hold on, your eyes.

368
00:18:15,347 --> 00:18:17,715
"Your eyes are so light," I told her.

369
00:18:18,117 --> 00:18:19,584
(At the Love Hideout this morning)

370
00:18:19,585 --> 00:18:20,952
Your eyes are so brown.

371
00:18:21,354 --> 00:18:24,756
At the hideout, I noticed
how light Dong Su's eyes were.

372
00:18:25,224 --> 00:18:26,991
(Strikingly similar...)

373
00:18:26,992 --> 00:18:29,227
(brown eyes)

374
00:18:29,662 --> 00:18:31,096
I think those two are siblings.

375
00:18:33,132 --> 00:18:34,232
That's how she knows?

376
00:18:34,233 --> 00:18:36,468
- Brown eyes.
- Their eyes are a similar shade.

377
00:18:36,469 --> 00:18:37,669
(Their eyes gave them away.)

378
00:18:37,903 --> 00:18:40,071
She's quick, as usual. Yu Ra's sharp.

379
00:18:40,472 --> 00:18:43,274
I went from Dong Su and Ye In
to Min Seo and Dong Su.

380
00:18:43,275 --> 00:18:44,909
I've changed my guess.

381
00:18:45,011 --> 00:18:46,077
They're siblings.

382
00:18:46,912 --> 00:18:48,846
Your eyes are naturally really light.

383
00:18:48,847 --> 00:18:49,981
They are.

384
00:18:51,617 --> 00:18:54,119
(Meanwhile, Ji Hwan plays Go alone.)

385
00:18:54,687 --> 00:18:56,855
(Deep in thought)

386
00:18:58,557 --> 00:19:00,992
(Spotting her brother)

387
00:19:01,160 --> 00:19:02,961
(Jwa Hyeon laughs.)

388
00:19:05,064 --> 00:19:05,964
You okay?

389
00:19:08,968 --> 00:19:09,801
Playing Go?

390
00:19:10,603 --> 00:19:11,469
Omok.

391
00:19:13,672 --> 00:19:15,973
And quit making it so obvious, will you?

392
00:19:15,974 --> 00:19:17,642
Anyone can tell we're siblings.

393
00:19:17,643 --> 00:19:18,543
I already know.

394
00:19:18,544 --> 00:19:19,944
I think I know who's related.

395
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,547
Still, cut it out.

396
00:19:28,854 --> 00:19:31,088
(Ye In walks in.)

397
00:19:31,490 --> 00:19:32,390
What are you up to?

398
00:19:33,425 --> 00:19:35,226
(She spots Ji Hwan.)

399
00:19:35,227 --> 00:19:36,527
Are you playing by yourself?

400
00:19:37,896 --> 00:19:40,498
I like playing five in a row by myself.

401
00:19:42,101 --> 00:19:46,337
(She overhears her brother talking
about his hobby.)

402
00:19:46,672 --> 00:19:48,773
- Five in a row?
- Yes.

403
00:19:49,675 --> 00:19:53,011
I have a quick errand.
Do you want to play when I'm back?

404
00:19:53,312 --> 00:19:54,379
Sure, I'd love to.

405
00:19:55,581 --> 00:19:57,582
I've never seen anyone play alone.

406
00:20:01,687 --> 00:20:02,920
(Snickering)

407
00:20:04,324 --> 00:20:05,938
"I like playing Omok by myself."

408
00:20:05,939 --> 00:20:07,060
Since when has he ever played Omok?

409
00:20:07,259 --> 00:20:08,829
I've seriously never seen him do that
in my life.

410
00:20:12,866 --> 00:20:13,801
What are you playing, Ji Hwan?

411
00:20:14,779 --> 00:20:16,103
Omok or Go?

412
00:20:16,606 --> 00:20:17,638
Omok.

413
00:20:18,105 --> 00:20:18,972
Can I join?

414
00:20:19,759 --> 00:20:21,909
Ye In is on her way to play.

415
00:20:22,286 --> 00:20:23,820
- Who?
- Ye In.

416
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:24,812
Oh, okay.

417
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:27,506
Maybe she felt sorry for me...

418
00:20:27,933 --> 00:20:29,933
when she saw me playing Omok alone.

419
00:20:31,533 --> 00:20:34,291
(The two men who chose Ye In play Omok.)

420
00:20:39,137 --> 00:20:40,997
Double three. Three white stones.

421
00:20:42,397 --> 00:20:43,697
(Glancing)

422
00:20:46,034 --> 00:20:47,355
(Glancing)

423
00:20:48,129 --> 00:20:49,203
How are you so good at this?

424
00:20:51,609 --> 00:20:53,562
(Ye In finally arrives.)

425
00:20:53,995 --> 00:20:55,967
- Shall we play Halli Galli, then?
- Sure.

426
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:57,978
- No getting upset if you lose.
- Of course.

427
00:20:59,102 --> 00:21:00,914
When guys play Halli Galli together,

428
00:21:01,648 --> 00:21:04,515
we usually have to buy
a new bell after every game.

429
00:21:05,408 --> 00:21:06,315
Because we hit it so hard!

430
00:21:07,122 --> 00:21:09,342
(Taking off her rings)

431
00:21:09,595 --> 00:21:10,691
You're even taking off your rings!

432
00:21:12,125 --> 00:21:13,594
- I'll go first.
- Okay.

433
00:21:14,442 --> 00:21:15,529
Oh, I'm nervous.

434
00:21:19,009 --> 00:21:20,055
(In Joong is the fastest.)

435
00:21:21,715 --> 00:21:22,669
You're quick.

436
00:21:22,671 --> 00:21:23,704
I'll start this round.

437
00:21:25,915 --> 00:21:27,153
(He hesitates.)

438
00:21:27,155 --> 00:21:28,308
Oh, you scared me.

439
00:21:29,910 --> 00:21:30,878
(Clearing her throat)

440
00:21:31,683 --> 00:21:33,123
(In Joong is faster again.)

441
00:21:33,590 --> 00:21:35,616
- You're really good at this.
- He really is.

442
00:21:35,916 --> 00:21:36,817
Thank you.

443
00:21:37,003 --> 00:21:37,885
Where did it go?

444
00:21:37,887 --> 00:21:38,655
(Just because)

445
00:21:40,603 --> 00:21:42,416
This is such an interesting dynamic.

446
00:21:42,417 --> 00:21:43,590
Why do things keep going like this?

447
00:21:43,592 --> 00:21:45,392
Even their personalities are different.

448
00:21:45,394 --> 00:21:46,197
I know!

449
00:21:46,198 --> 00:21:48,528
In Joong plays Halli Galli,
while Ji Hwan plays Omok.

450
00:21:48,683 --> 00:21:50,530
One is slow,
and the other is incredibly fast.

451
00:21:51,810 --> 00:21:53,303
(Ji Hwan rings the bell.)

452
00:21:53,950 --> 00:21:55,469
Why are you both so good at this?

453
00:21:55,617 --> 00:21:57,664
I sacrificed my ears for this.

454
00:21:58,503 --> 00:22:00,073
Your ears are your secret weapon?

455
00:22:00,616 --> 00:22:02,175
So this is disaster relief money?

456
00:22:02,823 --> 00:22:04,877
(His joke is right up her alley.)

457
00:22:05,612 --> 00:22:06,613
I like that.

458
00:22:07,677 --> 00:22:10,851
Ji Hwan has a really funny sense of humor.

459
00:22:11,218 --> 00:22:12,920
I like people who think intuitively...

460
00:22:13,343 --> 00:22:17,424
and come up with quirky, unexpected ideas.

461
00:22:17,691 --> 00:22:22,195
I saw that side of him
while we were playing Halli Galli.

462
00:22:22,395 --> 00:22:24,731
I think we have a similar sense of humor.

463
00:22:25,505 --> 00:22:26,967
I'm going to take a break now.

464
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,169
Would you like a second round
of disaster relief money?

465
00:22:29,405 --> 00:22:30,737
I'll sit this round out.

466
00:22:30,852 --> 00:22:32,039
My ears hurt too much.

467
00:22:32,312 --> 00:22:34,745
(The women's room on the third floor)

468
00:22:36,466 --> 00:22:38,712
(Min Seo opens the door
to the men's room across the hall.)

469
00:22:39,299 --> 00:22:40,946
(Dong Su happens to be inside.)

470
00:22:41,059 --> 00:22:42,819
(The siblings reunite.)

471
00:22:43,639 --> 00:22:45,719
- Has everyone gone downstairs?
- They're all downstairs.

472
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:46,586
Everyone?

473
00:22:46,812 --> 00:22:49,189
- Who do you like?
- Who?

474
00:22:49,632 --> 00:22:50,991
Who am I interested in?

475
00:22:51,127 --> 00:22:52,386
Yes. I have no clue.

476
00:22:52,699 --> 00:22:56,596
We barely had a chance
to figure that out yesterday.

477
00:22:58,053 --> 00:23:00,199
(The older brother is curious
about his sister's feelings.)

478
00:23:00,639 --> 00:23:01,401
Ji Hwan.

479
00:23:03,113 --> 00:23:04,972
Who did you think it was? Jin Sung?

480
00:23:05,013 --> 00:23:06,573
- In Joong.
- In Joong?

481
00:23:07,537 --> 00:23:10,110
(Her brother's guesses are way off.)

482
00:23:10,390 --> 00:23:12,157
In Joong? You thought I liked In Joong?

483
00:23:12,197 --> 00:23:13,613
You thought he had
that Gang Dong Won vibe?

484
00:23:13,804 --> 00:23:15,983
No, that's just my wishful thinking.

485
00:23:16,510 --> 00:23:18,802
(Who would he like Min Seo
to end up with?)

486
00:23:19,195 --> 00:23:20,087
In Joong.

487
00:23:20,787 --> 00:23:22,255
He's got this confident, easygoing charm.

488
00:23:22,295 --> 00:23:23,290
He's tall.

489
00:23:23,557 --> 00:23:24,491
And he has a solid build.

490
00:23:24,758 --> 00:23:26,008
He's not shy either.

491
00:23:26,259 --> 00:23:28,326
I think it'd be fun to have him
as my brother-in-law.

492
00:23:28,962 --> 00:23:33,333
But you can tell In Joong is going
straight for Ye In.

493
00:23:33,853 --> 00:23:36,226
(In Joong is busy pursuing Ye In
through Halli Galli.)

494
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:38,171
You seem like you'd be good at studying.

495
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:39,306
Studying?

496
00:23:40,707 --> 00:23:43,910
I'm actually pretty quick
at spotting things,

497
00:23:44,211 --> 00:23:45,925
so I'm usually fast at card games.

498
00:23:45,926 --> 00:23:46,947
I don't know about that!

499
00:23:47,853 --> 00:23:50,384
But In Joong was incredibly good
at Halli Galli.

500
00:23:50,605 --> 00:23:53,186
He seems really good
at reading situations.

501
00:23:53,453 --> 00:23:57,224
That means he notices things
other people miss and has a good memory.

502
00:23:57,365 --> 00:24:00,527
So I thought he seemed really smart,

503
00:24:00,583 --> 00:24:01,728
and I liked that.

504
00:24:01,776 --> 00:24:03,196
Does a game normally last this long?

505
00:24:03,563 --> 00:24:06,166
I've never played one this long either.

506
00:24:06,850 --> 00:24:09,536
But I thought your first choice was Ye In.

507
00:24:09,730 --> 00:24:11,972
- Isn't she your type physically?
- No.

508
00:24:12,194 --> 00:24:12,773
Really?

509
00:24:12,774 --> 00:24:14,534
(The siblings keep guessing wrong.)

510
00:24:16,468 --> 00:24:17,878
I like girls with softer,
rounder features.

511
00:24:18,041 --> 00:24:19,246
But I mean...

512
00:24:19,341 --> 00:24:22,416
She kind of looks like her, doesn't she?

513
00:24:23,305 --> 00:24:25,819
Come on, Ye In has
a pretty different vibe from my ex.

514
00:24:27,087 --> 00:24:28,055
Very different.

515
00:24:28,725 --> 00:24:30,765
Then is Yu Ra your first choice?

516
00:24:30,767 --> 00:24:31,458
Of course.

517
00:24:31,459 --> 00:24:32,819
- Oh, seriously?
- Yes.

518
00:24:32,851 --> 00:24:33,560
Bullshit!

519
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:36,891
(They burst out laughing.)

520
00:24:37,178 --> 00:24:38,098
A real sibling interaction!

521
00:24:38,100 --> 00:24:38,999
That's more like it!

522
00:24:39,045 --> 00:24:40,267
Definitely!

523
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:41,968
- Oh, seriously?
- Yes.

524
00:24:42,087 --> 00:24:42,869
Bullshit!

525
00:24:44,194 --> 00:24:45,038
Really?

526
00:24:45,039 --> 00:24:46,298
(His ideal type comes
as a surprise to her.)

527
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:50,499
But Jwa Hyeon has
a really nice personality.

528
00:24:50,500 --> 00:24:52,679
- She really does.
- She seemed lovely.

529
00:24:53,159 --> 00:24:55,115
Doesn't Jwa Hyeon like In Joong?

530
00:24:56,860 --> 00:24:59,019
- Isn't In Joong her choice?
- Oh, is that so?

531
00:24:59,126 --> 00:25:01,126
Did you get a card yesterday?

532
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,756
Did Yu Ra give you one?

533
00:25:02,826 --> 00:25:03,690
No.

534
00:25:03,746 --> 00:25:05,859
Who did you get one from?
You didn't get one from anyone?

535
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:08,528
- Then who did Yu Ra give hers to?
- Ji Hwan.

536
00:25:08,651 --> 00:25:09,496
Really?

537
00:25:11,764 --> 00:25:12,966
Who did you give yours to?

538
00:25:13,984 --> 00:25:15,402
Ji Hwan.

539
00:25:16,278 --> 00:25:18,271
- What about Ye In?
- She gave hers to In Joong.

540
00:25:18,578 --> 00:25:20,707
Then Jin Sung and I got zero votes.

541
00:25:21,241 --> 00:25:22,109
Really?

542
00:25:22,909 --> 00:25:27,414
That's why I got that call
from the Love Hideout yesterday.

543
00:25:28,448 --> 00:25:29,683
I had no idea what I was supposed to do.

544
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:32,486
But I think that's probably it.

545
00:25:32,513 --> 00:25:34,886
She's already got something going
with Ji Hwan, right?

546
00:25:34,888 --> 00:25:37,224
But she has the date ticket.

547
00:25:37,407 --> 00:25:38,191
I see.

548
00:25:38,320 --> 00:25:42,095
And apparently,
after I saw her choose Ji Hwan,

549
00:25:42,431 --> 00:25:44,664
she could tell I was a little upset.

550
00:25:45,298 --> 00:25:46,233
Something like that?

551
00:25:48,378 --> 00:25:49,436
I don't know.

552
00:25:51,938 --> 00:25:53,707
- Oh, it's over!
- Finally!

553
00:25:54,478 --> 00:25:55,575
Is everyone asleep?

554
00:25:56,209 --> 00:25:58,411
I think so.

555
00:25:59,145 --> 00:26:00,313
So are you set on pursuing
just one person?

556
00:26:01,081 --> 00:26:01,815
Me?

557
00:26:02,872 --> 00:26:04,965
So you're not going to eat?

558
00:26:05,662 --> 00:26:06,965
(Acting mode on)

559
00:26:07,125 --> 00:26:08,155
I don't eat lunch.

560
00:26:08,299 --> 00:26:09,789
Oh, really? Not even some snacks?

561
00:26:10,390 --> 00:26:12,624
- Shouldn't you change?
- Yes, I should.

562
00:26:12,626 --> 00:26:14,330
(She makes a natural exit.)

563
00:26:16,963 --> 00:26:18,963
Oh! Everyone's coming upstairs!

564
00:26:22,590 --> 00:26:23,801
That was no joke.

565
00:26:24,603 --> 00:26:26,309
- She's good.
- That was fast!

566
00:26:26,330 --> 00:26:27,440
I know!

567
00:26:28,463 --> 00:26:32,196
(A letter arrives.)

568
00:26:36,729 --> 00:26:37,717
Did something come?

569
00:26:43,857 --> 00:26:44,791
Gosh!

570
00:26:44,977 --> 00:26:45,692
What is it?

571
00:26:47,657 --> 00:26:49,095
I think there's something else in here.

572
00:26:52,024 --> 00:26:54,271
(An envelope containing mysterious cards)

573
00:26:54,601 --> 00:26:57,588
"Your first date will be
an activity date..."

574
00:26:57,590 --> 00:26:59,206
"where you can enjoy summer in Jeju."

575
00:26:59,806 --> 00:27:03,109
"Inside, you'll find two envelopes
containing activity cards."

576
00:27:03,343 --> 00:27:06,046
"Women, please gather on the first floor,
and men, on the second floor."

577
00:27:06,279 --> 00:27:10,050
"Open your activity card envelopes
and choose the date you'd like to go on."

578
00:27:10,350 --> 00:27:12,719
"Keep your choices secret
until departure."

579
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:20,126
Unlike the first day, we weren't choosing
based on first impressions,

580
00:27:20,493 --> 00:27:23,163
so I felt even more nervous.

581
00:27:23,256 --> 00:27:25,030
I was really excited.

582
00:27:25,031 --> 00:27:27,031
Because you have absolutely no idea
what's going to happen.

583
00:27:27,141 --> 00:27:28,635
There's excitement in that uncertainty.

584
00:27:28,814 --> 00:27:31,538
And I thought, "Now I finally get
to know someone 1-on-1."

585
00:27:32,439 --> 00:27:34,554
- Shall we head upstairs, guys?
- Let's go.

586
00:27:34,948 --> 00:27:37,210
Even if you don't end up
with the person you want,

587
00:27:37,221 --> 00:27:39,607
being paired
with someone else gives you...

588
00:27:39,608 --> 00:27:41,068
- a chance to discover their charms.
- Right.

589
00:27:41,088 --> 00:27:42,916
You get to see sides of them
you didn't know about.

590
00:27:43,663 --> 00:27:44,584
I wonder what the activities are.

591
00:27:45,708 --> 00:27:48,154
Let's open it up.

592
00:27:48,301 --> 00:27:50,359
(The activity cards are revealed.)

593
00:27:50,361 --> 00:27:52,459
First, surfing.

594
00:27:54,421 --> 00:27:57,135
Second, couples yoga.

595
00:27:57,397 --> 00:27:58,331
Yoga?

596
00:27:58,768 --> 00:28:01,375
Third, ATV riding.

597
00:28:04,001 --> 00:28:06,187
Fourth, rock climbing.

598
00:28:06,188 --> 00:28:07,374
Oh, rock climbing!

599
00:28:07,775 --> 00:28:10,243
- That's your hobby, right?
- I love rock climbing.

600
00:28:11,819 --> 00:28:15,699
(The men start choosing their activities.)

601
00:28:16,633 --> 00:28:18,918
- I'm definitely picking this one.
- Surfing?

602
00:28:19,566 --> 00:28:20,987
I'll take rock climbing.

603
00:28:21,057 --> 00:28:21,921
I'll take this.

604
00:28:22,656 --> 00:28:23,690
Couples yoga?

605
00:28:23,924 --> 00:28:25,358
Couples yoga is...

606
00:28:25,844 --> 00:28:26,660
Gosh...

607
00:28:26,661 --> 00:28:28,290
Ji Hwan, choose whichever one you want.

608
00:28:28,291 --> 00:28:29,329
I'm not too keen on yoga either.

609
00:28:30,964 --> 00:28:31,998
I'd prefer...

610
00:28:33,466 --> 00:28:35,201
surfing or rock climbing.

611
00:28:36,915 --> 00:28:38,972
Everyone's avoiding it.

612
00:28:39,191 --> 00:28:42,008
(No one wants to pick couples yoga.)

613
00:28:42,096 --> 00:28:45,026
I can see why guys might be
reluctant to do yoga.

614
00:28:45,040 --> 00:28:46,526
It's pretty slow-paced.

615
00:28:46,780 --> 00:28:48,781
And you might end up showing
some unflattering sides of yourself.

616
00:28:48,782 --> 00:28:50,400
Exactly. Your muscles start shaking
in weird ways.

617
00:28:50,433 --> 00:28:52,433
When you hold those poses,
your whole body starts trembling.

618
00:28:53,353 --> 00:28:55,621
Someone recommended Pilates to me once,

619
00:28:55,622 --> 00:28:56,831
- and I ended up looking ridiculous.
- Right.

620
00:28:56,864 --> 00:28:58,091
- I was shaking like this!
- Exactly!

621
00:28:58,291 --> 00:28:59,626
- I'd rather lift weights.
- The gym is better.

622
00:28:59,744 --> 00:29:02,811
Should we just draw lots to see
who does yoga?

623
00:29:02,984 --> 00:29:04,097
Rock, paper, scissors!

624
00:29:05,578 --> 00:29:07,365
(In Joong and Dong Su lose.)

625
00:29:07,458 --> 00:29:08,335
Rock, paper, scissors!

626
00:29:10,558 --> 00:29:13,091
(Dong Su gets stuck with couples yoga.)

627
00:29:13,092 --> 00:29:13,940
Yoga?

628
00:29:15,238 --> 00:29:17,938
I really wanted to avoid couples yoga.

629
00:29:18,032 --> 00:29:21,898
But everyone else was avoiding it too.

630
00:29:22,072 --> 00:29:23,216
And somehow, I ended up with it.

631
00:29:24,032 --> 00:29:26,052
(Dong Su is caught off guard.)

632
00:29:26,658 --> 00:29:28,897
Then what would you like to do, Ji Hwan?

633
00:29:28,898 --> 00:29:29,889
Well...

634
00:29:29,945 --> 00:29:32,422
Rock climbing is my first choice.

635
00:29:32,462 --> 00:29:34,127
Mine too.

636
00:29:34,602 --> 00:29:36,695
Then In Joong can take ATV riding.

637
00:29:36,855 --> 00:29:38,131
I'll take this one, then.

638
00:29:39,015 --> 00:29:40,595
- Rock, paper, scissors!
- Rock, paper, scissors!

639
00:29:41,135 --> 00:29:43,906
(Ji Hwan ends up getting rock climbing.)

640
00:29:44,413 --> 00:29:46,366
I haven't done it much, so I thought
this would be a good opportunity.

641
00:29:46,886 --> 00:29:49,300
Then I'll take surfing.

642
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:53,393
I'm suddenly feeling a lot better!

643
00:29:54,773 --> 00:29:55,849
Couples yoga?

644
00:29:56,073 --> 00:29:57,246
Oh, I'd like to try yoga.

645
00:29:57,248 --> 00:29:58,852
I've found something I want to do too.

646
00:29:59,368 --> 00:30:00,320
Yoga!

647
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:02,770
Goodness!

648
00:30:02,859 --> 00:30:06,008
I want to do yoga too.

649
00:30:06,009 --> 00:30:06,852
What should we do?

650
00:30:06,853 --> 00:30:08,775
Ye In, what do you want to do?

651
00:30:10,938 --> 00:30:12,346
I want to do this.

652
00:30:13,378 --> 00:30:15,155
Shall we play rock-paper-scissors?

653
00:30:15,156 --> 00:30:16,240
- Okay.
- Sounds good.

654
00:30:16,241 --> 00:30:17,251
Rock, paper, scissors.

655
00:30:18,852 --> 00:30:24,224
(The women also chose
by playing rock-paper-scissors.)

656
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:28,562
Starting off Day Two...

657
00:30:29,222 --> 00:30:31,832
with such an intense activity.

658
00:30:32,817 --> 00:30:35,235
I was hoping...

659
00:30:35,236 --> 00:30:37,715
either In Joong
or Ji Hwan would show up...

660
00:30:37,716 --> 00:30:40,541
because they were the ones I liked
based on first impressions.

661
00:30:41,003 --> 00:30:43,442
Ji Hwan or Jin Sung.

662
00:30:43,443 --> 00:30:45,759
I'm just curious about Ji Hwan.

663
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:48,781
I want to talk to him.

664
00:30:48,782 --> 00:30:50,582
As for Jin Sung,

665
00:30:50,583 --> 00:30:53,966
he showed interest in me yesterday,

666
00:30:53,967 --> 00:30:56,556
so I wanted to have
a conversation with him.

667
00:30:57,224 --> 00:31:01,595
(The women also chose their dates.)

668
00:31:02,711 --> 00:31:05,633
Jwa Hyeon, did you get what you liked?

669
00:31:06,069 --> 00:31:08,535
It worked out in the end.

670
00:31:09,199 --> 00:31:11,100
We played rock-paper-scissors.

671
00:31:11,101 --> 00:31:13,173
I chose first.

672
00:31:14,085 --> 00:31:15,609
I got the worst one.

673
00:31:16,120 --> 00:31:17,344
Really?

674
00:31:18,338 --> 00:31:19,513
Is that so?

675
00:31:21,448 --> 00:31:23,216
(Sneezing)

676
00:31:23,694 --> 00:31:25,586
Your sneeze is cute.

677
00:31:29,323 --> 00:31:31,592
(Embarrassed)

678
00:31:31,744 --> 00:31:33,194
That was a cute sneeze.

679
00:31:33,966 --> 00:31:36,830
Okay. That's how you sound cute
when you sneeze.

680
00:31:37,702 --> 00:31:38,754
I got it.

681
00:31:38,755 --> 00:31:39,833
Are you going to copy that?

682
00:31:41,138 --> 00:31:43,683
Can I be cute but also loud?

683
00:31:46,206 --> 00:31:47,239
(Heading out not knowing their dates)

684
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:48,493
See you later.

685
00:31:48,494 --> 00:31:50,811
- See you.
- See you later.

686
00:31:53,080 --> 00:31:56,116
(The women get in the cars first.)

687
00:31:57,117 --> 00:31:58,319
The parking lot?

688
00:31:59,568 --> 00:32:02,823
(Four cars are parked behind the house.)

689
00:32:12,799 --> 00:32:14,234
(Ye In gets in a car.)

690
00:32:14,902 --> 00:32:16,003
Amazing.

691
00:32:23,243 --> 00:32:25,078
(Min Seo gets in a car.)

692
00:32:28,215 --> 00:32:30,084
(Jwa Hyeon gets in a car.)

693
00:32:34,555 --> 00:32:36,724
(Yu Ra gets in a car.)

694
00:32:39,459 --> 00:32:45,365
(All the women got in their cars.)

695
00:32:49,169 --> 00:32:52,172
(Ji Hwan is the first man
to leave the house.)

696
00:33:03,650 --> 00:33:11,291
(Who is Ji Hwan's date?)

697
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:13,560
Yes.

698
00:33:14,294 --> 00:33:20,567
(Yu Ra and Min Seo gave Ji Hwan
their first-impression cards.)

699
00:33:23,537 --> 00:33:29,109
(Ye In was torn
between In Joong and Ji Hwan.)

700
00:33:29,910 --> 00:33:33,480
(Who will Ji Hwan be sitting next to?)

701
00:33:38,952 --> 00:33:40,718
(Who were you hoping for in the car?)

702
00:33:40,719 --> 00:33:44,291
Min Seo or Ye In.

703
00:33:54,242 --> 00:33:55,535
- Hello.
- Hi.

704
00:33:58,098 --> 00:33:59,673
- Hello.
- Hello.

705
00:33:59,675 --> 00:34:01,875
(Min Seo and Ji Hwan are matched.)

706
00:34:03,554 --> 00:34:05,946
- Yes! Min Seo and Ji Hwan.
- Min Seo and Ji Hwan.

707
00:34:06,168 --> 00:34:07,388
That's good.

708
00:34:07,389 --> 00:34:08,557
They look good together.

709
00:34:08,558 --> 00:34:10,717
I think so. They look cute.

710
00:34:10,917 --> 00:34:12,067
They seem like a good match
personality-wise.

711
00:34:12,068 --> 00:34:15,974
- They're both athletic too.
- They are.

712
00:34:16,170 --> 00:34:17,124
Oh, my.

713
00:34:19,010 --> 00:34:20,761
I chose climbing...

714
00:34:22,395 --> 00:34:24,031
because I thought Min Seo would too.

715
00:34:25,845 --> 00:34:28,135
When I actually saw her in the car,

716
00:34:28,765 --> 00:34:32,172
I couldn't really show how happy I was,

717
00:34:32,893 --> 00:34:35,141
but I was over the moon.

718
00:34:37,310 --> 00:34:39,213
- Hello.
- Hello.

719
00:34:39,812 --> 00:34:41,448
Did you choose climbing?

720
00:34:41,450 --> 00:34:42,816
Yes, I did.

721
00:34:43,116 --> 00:34:47,620
(A climbing date: Min Seo and Ji Hwan)

722
00:34:48,827 --> 00:34:51,458
I kind of expected it.

723
00:34:51,460 --> 00:34:53,060
- You did?
- Yes.

724
00:34:54,686 --> 00:34:56,787
I had a feeling you would like climbing.

725
00:34:56,788 --> 00:34:58,665
Me? I've never done it before.

726
00:34:59,917 --> 00:35:01,617
I was happy...

727
00:35:01,618 --> 00:35:04,438
but also worried at the same time.

728
00:35:04,729 --> 00:35:08,277
I was into him,

729
00:35:08,278 --> 00:35:10,686
and when I'm into someone,

730
00:35:10,687 --> 00:35:12,198
I tend to fumble a lot.

731
00:35:12,199 --> 00:35:14,389
I thought I'd be awkward...

732
00:35:14,390 --> 00:35:15,953
and too nervous to talk to him.

733
00:35:15,955 --> 00:35:17,492
I started getting a bit worried...

734
00:35:17,493 --> 00:35:19,953
thinking about that.

735
00:35:20,655 --> 00:35:22,890
- Let's get going.
- Okay.

736
00:35:23,223 --> 00:35:27,594
(Min Seo and Ji Hwan set off.)

737
00:35:29,196 --> 00:35:32,466
(Meanwhile, Yu Ra's date)

738
00:35:33,967 --> 00:35:35,535
- Hello.
- Hello.

739
00:35:35,727 --> 00:35:37,433
- My things are here.
- Let me put my things here.

740
00:35:37,434 --> 00:35:39,106
Did you expect me?

741
00:35:39,299 --> 00:35:41,408
- No, not at all.
- I didn't expect it at all.

742
00:35:43,477 --> 00:35:45,010
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

743
00:35:45,011 --> 00:35:46,412
(Yu Ra and Jin Sung head off.)

744
00:35:47,080 --> 00:35:50,383
(The third man, In Joong)

745
00:36:00,660 --> 00:36:04,861
(Who is In Joong's date?)

746
00:36:04,862 --> 00:36:06,432
Really?

747
00:36:10,370 --> 00:36:16,076
(Ye In and Jwa Hyeon showed interest
with their first-impression cards.)

748
00:36:18,278 --> 00:36:22,249
(Who will In Joong be sitting next to?)

749
00:36:29,161 --> 00:36:32,358
I was hoping I'd get Ye In.

750
00:36:39,145 --> 00:36:41,501
- Hello.
- What?

751
00:36:41,679 --> 00:36:43,501
- You were here?
- Yes.

752
00:36:43,502 --> 00:36:45,030
Did you think it was empty?

753
00:36:45,031 --> 00:36:46,545
- Yes.
- Really?

754
00:36:46,546 --> 00:36:48,241
The women were waiting
in the car, I guess.

755
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:51,144
- I guess we're going together.
- I like that.

756
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:58,152
- These two are meant to be.
- It seems like it.

757
00:36:59,599 --> 00:37:02,589
I opened the door and saw Ye In in there.

758
00:37:03,057 --> 00:37:04,148
I was so glad.

759
00:37:04,149 --> 00:37:06,726
We talked a lot the day before,

760
00:37:06,727 --> 00:37:08,895
so I was so happy to see her.

761
00:37:09,623 --> 00:37:10,730
I just loved it.

762
00:37:13,183 --> 00:37:16,536
I could see his silhouette
from a distance.

763
00:37:17,400 --> 00:37:20,207
A tall person was walking towards me,

764
00:37:20,458 --> 00:37:23,810
so I figured it had to be one of the two.

765
00:37:25,844 --> 00:37:27,683
As he got closer,

766
00:37:27,684 --> 00:37:29,475
I started noticing the checkered pattern,

767
00:37:30,156 --> 00:37:32,968
so I realized it was In Joong.

768
00:37:32,969 --> 00:37:34,254
I was really happy.

769
00:37:35,646 --> 00:37:38,095
- Was it fun?
- It was so much fun.

770
00:37:39,943 --> 00:37:43,697
Who is the last guy? I have no idea.

771
00:37:45,717 --> 00:37:49,839
Who could it be?

772
00:37:57,104 --> 00:37:58,578
Hello.

773
00:37:58,789 --> 00:38:01,115
Hello. I didn't expect you at all.

774
00:38:01,117 --> 00:38:02,947
- Really?
- Because...

775
00:38:02,948 --> 00:38:04,518
They'll do couples yoga.

776
00:38:05,189 --> 00:38:06,486
Actually...

777
00:38:06,487 --> 00:38:08,088
That's not a bad pair.

778
00:38:08,522 --> 00:38:10,902
You said you chose the worst one.

779
00:38:10,903 --> 00:38:13,126
I didn't think it was the worst.

780
00:38:13,361 --> 00:38:15,729
- What did everyone want?
- Yoga was the most popular one.

781
00:38:15,987 --> 00:38:16,960
- Really?
- Yes.

782
00:38:17,239 --> 00:38:18,749
Have you tried climbing before?

783
00:38:18,750 --> 00:38:20,133
No, not even once.

784
00:38:20,781 --> 00:38:23,069
It's your first time climbing.

785
00:38:23,346 --> 00:38:25,772
I'm worried I won't look very graceful.

786
00:38:26,274 --> 00:38:27,941
I'll be hanging like this.

787
00:38:28,919 --> 00:38:30,377
There's no such thing as looking bad...

788
00:38:31,168 --> 00:38:32,345
when you're exercising.

789
00:38:32,835 --> 00:38:35,448
I feel like you've never raised your voice
in your life.

790
00:38:36,071 --> 00:38:37,316
Raising my voice?

791
00:38:38,191 --> 00:38:39,852
I don't really remember.

792
00:38:40,995 --> 00:38:42,995
- Can someone be like that?
- How is that possible?

793
00:38:42,997 --> 00:38:44,164
I get mad all the time.

794
00:38:44,165 --> 00:38:45,925
He seems like the calm type.

795
00:38:46,508 --> 00:38:47,461
Why?

796
00:38:47,786 --> 00:38:50,363
Judging by your tone...

797
00:38:50,364 --> 00:38:51,732
and the way you speak.

798
00:38:54,487 --> 00:38:56,303
I'll try talking...

799
00:38:56,700 --> 00:38:58,471
in a higher tone.

800
00:38:59,770 --> 00:39:01,907
I like that. Keep talking like that.

801
00:39:01,908 --> 00:39:03,176
(Clearing his throat)

802
00:39:03,691 --> 00:39:05,879
What should we talk about?

803
00:39:08,723 --> 00:39:09,983
The weather is so nice.

804
00:39:15,922 --> 00:39:18,458
(Bouldering: Min Seo and Ji Hwan)

805
00:39:18,460 --> 00:39:22,028
I'm curious to see how you climb.

806
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:24,097
I feel like I'll be good at it.

807
00:39:25,922 --> 00:39:28,435
Let's stretch before we start.

808
00:39:35,208 --> 00:39:36,509
(Grunting)

809
00:39:36,910 --> 00:39:37,677
(Glancing)

810
00:39:39,245 --> 00:39:41,080
(Struggling)

811
00:39:43,009 --> 00:39:45,252
You'll hold hands and pull each other in.

812
00:39:46,414 --> 00:39:49,807
Please face each other. Sir, you as well.

813
00:39:50,704 --> 00:39:52,104
Face each other.

814
00:39:56,036 --> 00:39:57,330
Wait.

815
00:40:00,696 --> 00:40:02,609
Pull each other back and forth.

816
00:40:02,676 --> 00:40:05,343
Stretch your arms out.

817
00:40:11,849 --> 00:40:13,256
Now to the opposite side.

818
00:40:13,445 --> 00:40:14,271
Good.

819
00:40:19,343 --> 00:40:20,909
Don't loosen your grip.

820
00:40:24,745 --> 00:40:26,584
- Shall we get started?
- Sounds good.

821
00:40:28,205 --> 00:40:29,631
Lower your upper body.

822
00:40:29,751 --> 00:40:31,144
Ready, go!

823
00:40:36,722 --> 00:40:37,575
(Amazed)

824
00:40:42,929 --> 00:40:45,502
One, two, three. You've reached the top!

825
00:40:45,575 --> 00:40:46,995
You're great.

826
00:40:47,029 --> 00:40:49,089
I'm exhausted now that I'm done.

827
00:40:49,695 --> 00:40:51,082
I can do it too, right?

828
00:40:51,808 --> 00:40:53,295
(Min Seo takes her turn.)

829
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:54,387
(Heave-ho!)

830
00:40:55,300 --> 00:40:56,169
Good!

831
00:40:57,152 --> 00:40:58,332
You're almost there!

832
00:40:59,572 --> 00:41:00,599
(Holding tight)

833
00:41:01,079 --> 00:41:02,658
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

834
00:41:02,752 --> 00:41:04,579
(Min Seo reaches the top
on her first try.)

835
00:41:05,029 --> 00:41:06,023
I'll step here...

836
00:41:06,048 --> 00:41:08,032
Be careful.

837
00:41:11,598 --> 00:41:12,751
It was perfect.

838
00:41:13,684 --> 00:41:15,390
This is a great workout.

839
00:41:16,558 --> 00:41:18,824
She climbed up so effortlessly.

840
00:41:19,110 --> 00:41:24,271
She was so good that I could tell
she was really athletic.

841
00:41:24,323 --> 00:41:26,130
Ji Hwan was good.

842
00:41:26,804 --> 00:41:28,019
You're almost there.

843
00:41:30,165 --> 00:41:31,265
It's perfect.

844
00:41:31,931 --> 00:41:35,393
But I did just as well.

845
00:41:36,845 --> 00:41:38,775
(First climb: success)

846
00:41:39,142 --> 00:41:41,202
(Second climb: success)

847
00:41:43,109 --> 00:41:45,362
(She's breezing through it.)

848
00:41:45,808 --> 00:41:47,495
You're amazing.

849
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:49,040
You're making it look so easy.

850
00:41:49,402 --> 00:41:50,584
(Hup!)

851
00:41:52,015 --> 00:41:53,708
- Three, two, one.
- Three, two, one.

852
00:41:54,612 --> 00:41:55,967
Come down carefully.

853
00:41:57,747 --> 00:41:58,807
You're really good.

854
00:41:58,893 --> 00:42:00,227
How are you so good?

855
00:42:04,326 --> 00:42:05,323
You're so good.

856
00:42:06,071 --> 00:42:07,677
I need to lie down for a bit.

857
00:42:07,751 --> 00:42:09,264
Let's lie down for a minute.

858
00:42:12,999 --> 00:42:14,638
My muscles are going to be
so sore tomorrow.

859
00:42:15,613 --> 00:42:16,780
You're sweating so much.

860
00:42:17,500 --> 00:42:18,933
(Sweating buckets)

861
00:42:20,794 --> 00:42:24,967
It's not easy to let someone see you
looking so worn out like that.

862
00:42:25,228 --> 00:42:27,374
Seeing her that way made me feel like...

863
00:42:27,896 --> 00:42:29,656
we'd gotten much closer.

864
00:42:30,948 --> 00:42:32,917
(Forearm emergency stretch)

865
00:42:33,602 --> 00:42:35,062
Try this.

866
00:42:36,122 --> 00:42:37,715
(Stretching their forearms)

867
00:42:45,367 --> 00:42:46,267
(Poking)

868
00:42:48,917 --> 00:42:50,650
Why did he suddenly poke her arm?

869
00:42:50,684 --> 00:42:51,904
He just did it out of nowhere.

870
00:42:52,044 --> 00:42:53,910
Isn't that a sign he's interested?

871
00:42:53,951 --> 00:42:55,671
That's a pretty unusual way to flirt.

872
00:42:55,696 --> 00:42:58,917
Given Ji Hwan's personality,
that could mean a lot.

873
00:42:58,983 --> 00:43:00,770
- It could be a huge sign.
- Exactly.

874
00:43:01,037 --> 00:43:02,996
Did Min Seo notice too?

875
00:43:03,803 --> 00:43:05,009
(Poking)

876
00:43:10,274 --> 00:43:11,994
This is such a good workout, isn't it?

877
00:43:12,048 --> 00:43:14,776
Exactly. Dinner will taste
amazing tonight.

878
00:43:14,801 --> 00:43:16,428
Right? I can't even imagine.

879
00:43:16,453 --> 00:43:18,678
(Heading out for dinner)

880
00:43:21,075 --> 00:43:22,528
(Yawning)

881
00:43:23,008 --> 00:43:23,955
(Laughing)

882
00:43:24,321 --> 00:43:25,414
You're tired, aren't you?

883
00:43:25,608 --> 00:43:26,168
Sorry?

884
00:43:26,254 --> 00:43:27,627
- You're tired.
- No.

885
00:43:27,808 --> 00:43:29,328
I'm totally fine.

886
00:43:29,681 --> 00:43:34,727
But you said when we left
that if I got sleepy,

887
00:43:34,854 --> 00:43:36,610
I should tell you, and you'd sing to me.

888
00:43:36,635 --> 00:43:37,568
Did I?

889
00:43:37,862 --> 00:43:38,522
Yes.

890
00:43:38,547 --> 00:43:40,081
Sing me a song to cheer me on.

891
00:43:41,007 --> 00:43:45,361
If you get sleepy, let me know.

892
00:43:45,835 --> 00:43:47,892
I'll sing you a song to cheer you on.

893
00:43:49,387 --> 00:43:50,924
I don't remember saying that.

894
00:43:51,610 --> 00:43:54,598
I bet hearing you sing
would make all my fatigue disappear.

895
00:43:55,040 --> 00:43:57,343
I have vocal nodules, so I can't sing.

896
00:43:58,387 --> 00:44:00,187
Oh, vocal nodules... I see.

897
00:44:01,100 --> 00:44:03,274
But how did you get vocal nodules?

898
00:44:03,580 --> 00:44:04,920
I was kidding.

899
00:44:06,394 --> 00:44:08,733
- You were kidding?
- I was.

900
00:44:10,007 --> 00:44:17,191
I was genuinely worried you were sick,
so I asked you very carefully.

901
00:44:17,364 --> 00:44:20,318
I thought you were still recovering
from vocal nodules.

902
00:44:20,785 --> 00:44:22,925
I feel so embarrassed.

903
00:44:24,023 --> 00:44:26,924
(They arrive at a beach,
feeling embarrassed.)

904
00:44:28,123 --> 00:44:29,583
The ocean is so nice.

905
00:44:30,670 --> 00:44:31,637
It really is.

906
00:44:31,686 --> 00:44:33,913
(Taking in the view)

907
00:44:34,290 --> 00:44:36,209
Would you like me
to take your picture here?

908
00:44:36,629 --> 00:44:37,862
Should we take a picture?

909
00:44:38,544 --> 00:44:39,324
You mean together?

910
00:44:39,349 --> 00:44:40,878
Of course we should take it together.

911
00:44:42,149 --> 00:44:45,989
I'd look like some old guy
taking a selfie by myself.

912
00:44:46,576 --> 00:44:48,556
- Shall we take it now?
- Are you good at taking pictures?

913
00:44:49,529 --> 00:44:51,455
My face doesn't look great right now.

914
00:44:52,618 --> 00:44:54,776
We were going to take a picture together,

915
00:44:54,801 --> 00:44:56,988
but I looked like a mess.

916
00:44:57,827 --> 00:44:59,695
My face is...

917
00:44:59,719 --> 00:45:01,532
Please don't look at me for a second.

918
00:45:01,714 --> 00:45:02,400
(Turning away)

919
00:45:02,425 --> 00:45:03,240
Sure.

920
00:45:06,455 --> 00:45:07,248
(Snap!)

921
00:45:07,273 --> 00:45:08,420
I'm not ready yet!

922
00:45:08,445 --> 00:45:09,736
(Phone confiscated)

923
00:45:10,298 --> 00:45:11,745
You can't just do that!

924
00:45:12,188 --> 00:45:12,981
What?

925
00:45:13,006 --> 00:45:14,219
Let's look at it together.

926
00:45:17,199 --> 00:45:19,284
By then, my phone was already
out of my hands.

927
00:45:19,639 --> 00:45:22,186
I couldn't take any pictures,
so I just took it all in.

928
00:45:22,705 --> 00:45:23,988
I wish I could've taken one.

929
00:45:25,326 --> 00:45:28,426
(Taking in the view with their own eyes)

930
00:45:30,828 --> 00:45:33,436
The camera can't capture it
the way we see it, can it?

931
00:45:33,497 --> 00:45:34,699
Exactly.

932
00:45:37,424 --> 00:45:38,444
(Scaring him)

933
00:45:40,605 --> 00:45:42,778
I felt butterflies in that moment,

934
00:45:42,872 --> 00:45:46,891
watching the sunset and playing around
without a care in the world.

935
00:45:48,126 --> 00:45:49,713
What's your go-to song?

936
00:45:49,738 --> 00:45:50,852
"In the Rain."

937
00:45:51,163 --> 00:45:52,136
Really?

938
00:45:54,329 --> 00:45:57,069
I like "My Love by My Side."

939
00:45:57,640 --> 00:45:59,127
A Kim Hyun Sik song?

940
00:45:59,928 --> 00:46:01,095
I think we got here.

941
00:46:01,120 --> 00:46:02,414
- Right? Shall we go in?
- Sure.

942
00:46:04,953 --> 00:46:07,186
Isn't this path pretty?

943
00:46:08,256 --> 00:46:09,570
(A little forest surrounded by tall trees)

944
00:46:09,597 --> 00:46:10,777
I love it here.

945
00:46:14,181 --> 00:46:15,894
You really like this kind of vibe,
don't you?

946
00:46:16,021 --> 00:46:17,108
I do. I love romantic things.

947
00:46:18,488 --> 00:46:20,662
We're wearing similar outfits.

948
00:46:20,687 --> 00:46:22,747
We are. We didn't plan it, though.

949
00:46:24,113 --> 00:46:26,067
Please face each other.

950
00:46:26,381 --> 00:46:27,645
Try not to laugh.

951
00:46:28,288 --> 00:46:29,881
Don't laugh at me.

952
00:46:31,259 --> 00:46:33,866
Interlace your fingers
and stretch your arms out in front of you.

953
00:46:34,313 --> 00:46:35,479
Turn your hands inward.

954
00:46:36,013 --> 00:46:37,394
Rotate your hands all the way around,

955
00:46:37,419 --> 00:46:38,829
then place your palms on the floor.

956
00:46:43,021 --> 00:46:45,408
Now look toward your belly button.

957
00:46:46,155 --> 00:46:47,808
Press down with your hands...

958
00:46:47,842 --> 00:46:49,702
and stretch the insides of your wrists.

959
00:46:52,483 --> 00:46:53,638
You're pretty good at this.

960
00:46:53,692 --> 00:46:54,899
I'm good at this.

961
00:46:55,499 --> 00:46:57,031
(Trying a forward bend)

962
00:46:57,284 --> 00:46:58,985
Bend down as far as you can.

963
00:46:59,904 --> 00:47:01,997
- You're really good!
- Give me a little push.

964
00:47:02,732 --> 00:47:03,685
(Groaning)

965
00:47:03,818 --> 00:47:05,158
(Laughing)

966
00:47:08,749 --> 00:47:11,208
I heard he wasn't too keen
on doing yoga at first,

967
00:47:11,475 --> 00:47:14,561
so I was surprised
he did much better than I expected.

968
00:47:14,688 --> 00:47:16,548
Take a deep breath in,

969
00:47:17,809 --> 00:47:18,609
then breathe out.

970
00:47:18,682 --> 00:47:21,238
Push against the floor
and slowly bring your body back up.

971
00:47:22,041 --> 00:47:24,508
There you go. You've mastered yoga!

972
00:47:25,521 --> 00:47:28,388
I could see how much I was struggling,

973
00:47:28,469 --> 00:47:31,202
but she kept encouraging me...

974
00:47:31,521 --> 00:47:33,628
and telling me how well I was doing.

975
00:47:33,869 --> 00:47:35,589
It made me want to try even harder.

976
00:47:36,842 --> 00:47:38,215
I think he's getting smitten.

977
00:47:38,282 --> 00:47:41,195
He seems different with her
than he does with Yu Ra.

978
00:47:42,535 --> 00:47:45,488
- It feels amazing.
- Doesn't it?

979
00:47:49,127 --> 00:47:51,574
The sound of the leaves rustling...

980
00:47:52,379 --> 00:47:54,113
It's so therapeutic.

981
00:47:54,967 --> 00:47:57,054
Have you ever lain down
and looked up at the sky like this?

982
00:47:57,101 --> 00:47:58,274
Never.

983
00:47:59,103 --> 00:48:03,336
I'd always just imagined
lying down like this.

984
00:48:03,361 --> 00:48:06,520
- It's really nice to do it.
- I love this silence too.

985
00:48:07,896 --> 00:48:10,429
We were lying down
and looking up at the sky,

986
00:48:10,463 --> 00:48:13,749
listening to the wind
and the leaves rustling.

987
00:48:14,043 --> 00:48:15,559
I really loved that.

988
00:48:16,116 --> 00:48:19,662
Then Jwa Hyeon said,
"Doesn't it feel great?"

989
00:48:20,662 --> 00:48:24,368
That's when I thought she must enjoy
the same kind of romantic things I do.

990
00:48:25,043 --> 00:48:29,009
I got to fulfill one of my dreams
in Jeju with you.

991
00:48:29,335 --> 00:48:30,242
What was it?

992
00:48:30,718 --> 00:48:31,824
Outdoor yoga.

993
00:48:31,849 --> 00:48:32,922
- Really?
- Yes.

994
00:48:32,947 --> 00:48:36,276
Weren't you a little disappointed
when we picked yoga?

995
00:48:36,864 --> 00:48:37,802
It's just that...

996
00:48:37,888 --> 00:48:39,875
I wanted to look good in front of you...

997
00:48:39,996 --> 00:48:42,509
Look good? This is you looking good!

998
00:48:42,534 --> 00:48:44,442
- Really?
- Of course.

999
00:48:45,651 --> 00:48:48,797
I heard yoga was the last thing
you wanted to do.

1000
00:48:48,822 --> 00:48:50,582
I didn't know it was actually
one of your dreams.

1001
00:48:51,562 --> 00:48:53,631
Maybe it became a dream
because I got to do it with you.

1002
00:48:53,869 --> 00:48:54,999
Is that so?

1003
00:48:55,573 --> 00:48:57,087
Dong Su, come on!

1004
00:48:57,129 --> 00:48:59,629
- Dong Su, what was that line?
- Come on!

1005
00:48:59,662 --> 00:49:00,971
That was pretty bold of him.

1006
00:49:02,010 --> 00:49:03,883
Maybe it became a dream
because I got to do it with you.

1007
00:49:05,853 --> 00:49:09,885
He kept saying how much he loved yoga,

1008
00:49:09,910 --> 00:49:12,923
during the session
and even after it was over.

1009
00:49:13,729 --> 00:49:15,182
I really liked that.

1010
00:49:16,520 --> 00:49:19,774
I'm going to tell everyone
how much I enjoyed it.

1011
00:49:19,799 --> 00:49:21,032
I'm really going to brag...

1012
00:49:21,073 --> 00:49:23,073
about having two yoga instructors.

1013
00:49:24,498 --> 00:49:27,004
- Jeju is so beautiful.
- It really is.

1014
00:49:27,658 --> 00:49:29,578
- I'm really looking forward to today.
- Me too.

1015
00:49:31,459 --> 00:49:33,146
(A light rain begins to fall.)

1016
00:49:34,268 --> 00:49:35,972
Do you think we can ride it
in this weather?

1017
00:49:35,997 --> 00:49:37,039
I don't think we can.

1018
00:49:37,086 --> 00:49:38,906
Yes, it's not good.

1019
00:49:39,952 --> 00:49:42,680
If we ride in this weather,
it'll be like going to a water park.

1020
00:49:44,324 --> 00:49:45,651
I guess this is the place.

1021
00:49:48,470 --> 00:49:49,076
(The mountain biking spot)

1022
00:49:55,948 --> 00:49:58,440
(Ye In and In Joong,
Mountain biking on a volcanic cone)

1023
00:49:58,880 --> 00:50:00,727
This umbrella is a little small, though.

1024
00:50:01,532 --> 00:50:02,499
We should each take one.

1025
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:04,868
- Here, take this.
- Thank you.

1026
00:50:06,437 --> 00:50:09,773
(A rainy bike ride in the wind and rain)

1027
00:50:09,907 --> 00:50:11,975
Can they even ride in this weather?

1028
00:50:11,976 --> 00:50:13,243
Mud is going to fly everywhere.

1029
00:50:13,244 --> 00:50:16,479
Still, it'll be a memory
they'll never forget.

1030
00:50:16,480 --> 00:50:18,715
- That's true.
- This rainy day,

1031
00:50:18,783 --> 00:50:20,150
this activity.

1032
00:50:20,151 --> 00:50:22,252
Personally, I wouldn't ride.

1033
00:50:22,520 --> 00:50:23,420
Yeah.

1034
00:50:23,421 --> 00:50:24,321
Right?

1035
00:50:24,922 --> 00:50:27,624
Mud is going to splash
all over their backs.

1036
00:50:27,625 --> 00:50:28,458
Totally.

1037
00:50:29,860 --> 00:50:30,761
Hello.

1038
00:50:30,762 --> 00:50:31,995
- Hello.
- Hello.

1039
00:50:31,996 --> 00:50:35,164
Just remember three things.
Gas, handlebars, and brakes.

1040
00:50:35,165 --> 00:50:36,632
Those are the only three you'll use.

1041
00:50:36,633 --> 00:50:39,101
Don't touch anything up front.

1042
00:50:39,102 --> 00:50:39,969
- Okay.
- Okay.

1043
00:50:40,504 --> 00:50:41,604
How did you do that?

1044
00:50:41,940 --> 00:50:43,673
- Want me to do yours?
- Thanks.

1045
00:50:44,443 --> 00:50:45,308
All set.

1046
00:50:45,843 --> 00:50:46,943
- Shall we?
- Yeah.

1047
00:50:49,147 --> 00:50:51,147
(In Joong hops on first.)

1048
00:50:52,049 --> 00:50:53,049
Hold the brakes.

1049
00:50:53,050 --> 00:50:54,517
- Oh, wow.
- Step on it.

1050
00:50:59,890 --> 00:51:00,923
- You okay?
- Yeah.

1051
00:51:01,826 --> 00:51:03,060
- I'll hold on.
- Yes, sure.

1052
00:51:06,230 --> 00:51:07,230
- Ready?
- Yep.

1053
00:51:07,531 --> 00:51:09,465
I was super nervous and super excited.

1054
00:51:09,734 --> 00:51:11,134
I was blushing so much.

1055
00:51:11,702 --> 00:51:12,635
Wow, wait.

1056
00:51:13,237 --> 00:51:14,571
- You can hold on tight.
- Okay.

1057
00:51:18,576 --> 00:51:21,178
This is actually kind of fun.

1058
00:51:21,179 --> 00:51:22,279
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

1059
00:51:22,613 --> 00:51:23,714
Tell me if it's too fast.

1060
00:51:24,014 --> 00:51:26,215
- I think faster would be fine.
- Really?

1061
00:51:27,852 --> 00:51:28,952
This feels awesome.

1062
00:51:29,620 --> 00:51:30,754
(Officially off-road)

1063
00:51:30,755 --> 00:51:32,722
- You're a good driver.
- You think so?

1064
00:51:35,459 --> 00:51:36,592
This is so fun.

1065
00:51:37,828 --> 00:51:39,295
It feels like a video game.

1066
00:51:39,296 --> 00:51:40,296
Right?

1067
00:51:40,831 --> 00:51:41,731
I love it.

1068
00:51:42,700 --> 00:51:44,468
- It's such a unique experience.
- Right?

1069
00:51:44,469 --> 00:51:47,203
Bet no one's having more fun than us.

1070
00:51:47,204 --> 00:51:48,438
No chance.

1071
00:51:54,514 --> 00:51:56,012
This feels so surreal right now.

1072
00:51:56,781 --> 00:51:58,081
I'm so happy.

1073
00:51:58,415 --> 00:51:59,348
Really?

1074
00:52:00,252 --> 00:52:02,052
I'll never forget this.

1075
00:52:02,253 --> 00:52:03,721
I'll remember it forever.

1076
00:52:03,954 --> 00:52:05,021
What an experience.

1077
00:52:05,022 --> 00:52:06,756
- It'll stay with me forever.
- Same here.

1078
00:52:09,226 --> 00:52:10,393
No way.

1079
00:52:12,830 --> 00:52:14,230
(The ATV won't move.)

1080
00:52:14,898 --> 00:52:16,432
(The instructor to the rescue)

1081
00:52:16,673 --> 00:52:18,641
- Looks like the wheel is stuck.
- Okay.

1082
00:52:18,869 --> 00:52:20,237
- Could you hop off for a sec?
- Okay.

1083
00:52:21,873 --> 00:52:22,838
Are your hands okay?

1084
00:52:23,707 --> 00:52:24,607
Wipe them off.

1085
00:52:26,410 --> 00:52:28,378
- You'll get dirty.
- I already am.

1086
00:52:31,348 --> 00:52:32,481
I'll never forget this.

1087
00:52:34,084 --> 00:52:37,620
I really like guys
who are sweet and attentive.

1088
00:52:37,621 --> 00:52:39,989
And In Joong is super attentive.

1089
00:52:39,990 --> 00:52:41,957
Whenever we hit puddles...

1090
00:52:42,226 --> 00:52:43,193
Watch the water.

1091
00:52:43,527 --> 00:52:45,294
he slowed down.

1092
00:52:46,490 --> 00:52:47,457
- Watch the water.
- Okay.

1093
00:52:48,399 --> 00:52:49,399
Careful.

1094
00:52:49,934 --> 00:52:51,067
Watch the puddle.

1095
00:52:51,735 --> 00:52:53,235
If there were branches or obstacles...

1096
00:52:53,637 --> 00:52:54,570
Ye In, duck.

1097
00:52:55,706 --> 00:52:57,073
he'd tell me to duck.

1098
00:52:57,074 --> 00:52:57,940
Nice.

1099
00:52:58,512 --> 00:53:02,011
I saw how considerate he was.

1100
00:53:03,781 --> 00:53:05,849
So my feelings for him shot way up.

1101
00:53:07,017 --> 00:53:07,984
Thank you.

1102
00:53:10,153 --> 00:53:11,053
Here.

1103
00:53:15,025 --> 00:53:16,092
- All set?
- Yes.

1104
00:53:17,394 --> 00:53:19,095
- Shall we get going again?
- Let's go.

1105
00:53:20,998 --> 00:53:22,866
(Back on the road)

1106
00:53:24,269 --> 00:53:25,802
Are you getting the hang of it?

1107
00:53:25,803 --> 00:53:26,703
Yep.

1108
00:53:28,672 --> 00:53:30,373
(In perfect sync)

1109
00:53:30,908 --> 00:53:32,242
- This feels great.
- Ready?

1110
00:53:33,944 --> 00:53:36,012
(Squeeze)

1111
00:53:36,113 --> 00:53:36,979
- Wow.
- Ah!

1112
00:53:36,980 --> 00:53:38,681
(Flying down the hill)

1113
00:53:39,550 --> 00:53:40,650
I love it!

1114
00:53:44,254 --> 00:53:45,554
This is so fun.

1115
00:53:47,758 --> 00:53:49,158
It feels amazing.

1116
00:53:49,393 --> 00:53:51,494
- It really feels like Jeju Island.
- I know, right?

1117
00:53:51,662 --> 00:53:53,996
I think this is
a once-in-a-lifetime thing.

1118
00:53:55,899 --> 00:53:57,433
One, two, three.

1119
00:54:01,639 --> 00:54:04,541
It felt like that one ride
brought us way closer.

1120
00:54:04,908 --> 00:54:06,842
She seemed so prim and proper.

1121
00:54:07,111 --> 00:54:10,146
But she was so chill, like, "Go faster."

1122
00:54:10,447 --> 00:54:12,114
It was so attractive.

1123
00:54:12,549 --> 00:54:13,516
My heart was racing.

1124
00:54:14,084 --> 00:54:15,551
Riding an ATV,

1125
00:54:15,552 --> 00:54:18,054
you could easily complain
about getting soaked.

1126
00:54:18,055 --> 00:54:20,056
But he didn't at all.

1127
00:54:20,057 --> 00:54:21,891
He kept looking out for me.

1128
00:54:21,892 --> 00:54:24,694
And seeing that side of him...

1129
00:54:24,862 --> 00:54:28,298
made the date even more fun.

1130
00:54:29,033 --> 00:54:31,334
When we got off at the end,

1131
00:54:31,335 --> 00:54:32,937
she felt like my girlfriend.

1132
00:54:33,570 --> 00:54:34,937
It was such a strange feeling.

1133
00:54:37,608 --> 00:54:39,142
- A girlfriend.
- That's the best way to put it.

1134
00:54:39,143 --> 00:54:40,843
That's so romantic.

1135
00:54:40,844 --> 00:54:42,380
Maybe even more so because of the rain?

1136
00:54:42,381 --> 00:54:45,648
When it rains,
you focus on each other more.

1137
00:54:46,250 --> 00:54:48,017
Hop in and fix up in the mirror.

1138
00:54:48,018 --> 00:54:49,352
Thank you.

1139
00:54:49,653 --> 00:54:50,686
I'll be in in ten.

1140
00:54:51,088 --> 00:54:52,021
That's quick.

1141
00:54:55,693 --> 00:54:58,762
(In Joong waited outside for a long time.)

1142
00:55:01,398 --> 00:55:03,399
- All done?
- I just gave up.

1143
00:55:03,734 --> 00:55:05,401
- There's no saving it.
- No?

1144
00:55:06,003 --> 00:55:08,438
I look like I just stepped
out of the shower.

1145
00:55:08,906 --> 00:55:11,007
You look pretty right now, though.
I swear.

1146
00:55:11,008 --> 00:55:12,608
Stop lying.

1147
00:55:12,609 --> 00:55:13,576
No, seriously.

1148
00:55:13,953 --> 00:55:15,419
- There's a rainbow.
- Where?

1149
00:55:15,444 --> 00:55:16,712
See that rainbow?

1150
00:55:16,713 --> 00:55:17,813
- Oh, wow!
- I know, right?

1151
00:55:19,750 --> 00:55:21,818
- That's crazy.
- Unbelievable.

1152
00:55:22,786 --> 00:55:24,019
It's super clear.

1153
00:55:24,488 --> 00:55:26,823
It goes all the way across. Do you see it?

1154
00:55:27,057 --> 00:55:28,224
Over there.

1155
00:55:28,594 --> 00:55:29,892
It stretches from here to there.

1156
00:55:30,370 --> 00:55:32,438
- Oh, wow.
- See it now? A half circle.

1157
00:55:32,463 --> 00:55:33,396
Incredible.

1158
00:55:35,265 --> 00:55:36,799
Do you just see rainbows this easily?

1159
00:55:36,800 --> 00:55:37,833
I don't think so.

1160
00:55:38,268 --> 00:55:39,735
This is so cool.

1161
00:55:40,204 --> 00:55:41,137
So cool.

1162
00:55:41,905 --> 00:55:43,672
- Unbelievable.
- It's so pretty.

1163
00:55:44,074 --> 00:55:47,410
Honestly, seeing one like that
was a first for me.

1164
00:55:48,245 --> 00:55:49,345
Wow.

1165
00:55:49,681 --> 00:55:52,148
- I'll never forget it.
- Same.

1166
00:55:53,450 --> 00:55:56,019
Being with someone I have feelings for...

1167
00:55:56,020 --> 00:55:58,187
and seeing a rainbow
doesn't happen every day.

1168
00:55:58,188 --> 00:55:59,088
Is this fate?

1169
00:55:59,523 --> 00:56:00,823
That's honestly what I thought.

1170
00:56:01,725 --> 00:56:03,392
Thank you so much.

1171
00:56:03,393 --> 00:56:05,562
- You too.
- You drove the whole time.

1172
00:56:06,163 --> 00:56:07,130
It was so much fun.

1173
00:56:07,231 --> 00:56:08,631
Should I wash up downstairs?

1174
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:11,033
My feet.

1175
00:56:11,468 --> 00:56:12,401
Oh, right.

1176
00:56:12,402 --> 00:56:13,502
You're okay, right?

1177
00:56:13,737 --> 00:56:15,438
(Kitchen towels acquired)

1178
00:56:16,406 --> 00:56:17,539
Follow the footprints.

1179
00:56:19,103 --> 00:56:20,976
- Hold on.
- Wait, really?

1180
00:56:22,713 --> 00:56:23,646
Go ahead.

1181
00:56:25,449 --> 00:56:26,549
- Like this.
- This is hilarious.

1182
00:56:27,117 --> 00:56:28,217
This is actually genius.

1183
00:56:28,218 --> 00:56:29,118
(Towel by towel)

1184
00:56:29,119 --> 00:56:30,419
It's like dominoes.

1185
00:56:30,420 --> 00:56:33,289
This is so funny.

1186
00:56:36,527 --> 00:56:37,527
It's hilarious.

1187
00:56:38,963 --> 00:56:40,096
(A path to the bathroom for Ye In)

1188
00:56:40,097 --> 00:56:41,130
I'm on a roll.

1189
00:56:43,734 --> 00:56:46,169
My feet are a total mess,

1190
00:56:46,170 --> 00:56:48,438
- so I'd recommend not looking.
- Oh, got it.

1191
00:56:48,939 --> 00:56:50,106
Do you need anything?

1192
00:56:50,107 --> 00:56:51,540
I'll just wash my feet...

1193
00:56:51,541 --> 00:56:52,808
- and head back up.
- Ah, okay.

1194
00:56:54,978 --> 00:56:58,247
In Joong tore off paper towels...

1195
00:56:58,248 --> 00:57:00,215
and made me stepping stones with them.

1196
00:57:01,552 --> 00:57:03,019
Isn't that the cutest thing?

1197
00:57:03,220 --> 00:57:05,021
Laying down paper towels.

1198
00:57:05,355 --> 00:57:07,323
That's next-level thoughtful.

1199
00:57:07,324 --> 00:57:08,357
Who even thinks of that?

1200
00:57:08,358 --> 00:57:10,726
If she were my girlfriend,
I would've carried her.

1201
00:57:10,727 --> 00:57:12,695
But we barely know each other,

1202
00:57:12,696 --> 00:57:13,796
so I couldn't carry her.

1203
00:57:13,931 --> 00:57:15,430
Then I saw the paper towels.

1204
00:57:15,431 --> 00:57:16,699
I instantly thought of using them.

1205
00:57:17,334 --> 00:57:18,634
Are you wearing different shoes?

1206
00:57:18,635 --> 00:57:20,169
- Yeah, another pair.
- Got it.

1207
00:57:20,170 --> 00:57:22,271
Then I'll set these outside.

1208
00:57:22,272 --> 00:57:23,572
Thank you.

1209
00:57:25,409 --> 00:57:27,944
(Drying Ye In's shoes in the breeze)

1210
00:57:28,712 --> 00:57:30,212
- Let's go.
- I'm starving.

1211
00:57:30,213 --> 00:57:31,180
Me too.

1212
00:57:33,317 --> 00:57:34,317
This is going to be fun.

1213
00:57:34,685 --> 00:57:36,552
- Yeah.
- It'll be so much fun.

1214
00:57:37,487 --> 00:57:38,420
Let's go.

1215
00:57:38,890 --> 00:57:39,856
Let's do this.

1216
00:57:40,858 --> 00:57:41,825
We've got this.

1217
00:57:44,328 --> 00:57:45,995
Wow, look at the weather.

1218
00:57:46,096 --> 00:57:47,797
Good thing the weather's nice.

1219
00:57:48,332 --> 00:57:49,732
Told you I'm a weather fairy.

1220
00:57:49,733 --> 00:57:50,633
True.

1221
00:57:51,535 --> 00:57:52,902
I'm glad I came with you, Yu Ra.

1222
00:57:53,704 --> 00:57:54,771
And the weather's gorgeous.

1223
00:57:55,139 --> 00:57:56,238
This ocean is amazing.

1224
00:57:56,740 --> 00:57:58,908
I can't even remember
the last time I went in the ocean.

1225
00:58:00,244 --> 00:58:02,612
- Hello.
- Hello.

1226
00:58:03,580 --> 00:58:05,981
- Wow, it's deep.
- It's getting deeper.

1227
00:58:07,117 --> 00:58:08,584
So I'm supposed to...

1228
00:58:09,319 --> 00:58:10,520
ride the waves out here, right?

1229
00:58:11,355 --> 00:58:12,355
I'll hold it for you.

1230
00:58:12,456 --> 00:58:13,556
Thank you.

1231
00:58:15,459 --> 00:58:16,392
Do you want to hold on?

1232
00:58:17,027 --> 00:58:19,195
Grab my arm. Hold on tight.

1233
00:58:21,832 --> 00:58:25,168
I was wobbling,
so he told me to hold onto him.

1234
00:58:25,202 --> 00:58:26,269
I was so grateful.

1235
00:58:27,304 --> 00:58:28,237
I melted.

1236
00:58:28,872 --> 00:58:30,673
I think he has a sweet side.

1237
00:58:31,308 --> 00:58:34,176
(Arrived at the surf spot)

1238
00:58:35,078 --> 00:58:36,278
Go, Yu Ra!

1239
00:58:36,279 --> 00:58:37,446
(Yu Ra tries first.)

1240
00:58:41,351 --> 00:58:44,053
I didn't even have time to get my footing.

1241
00:58:44,688 --> 00:58:46,856
(Round two)

1242
00:58:48,792 --> 00:58:49,992
Nice. You did great.

1243
00:58:51,128 --> 00:58:52,095
Go!

1244
00:58:52,096 --> 00:58:53,563
(Jin Sung's turn)

1245
00:58:55,132 --> 00:58:55,898
Oh no!

1246
00:58:58,068 --> 00:58:59,035
You got this.

1247
00:58:59,836 --> 00:59:01,103
And three!

1248
00:59:01,571 --> 00:59:03,739
Wow! Let's go!

1249
00:59:07,110 --> 00:59:08,043
She's good.

1250
00:59:09,005 --> 00:59:10,472
- You got this!
- Ready.

1251
00:59:10,981 --> 00:59:12,148
And three!

1252
00:59:27,223 --> 00:59:28,398
Wow, it's...

1253
00:59:29,708 --> 00:59:31,166
This isn't easy.

1254
00:59:31,401 --> 00:59:33,802
Thank you. At least I stood up once today.

1255
00:59:33,803 --> 00:59:36,672
The waves were rough, but you did great.

1256
00:59:37,174 --> 00:59:38,808
Did I ride it for like 0.1 seconds?

1257
00:59:39,376 --> 00:59:40,943
That still counts as a win.

1258
00:59:42,512 --> 00:59:44,379
Great job.

1259
00:59:44,380 --> 00:59:46,381
- You did great.
- You too.

1260
00:59:47,150 --> 00:59:49,251
We need to work
on our rock-paper-scissors.

1261
00:59:50,787 --> 00:59:53,355
It's not about how well you surf.

1262
00:59:54,925 --> 00:59:56,692
- Today was so fun.
- Yeah?

1263
00:59:57,527 --> 00:59:58,861
I had a great time too.

1264
00:59:59,076 --> 01:00:00,097
Do you drop formalities easily?

1265
01:00:00,777 --> 01:00:01,796
It comes easily to me.

1266
01:00:02,699 --> 01:00:03,533
Me too.

1267
01:00:04,226 --> 01:00:05,302
In that case,

1268
01:00:05,635 --> 01:00:06,970
could you speak casually first?

1269
01:00:07,139 --> 01:00:08,271
- Should I?
- Sure.

1270
01:00:09,506 --> 01:00:11,674
"Can you switch to casual speech first?"

1271
01:00:11,675 --> 01:00:13,043
Now they're getting closer.

1272
01:00:13,106 --> 01:00:14,543
Dong Su drops formalities a lot.

1273
01:00:14,544 --> 01:00:16,146
He's a pro at it by now.

1274
01:00:18,273 --> 01:00:19,748
(They reach a seaside restaurant.)

1275
01:00:19,749 --> 01:00:20,750
This is unreal.

1276
01:00:21,418 --> 01:00:23,220
I bet it's even prettier after dark.

1277
01:00:23,487 --> 01:00:24,721
I love this.

1278
01:00:26,917 --> 01:00:27,824
So romantic.

1279
01:00:28,457 --> 01:00:29,217
Right?

1280
01:00:29,251 --> 01:00:30,193
(Startled Jwa Hyeon)

1281
01:00:31,204 --> 01:00:32,931
- You scared me.
- Hi.

1282
01:00:32,984 --> 01:00:34,598
What a lucky find.

1283
01:00:37,368 --> 01:00:39,236
That cat's gorgeous.

1284
01:00:39,238 --> 01:00:41,922
(Showing off its good looks)

1285
01:00:42,015 --> 01:00:44,035
Now it's loafing.

1286
01:00:44,037 --> 01:00:45,295
(Distracted by the cat)

1287
01:00:45,648 --> 01:00:48,355
(The food arrives.)

1288
01:00:49,068 --> 01:00:50,747
- Look at that.
- That's incredible.

1289
01:00:53,125 --> 01:00:54,417
I was starving.

1290
01:00:55,184 --> 01:00:57,754
- You take this.
- I'll do what you did.

1291
01:00:59,138 --> 01:01:00,257
Can you eat this?

1292
01:01:00,557 --> 01:01:03,293
- I can eat sea urchin.
- I haven't used my chopsticks yet.

1293
01:01:06,570 --> 01:01:08,870
(A slice of raw fish with sea urchin roe)

1294
01:01:11,690 --> 01:01:12,536
Is it unreal?

1295
01:01:17,621 --> 01:01:18,341
So good.

1296
01:01:19,442 --> 01:01:20,210
Incredible.

1297
01:01:20,354 --> 01:01:22,768
(At a loss for words)

1298
01:01:23,354 --> 01:01:25,148
I can't believe this. What do you think?

1299
01:01:25,966 --> 01:01:28,185
It's amazing.

1300
01:01:29,746 --> 01:01:31,021
Guess I like raw fish after all.

1301
01:01:32,939 --> 01:01:34,124
She felt it too.

1302
01:01:34,192 --> 01:01:35,192
So good, right?

1303
01:01:36,393 --> 01:01:38,628
What matters most to you
in a relationship?

1304
01:01:40,397 --> 01:01:42,599
I think a lot about the future.

1305
01:01:43,033 --> 01:01:44,000
Marriage?

1306
01:01:44,240 --> 01:01:45,535
I've always dated with marriage in mind.

1307
01:01:45,594 --> 01:01:46,236
You?

1308
01:01:46,307 --> 01:01:48,538
I was a little surprised
because I feel the same way.

1309
01:01:48,772 --> 01:01:53,310
I see marriage as the end goal too.

1310
01:01:54,010 --> 01:01:56,010
Have you ever felt like you wanted
to marry someone?

1311
01:01:56,680 --> 01:01:59,783
Someone I could spend a long time with
and never get bored.

1312
01:02:01,785 --> 01:02:05,021
- That's what matters most to me too.
- I like it when we feel like friends.

1313
01:02:05,172 --> 01:02:06,489
Have you had that before?

1314
01:02:06,756 --> 01:02:09,752
I've been in both kinds of relationships.

1315
01:02:09,932 --> 01:02:11,795
Looking back on when I was happiest,

1316
01:02:12,329 --> 01:02:14,197
it was the ones
that felt like friendships.

1317
01:02:14,324 --> 01:02:16,800
Those made me way happier.

1318
01:02:18,610 --> 01:02:19,402
Friends.

1319
01:02:20,470 --> 01:02:23,240
We talked about what matters most
to each of us when dating.

1320
01:02:23,773 --> 01:02:27,811
I told her I usually date
with marriage in mind.

1321
01:02:28,278 --> 01:02:30,213
Jwa Hyeon said she feels the same way.

1322
01:02:30,248 --> 01:02:33,650
I'd been hoping to meet someone
who sees marriage as the end goal.

1323
01:02:33,793 --> 01:02:35,585
And we were on the same page there too.

1324
01:02:35,946 --> 01:02:36,786
Look at that.

1325
01:02:40,739 --> 01:02:43,939
(The sky turns pink at sunset.)

1326
01:02:44,261 --> 01:02:46,830
I like seeing that too.
People out fishing.

1327
01:03:05,122 --> 01:03:06,549
How do you feel about long-distance?

1328
01:03:07,817 --> 01:03:10,553
I've never done long-distance.

1329
01:03:10,728 --> 01:03:12,289
- You haven't? Never?
- No.

1330
01:03:12,856 --> 01:03:15,925
I feel like you'd have to trust
each other a ton.

1331
01:03:16,106 --> 01:03:17,294
It kind of scares me.

1332
01:03:17,493 --> 01:03:19,029
Maybe just because I've never tried it.

1333
01:03:19,272 --> 01:03:21,097
- Done long-distance?
- I have.

1334
01:03:21,146 --> 01:03:23,366
Really? How far apart were you?

1335
01:03:23,667 --> 01:03:24,467
Three hours?

1336
01:03:24,854 --> 01:03:25,802
Three hours?

1337
01:03:26,469 --> 01:03:28,517
I bet it'd be long-distance here.

1338
01:03:28,518 --> 01:03:30,307
Really? I could see that.

1339
01:03:30,740 --> 01:03:33,143
That's why he's bringing up distance.

1340
01:03:33,458 --> 01:03:34,878
I actually like long-distance.

1341
01:03:35,278 --> 01:03:36,846
Really? What do you like about it?

1342
01:03:36,940 --> 01:03:40,683
You don't see each other often,
so you try harder not to fight.

1343
01:03:40,684 --> 01:03:42,552
Time apart makes you miss each other more.

1344
01:03:42,601 --> 01:03:44,220
Your time together feels more precious.

1345
01:03:44,815 --> 01:03:47,057
Dong Su was the one
who asked her about that.

1346
01:03:47,089 --> 01:03:48,888
- It could end up being long-distance.
- For him.

1347
01:03:48,902 --> 01:03:50,902
It'd probably be long-distance.

1348
01:03:51,161 --> 01:03:53,262
First off, he's interested in Jwa Hyeon.

1349
01:03:53,263 --> 01:03:54,830
- Right.
- He's thinking ahead.

1350
01:03:54,831 --> 01:03:56,715
- He's weighing his options.
- Yes, his own situation.

1351
01:03:56,741 --> 01:03:57,600
- Right.
- Yes.

1352
01:03:57,620 --> 01:03:59,620
- He didn't ask this earlier.
- Right.

1353
01:03:59,669 --> 01:04:01,271
- With Yu Ra.
- He didn't.

1354
01:04:01,905 --> 01:04:04,674
We don't know where anyone lives yet.

1355
01:04:04,858 --> 01:04:06,476
You've got an accent, though.

1356
01:04:07,110 --> 01:04:08,411
Did you just catch an accent?

1357
01:04:08,578 --> 01:04:11,514
You sound like you have an accent
all the time.

1358
01:04:14,784 --> 01:04:17,954
So when distance came up,
my ears really perked up.

1359
01:04:19,656 --> 01:04:20,890
I don't have an accent.

1360
01:04:21,758 --> 01:04:24,194
I don't really care
if my accent slips out, though.

1361
01:04:24,494 --> 01:04:26,696
I wanted to keep it under wraps
until the reveal.

1362
01:04:28,198 --> 01:04:29,366
Guess I can't.

1363
01:04:30,483 --> 01:04:31,701
I have to ask, though.

1364
01:04:32,302 --> 01:04:34,838
You have a sibling here, right?

1365
01:04:35,381 --> 01:04:36,773
Here's why I'm asking.

1366
01:04:36,902 --> 01:04:41,144
None of the other women
speak with an accent.

1367
01:04:41,911 --> 01:04:43,246
I could be faking it, you know.

1368
01:04:43,389 --> 01:04:44,647
You can fake it that well?

1369
01:04:45,715 --> 01:04:47,484
You deserve a Baeksang Arts Award.

1370
01:04:48,985 --> 01:04:50,687
I've figured out your job. Actor.

1371
01:04:51,262 --> 01:04:52,355
You're an actor.

1372
01:04:52,628 --> 01:04:53,656
You've got a point.

1373
01:04:53,955 --> 01:04:55,258
You really think so?

1374
01:04:55,731 --> 01:04:57,127
It's tough to hide an accent.

1375
01:04:58,027 --> 01:05:01,030
- I'm stuffed.
- Right? We were so hungry earlier.

1376
01:05:01,942 --> 01:05:04,067
Where'd it go? Where'd the sunset go?

1377
01:05:04,567 --> 01:05:06,034
Well, it's dark now.

1378
01:05:06,035 --> 01:05:08,029
(Darkness settles over the sea.)

1379
01:05:08,729 --> 01:05:10,940
It'll look amazing
once it gets even darker.

1380
01:05:12,742 --> 01:05:14,043
We're on our last drink.

1381
01:05:15,027 --> 01:05:17,534
(Finishing their last drinks)

1382
01:05:24,053 --> 01:05:26,289
Which sounds better,
the waves or the trees?

1383
01:05:26,756 --> 01:05:28,825
They're almost tied for me.

1384
01:05:28,865 --> 01:05:31,227
The ocean moves me a little more, though.

1385
01:05:31,895 --> 01:05:32,629
The ocean?

1386
01:05:33,263 --> 01:05:34,597
I don't get to hear it often.

1387
01:05:36,431 --> 01:05:38,168
- Right, exactly.
- The sheer scale of it?

1388
01:05:38,968 --> 01:05:40,503
I'd go with the sound of the trees.

1389
01:05:40,604 --> 01:05:41,905
Why the trees?

1390
01:05:42,698 --> 01:05:46,776
I'd never listened to the trees like that
while lying in the breeze.

1391
01:05:47,777 --> 01:05:49,145
And you loved it.

1392
01:05:49,998 --> 01:05:51,014
I really did.

1393
01:05:51,848 --> 01:05:55,985
I'm glad I got the chance
to get to know you.

1394
01:05:56,543 --> 01:05:57,320
You know what?

1395
01:05:57,787 --> 01:05:59,787
I wanted to spend time with you too.

1396
01:06:00,056 --> 01:06:00,924
You did?

1397
01:06:01,191 --> 01:06:04,027
I'd mentioned I really like people
with a personality like yours.

1398
01:06:04,627 --> 01:06:06,763
So when it turned out to be you today,

1399
01:06:07,130 --> 01:06:08,031
I was really happy.

1400
01:06:08,154 --> 01:06:09,081
Really?

1401
01:06:09,966 --> 01:06:11,768
Can we hang out like this again?

1402
01:06:12,261 --> 01:06:13,129
I think so.

1403
01:06:18,021 --> 01:06:18,875
That eye smile.

1404
01:06:18,894 --> 01:06:19,909
Look at that eye smile.

1405
01:06:20,068 --> 01:06:21,188
What's going on?

1406
01:06:21,248 --> 01:06:23,012
They're really hitting it off.

1407
01:06:27,210 --> 01:06:29,370
Thanks to you, Jin Sung,

1408
01:06:29,395 --> 01:06:31,515
I get to eat some amazing meat today.

1409
01:06:31,945 --> 01:06:34,123
About last night, though.

1410
01:06:34,139 --> 01:06:36,426
Is where you went a secret forever?

1411
01:06:37,463 --> 01:06:40,063
- What went on there?
- You mean what happened there?

1412
01:06:41,583 --> 01:06:42,265
Yeah.

1413
01:06:44,103 --> 01:06:47,637
What kind of dynamic do you prefer?

1414
01:06:48,505 --> 01:06:49,772
I like dating someone older.

1415
01:06:50,063 --> 01:06:51,941
Older, younger, or the same age?

1416
01:06:52,203 --> 01:06:53,843
- I prefer older.
- Older?

1417
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:54,944
How much older?

1418
01:06:55,107 --> 01:06:57,113
- Maybe seven or eight years?
- Up to seven or eight?

1419
01:06:59,215 --> 01:07:01,317
Jin Sung, older, younger, or your age?

1420
01:07:01,395 --> 01:07:05,175
I'm most comfortable
with someone my own age.

1421
01:07:05,177 --> 01:07:06,256
- Your top pick?
- Yes.

1422
01:07:06,523 --> 01:07:08,625
I like it when we feel like friends.

1423
01:07:08,795 --> 01:07:10,527
- Total opposites.
- Opposite types.

1424
01:07:10,962 --> 01:07:15,214
Jin Sung just seemed
like such an easygoing guy.

1425
01:07:15,215 --> 01:07:17,215
There was a genuine innocence to him.

1426
01:07:17,233 --> 01:07:20,570
He came across as a really kind person.

1427
01:07:20,813 --> 01:07:23,406
I felt comfortable talking to her,

1428
01:07:23,673 --> 01:07:26,109
so I'd love to talk to her again.

1429
01:07:27,187 --> 01:07:30,500
(Min Seo and Ji Hwan
at Gimnyeong Restaurant)

1430
01:07:30,920 --> 01:07:32,248
Let's dig in.

1431
01:07:32,571 --> 01:07:33,850
Let's eat.

1432
01:07:47,082 --> 01:07:50,762
(They just eat in silence.)

1433
01:07:54,771 --> 01:07:56,439
It's so quiet.

1434
01:07:56,706 --> 01:07:59,526
There should be some sizzling
and splattering oil.

1435
01:07:59,793 --> 01:08:00,743
It feels dead.

1436
01:08:00,839 --> 01:08:03,346
Min Seo's an introvert too.

1437
01:08:04,446 --> 01:08:06,086
Here's the raw shrimp.

1438
01:08:07,993 --> 01:08:08,952
Finally!

1439
01:08:16,025 --> 01:08:17,520
(Squealing)

1440
01:08:18,124 --> 01:08:19,329
I'm going to pass out.

1441
01:08:20,724 --> 01:08:22,532
Do you like octopus?

1442
01:08:24,944 --> 01:08:25,868
I do.

1443
01:08:38,348 --> 01:08:39,415
This is so good.

1444
01:08:43,032 --> 01:08:46,456
I'm so hungry.
All I've been doing is eating.

1445
01:08:46,672 --> 01:08:48,925
I really should be making conversation.

1446
01:08:49,452 --> 01:08:51,027
I must've been starving.

1447
01:08:51,210 --> 01:08:52,261
I know.

1448
01:08:53,603 --> 01:08:55,531
It's nice here, isn't it?

1449
01:08:56,297 --> 01:08:57,934
I had no idea this place was here.

1450
01:09:07,895 --> 01:09:10,380
I knew he was on the quiet side.

1451
01:09:16,006 --> 01:09:18,855
He was even quieter than I'd imagined.

1452
01:09:23,526 --> 01:09:24,710
She says he's really quiet.

1453
01:09:24,750 --> 01:09:27,657
Min Seo isn't exactly quiet herself.

1454
01:09:27,670 --> 01:09:28,998
Right, we've seen that.

1455
01:09:29,037 --> 01:09:30,767
- Not at all.
- She's holding back.

1456
01:09:30,804 --> 01:09:33,269
- Someone just needs to draw her out.
- Right.

1457
01:09:33,324 --> 01:09:35,438
That's the tough part for Ji Hwan.

1458
01:09:36,482 --> 01:09:38,441
- What can he do?
- This is tricky.

1459
01:09:43,362 --> 01:09:46,822
(Silence hangs between them.)

1460
01:09:47,022 --> 01:09:50,053
Now that I'm sitting here,
the appetite is kind of gone.

1461
01:09:50,881 --> 01:09:52,555
I think we're just too hungry.

1462
01:09:52,582 --> 01:09:55,168
I think so too.

1463
01:09:57,327 --> 01:10:00,699
That awkwardness with Ji Hwan
crept back in,

1464
01:10:00,700 --> 01:10:03,066
and I had no idea what to do or say.

1465
01:10:08,684 --> 01:10:11,074
Is there any food you really love?

1466
01:10:11,310 --> 01:10:12,575
Really love?

1467
01:10:12,990 --> 01:10:13,876
Sashimi.

1468
01:10:14,017 --> 01:10:15,751
I eat sashimi all the time.

1469
01:10:15,752 --> 01:10:17,752
Sashimi... Go ahead.

1470
01:10:20,278 --> 01:10:21,251
Go ahead and eat.

1471
01:10:30,115 --> 01:10:31,173
- That's just...
- "Go ahead and eat?"

1472
01:10:31,174 --> 01:10:32,595
"How much?"

1473
01:10:32,596 --> 01:10:34,164
"How much sashimi do you eat?"

1474
01:10:34,166 --> 01:10:35,498
What kind of conversation is that?

1475
01:10:35,500 --> 01:10:36,654
He asks her a question,

1476
01:10:36,678 --> 01:10:38,433
and when she says,
"I love sashimi. I eat it all the time,"

1477
01:10:38,458 --> 01:10:40,031
- he just says, "Go ahead and eat."
- "Go ahead."

1478
01:10:40,033 --> 01:10:40,956
"Help yourself."

1479
01:10:40,957 --> 01:10:42,259
He could've asked,
"I'm more of a meat guy."

1480
01:10:42,284 --> 01:10:44,465
Or, "How about having it with ramyeon?"

1481
01:10:44,699 --> 01:10:45,963
When he gives such dry answers,

1482
01:10:45,987 --> 01:10:48,277
it's impossible
to keep the conversation going.

1483
01:10:49,831 --> 01:10:50,947
This is really good.

1484
01:10:57,825 --> 01:11:01,023
Are you always this quiet?

1485
01:11:03,897 --> 01:11:04,994
I'm just curious.

1486
01:11:07,305 --> 01:11:08,298
Yeah.

1487
01:11:09,691 --> 01:11:10,900
I'm usually even quieter.

1488
01:11:14,673 --> 01:11:17,006
Have you ever thought
about speaking a little louder?

1489
01:11:17,229 --> 01:11:18,508
Is that something you want to work on?

1490
01:11:18,510 --> 01:11:20,463
Yeah. I don't think...

1491
01:11:20,465 --> 01:11:25,248
speaking so slowly and quietly is
necessarily a good habit for me.

1492
01:11:25,250 --> 01:11:26,751
I talk really slowly...

1493
01:11:26,752 --> 01:11:28,551
and my voice doesn't carry.

1494
01:11:28,912 --> 01:11:32,956
I've actually thought
about taking voice lessons.

1495
01:11:32,958 --> 01:11:34,557
To learn how to project my voice.

1496
01:11:35,342 --> 01:11:39,155
Honestly, I'd love to learn
how to speak as softly as you do.

1497
01:11:41,145 --> 01:11:42,531
I tend to talk fast...

1498
01:11:42,846 --> 01:11:44,379
and loudly.

1499
01:11:45,459 --> 01:11:46,618
That's a good thing.

1500
01:11:47,978 --> 01:11:50,102
I was surprised,

1501
01:11:50,103 --> 01:11:51,641
but it also made me really happy.

1502
01:11:52,722 --> 01:11:56,277
I'd always been self-conscious...

1503
01:11:56,278 --> 01:11:59,678
about how softly I spoke.

1504
01:11:59,679 --> 01:12:01,751
So hearing her say
something positive about it...

1505
01:12:02,688 --> 01:12:03,987
meant a lot to me.

1506
01:12:05,344 --> 01:12:07,923
I felt a little more at ease around her,

1507
01:12:07,925 --> 01:12:10,259
and I think that made my heart flutter.

1508
01:12:12,165 --> 01:12:15,324
- What exactly did he like about that?
- I really can't read this guy.

1509
01:12:15,911 --> 01:12:18,276
It's so hard to even bounce off him.

1510
01:12:18,494 --> 01:12:20,169
Maybe he grew up
in the mountains or something.

1511
01:12:21,481 --> 01:12:22,672
Who knows?

1512
01:12:23,023 --> 01:12:25,574
We actually spent quite a while together.

1513
01:12:25,742 --> 01:12:28,043
Somehow, though...

1514
01:12:30,011 --> 01:12:33,282
I don't think we had
a very deep conversation.

1515
01:12:35,669 --> 01:12:39,889
I'd been interested in Ji Hwan
ever since we met,

1516
01:12:40,004 --> 01:12:42,199
so I asked him a ton of questions.

1517
01:12:42,200 --> 01:12:45,094
All I got back were short answers...

1518
01:12:45,341 --> 01:12:47,997
and the occasional question in return.

1519
01:12:48,856 --> 01:12:51,400
Do you work out regularly?
Like hitting the gym?

1520
01:12:51,524 --> 01:12:52,235
Yeah.

1521
01:12:53,275 --> 01:12:55,438
I work out pretty much every day.

1522
01:12:58,950 --> 01:13:01,978
Have you gotten settled
into the house yet?

1523
01:13:01,980 --> 01:13:02,945
Yeah.

1524
01:13:05,630 --> 01:13:07,683
After walking around a few times.

1525
01:13:16,092 --> 01:13:20,129
(Their conversation was filled
with long, awkward silences.)

1526
01:13:22,102 --> 01:13:25,001
He didn't seem curious about me at all.

1527
01:13:25,849 --> 01:13:28,471
So I'm still not sure where things stand.

1528
01:13:29,842 --> 01:13:31,368
(Ye In and In Joong)

1529
01:13:31,369 --> 01:13:32,532
This is so good.

1530
01:13:32,533 --> 01:13:35,592
I still can't get over those
stepping stones earlier.

1531
01:13:35,740 --> 01:13:38,581
Oh, finally! Someone actually talking!

1532
01:13:39,214 --> 01:13:40,583
- Oh, the stepping stones?
- Yeah.

1533
01:13:42,436 --> 01:13:43,953
Did the paper towels help?

1534
01:13:43,955 --> 01:13:46,255
- Yeah, they came in super handy.
- Really?

1535
01:13:47,949 --> 01:13:48,742
The stepping stones...

1536
01:13:48,743 --> 01:13:49,992
When you date someone,

1537
01:13:50,308 --> 01:13:52,154
do you usually...

1538
01:13:52,155 --> 01:13:55,035
take your time getting to know them first?

1539
01:13:55,288 --> 01:13:57,433
Or do you jump in pretty quickly?

1540
01:13:58,071 --> 01:13:59,636
I think I usually take my time.

1541
01:14:00,659 --> 01:14:03,338
Once I'm sure about someone, though,
I don't hesitate.

1542
01:14:04,205 --> 01:14:05,307
What about you?

1543
01:14:05,952 --> 01:14:08,154
I'm the type to go straight for it too...

1544
01:14:08,155 --> 01:14:10,780
once I'm sure about someone.

1545
01:14:11,722 --> 01:14:14,620
I like someone who's kindhearted.

1546
01:14:14,621 --> 01:14:18,255
And thoughtful.

1547
01:14:18,256 --> 01:14:22,825
And I think I'm drawn to someone
who takes the lead.

1548
01:14:23,882 --> 01:14:24,927
It stopped raining.

1549
01:14:25,300 --> 01:14:26,729
The weather's nice.

1550
01:14:27,463 --> 01:14:29,231
(On the way back home)

1551
01:14:30,970 --> 01:14:32,785
(Waiting)

1552
01:14:32,787 --> 01:14:34,270
Thanks.

1553
01:14:34,565 --> 01:14:36,706
You're really thoughtful.

1554
01:14:37,723 --> 01:14:39,584
Actually,

1555
01:14:39,585 --> 01:14:40,843
there's something I've been
curious about since yesterday.

1556
01:14:40,845 --> 01:14:43,646
Why did you pick me?

1557
01:14:45,014 --> 01:14:47,929
First off, you were the closest
to my ideal type physically.

1558
01:14:47,930 --> 01:14:49,619
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.

1559
01:14:50,177 --> 01:14:51,647
You have a sweet, innocent look,
kind of like a puppy.

1560
01:14:51,648 --> 01:14:53,589
And you give off such good energy.

1561
01:14:53,888 --> 01:14:55,458
"Good energy?"

1562
01:14:56,959 --> 01:14:58,361
Were you expecting that?

1563
01:14:58,362 --> 01:14:59,992
- I...
- No, not at all.

1564
01:14:59,993 --> 01:15:01,230
- Really?
- No.

1565
01:15:01,393 --> 01:15:02,531
So...

1566
01:15:03,247 --> 01:15:04,600
I was really grateful.

1567
01:15:04,731 --> 01:15:05,768
Really?

1568
01:15:06,310 --> 01:15:08,127
- Time flew by so fast, though.
- Didn't it?

1569
01:15:08,128 --> 01:15:09,870
It felt like five minutes,

1570
01:15:09,871 --> 01:15:11,871
- when over ten minutes had passed.
- To me, it felt like one minute!

1571
01:15:12,009 --> 01:15:14,043
And then the bell suddenly rang.

1572
01:15:14,045 --> 01:15:17,755
Honestly, I was hoping
you'd come out today.

1573
01:15:17,756 --> 01:15:19,382
- Really?
- Because I wanted to talk to you more.

1574
01:15:22,664 --> 01:15:24,854
- I had so much fun today.
- Me too.

1575
01:15:25,071 --> 01:15:27,523
I feel like we were laughing
the whole time.

1576
01:15:28,551 --> 01:15:30,164
We have quite a bit of time here,

1577
01:15:30,166 --> 01:15:32,528
yet it's also pretty short
when you think about it.

1578
01:15:34,509 --> 01:15:36,732
Still, I feel like things...

1579
01:15:37,425 --> 01:15:39,168
might start shifting after today.

1580
01:15:43,458 --> 01:15:44,840
I hope so.

1581
01:15:50,007 --> 01:15:51,855
- Looks like we're the only ones here.
- What makes you say that?

1582
01:15:51,880 --> 01:15:52,982
- Nobody's around.
- Oh, there aren't any cars.

1583
01:15:53,277 --> 01:15:54,984
Are we seriously the only ones back?

1584
01:15:56,580 --> 01:15:57,853
I can't believe we're the first ones back.

1585
01:15:57,855 --> 01:15:59,855
Where is everyone else,
and what are they up to?

1586
01:16:01,260 --> 01:16:02,478
We're the first ones back.

1587
01:16:03,206 --> 01:16:04,139
Are we really first?

1588
01:16:04,140 --> 01:16:05,441
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

1589
01:16:05,442 --> 01:16:07,336
- You're not first.
- Oh, we're not?

1590
01:16:08,407 --> 01:16:10,398
- What did you guys do?
- Oh, right.

1591
01:16:10,399 --> 01:16:12,134
(Yoga)

1592
01:16:12,616 --> 01:16:15,304
I'm dying to know
how everyone else's dates went.

1593
01:16:15,473 --> 01:16:18,494
- Who went rock climbing again?
- Was it Min Seo?

1594
01:16:18,495 --> 01:16:20,342
- And Ji Hwan.
- Oh, Ji Hwan!

1595
01:16:20,495 --> 01:16:21,587
Ji Hwan and Min Seo.

1596
01:16:21,588 --> 01:16:24,313
I'm really curious
about those two together.

1597
01:16:25,229 --> 01:16:27,049
That's a pairing
I never would've pictured.

1598
01:16:29,207 --> 01:16:30,586
I was super curious.

1599
01:16:31,315 --> 01:16:34,843
I'd pictured either In Joong
or Jin Sung...

1600
01:16:34,844 --> 01:16:37,206
as my future brother-in-law,

1601
01:16:37,207 --> 01:16:39,028
and then she suddenly said Ji Hwan.

1602
01:16:39,572 --> 01:16:41,572
I didn't think my sister would click...

1603
01:16:41,574 --> 01:16:46,286
with someone as quiet
and soft-spoken as Ji Hwan.

1604
01:16:46,287 --> 01:16:48,337
So I wanted to see how it went.

1605
01:16:48,339 --> 01:16:49,738
I wonder how their date went.

1606
01:16:51,722 --> 01:16:53,722
He knows his sister inside out.

1607
01:16:53,724 --> 01:16:55,380
He's spot-on.

1608
01:16:55,381 --> 01:16:56,612
He really is her older brother.

1609
01:16:57,421 --> 01:16:59,548
- Hey.
- Hi.

1610
01:16:59,657 --> 01:17:01,083
How was your date?

1611
01:17:01,085 --> 01:17:02,785
- It was fun.
- Was it?

1612
01:17:03,476 --> 01:17:04,726
You're back.

1613
01:17:04,728 --> 01:17:07,056
- Hey.
- Oh, how was surfing?

1614
01:17:07,189 --> 01:17:09,391
(They share stories from their dates.)

1615
01:17:09,478 --> 01:17:10,557
Did you guys talk a lot?

1616
01:17:10,559 --> 01:17:11,860
(Shaking her head)

1617
01:17:11,968 --> 01:17:13,968
How was it? Did you talk much?

1618
01:17:14,169 --> 01:17:16,532
Hardly at all.

1619
01:17:16,690 --> 01:17:18,267
I think I know who she went with.

1620
01:17:18,796 --> 01:17:20,035
Hardly any talking?

1621
01:17:20,037 --> 01:17:21,470
Then it must've been Ji Hwan.

1622
01:17:21,660 --> 01:17:24,829
The vibe was really nice,
and the food was great,

1623
01:17:25,242 --> 01:17:26,742
but there were so many awkward silences.

1624
01:17:28,007 --> 01:17:29,668
All I could hear was us chewing,

1625
01:17:29,669 --> 01:17:31,480
so I could barely even swallow my food...

1626
01:17:31,826 --> 01:17:33,082
It was still nice, though.

1627
01:17:33,732 --> 01:17:36,029
I know that feeling all too well.

1628
01:17:36,030 --> 01:17:38,454
Those suffocating silences
when you're with Ji Hwan.

1629
01:17:38,954 --> 01:17:40,756
(Frustrated)

1630
01:17:41,402 --> 01:17:42,892
Did you two talk a lot?

1631
01:17:43,732 --> 01:17:45,060
Yeah, we talked nonstop.

1632
01:17:45,085 --> 01:17:46,622
In Joong was great at keeping
the conversation flowing.

1633
01:17:46,623 --> 01:17:48,878
With In Joong, the conversation
must've flowed naturally.

1634
01:17:48,880 --> 01:17:50,566
There wasn't a single awkward silence.

1635
01:17:51,033 --> 01:17:53,202
We were even saying
In Joong is like a pro host.

1636
01:17:53,227 --> 01:17:54,128
Right?

1637
01:17:54,503 --> 01:17:56,872
(And right on cue,
the professional host arrives.)

1638
01:17:57,109 --> 01:17:58,808
Min Seo, Yu Ra, how were your dates today?

1639
01:17:59,251 --> 01:18:00,976
I've heard about everyone else's dates,
just not yours.

1640
01:18:00,978 --> 01:18:02,311
It was fun.

1641
01:18:02,313 --> 01:18:04,146
I had a great time.

1642
01:18:04,264 --> 01:18:05,517
You did?

1643
01:18:05,518 --> 01:18:06,883
So it was a good time?

1644
01:18:07,690 --> 01:18:10,438
If you could do
one of the activities again...

1645
01:18:10,439 --> 01:18:11,786
I'd definitely pick yoga.

1646
01:18:11,787 --> 01:18:12,921
- Oh, really?
- Again?

1647
01:18:12,922 --> 01:18:14,448
(He'd choose couples yoga all over again.)

1648
01:18:14,449 --> 01:18:15,737
You're not curious
about the other activities?

1649
01:18:15,738 --> 01:18:17,560
I just felt so relaxed
and refreshed today.

1650
01:18:17,711 --> 01:18:20,462
There was a moment
when we just looked up at the trees.

1651
01:18:20,649 --> 01:18:22,594
- The sound of the leaves rustling...
- The leaves...

1652
01:18:22,595 --> 01:18:24,309
There was a part where we lay down...

1653
01:18:24,310 --> 01:18:26,310
and watched the leaves swaying overhead.

1654
01:18:26,603 --> 01:18:29,999
They came back with hearts in their eyes.

1655
01:18:30,000 --> 01:18:31,460
Looking completely recharged.

1656
01:18:31,462 --> 01:18:34,439
Couples yoga is definitely worth trying.

1657
01:18:34,441 --> 01:18:35,812
I loved it.

1658
01:18:36,085 --> 01:18:38,847
I figured they must've had a good time.

1659
01:18:40,454 --> 01:18:43,350
Still, Dong Su keeps going on and on...

1660
01:18:43,351 --> 01:18:45,554
about how amazing it was.

1661
01:18:46,552 --> 01:18:48,027
Right in front of Yu Ra.

1662
01:18:48,052 --> 01:18:51,227
If a guy who slept next to me last night
acted like that, I'd be livid.

1663
01:18:57,788 --> 01:18:58,792
Something just arrived.

1664
01:18:58,794 --> 01:19:00,936
(A letter arrives.)

1665
01:19:02,638 --> 01:19:03,452
(Gasping)

1666
01:19:03,453 --> 01:19:05,859
"Your photo album has arrived."

1667
01:19:05,860 --> 01:19:07,976
"Please gather at the sofa in the garden."

1668
01:19:07,977 --> 01:19:08,845
Oh, gosh.

1669
01:19:10,329 --> 01:19:12,615
Are we finally revealing
who's related to whom?

1670
01:19:12,760 --> 01:19:14,884
- The garden?
- The sofa in the garden?

1671
01:19:15,478 --> 01:19:16,652
Oh, the one outside?

1672
01:19:22,237 --> 01:19:23,583
"Our photo album"?

1673
01:19:23,585 --> 01:19:24,893
(Everyone heads straight outside
to find the album.)

1674
01:19:30,806 --> 01:19:31,700
Oh, my.

1675
01:19:31,935 --> 01:19:33,338
What's that? Is something over there?

1676
01:19:33,339 --> 01:19:34,670
There's an album!

1677
01:19:34,672 --> 01:19:37,306
(What photos could be inside?)

1678
01:19:37,508 --> 01:19:38,977
Can I open it?

1679
01:19:38,978 --> 01:19:40,443
- Sure!
- Go for it.

1680
01:19:41,569 --> 01:19:43,245
Oh, I can't wait!

1681
01:19:46,782 --> 01:19:48,484
(Cute)

1682
01:19:49,351 --> 01:19:50,619
What?

1683
01:19:50,997 --> 01:19:52,321
- Who is that?
- Who could it be?

1684
01:19:52,979 --> 01:19:55,330
- I think I know who it is.
- I think I do too.

1685
01:19:55,583 --> 01:19:56,892
Jin Sung?

1686
01:19:57,195 --> 01:19:58,560
I think it's Jin Sung too.

1687
01:20:00,960 --> 01:20:03,840
I think this is Ji Hwan.

1688
01:20:04,953 --> 01:20:05,740
Sorry?

1689
01:20:08,887 --> 01:20:10,480
He looks adorable.

1690
01:20:11,720 --> 01:20:12,900
Dong Su?

1691
01:20:13,013 --> 01:20:14,847
My eyes are not that big.

1692
01:20:15,809 --> 01:20:18,643
What if he doesn't recognize himself?

1693
01:20:22,406 --> 01:20:24,946
That's obviously Jin Sung.

1694
01:20:24,993 --> 01:20:27,146
Even though we can't even see his face.

1695
01:20:27,187 --> 01:20:30,847
Who is it? Someone said they do fencing.

1696
01:20:34,104 --> 01:20:36,004
(Someone who does fencing)

1697
01:20:36,244 --> 01:20:37,378
Like that?

1698
01:20:38,138 --> 01:20:40,544
- He's even competed.
- He won a medal.

1699
01:20:41,381 --> 01:20:44,068
Does he do something related to fencing?

1700
01:20:45,140 --> 01:20:48,013
"If you're the person in these photos,
open this envelope."

1701
01:20:48,155 --> 01:20:49,215
It's an introduction.

1702
01:20:49,408 --> 01:20:52,861
"Please read the introduction
written by your sibling."

1703
01:20:56,734 --> 01:21:00,207
(They each have an introduction
written by their sibling.)

1704
01:21:01,247 --> 01:21:04,093
Goodness. It's so long.

1705
01:21:04,991 --> 01:21:05,938
Let me read it out loud.

1706
01:21:06,604 --> 01:21:08,938
"When Jin Sung sets his mind
to something,"

1707
01:21:08,965 --> 01:21:11,325
"he makes sure to see it through."

1708
01:21:11,418 --> 01:21:15,258
"Even when it comes to love,
if he genuinely likes someone,"

1709
01:21:15,285 --> 01:21:17,025
"he wants to do everything he can
to take care of them."

1710
01:21:17,364 --> 01:21:19,158
"He's sweet and thoughtful,"

1711
01:21:19,211 --> 01:21:20,771
"but when it comes
to important moments in life,"

1712
01:21:20,804 --> 01:21:23,497
"he's brave and makes bolder choices
than anyone else."

1713
01:21:23,698 --> 01:21:26,605
"Last month, he got accepted
for an internship at a major company."

1714
01:21:28,500 --> 01:21:31,120
"But he decided to turn down
that opportunity and come here..."

1715
01:21:31,221 --> 01:21:33,281
"because he wanted to meet someone..."

1716
01:21:33,354 --> 01:21:34,814
"he could fall in love with."

1717
01:21:35,208 --> 01:21:36,928
- Really?
- For real?

1718
01:21:36,968 --> 01:21:38,014
Seriously?

1719
01:21:38,041 --> 01:21:40,321
He gave up a huge opportunity
to be on My Sibling's Romance 2?

1720
01:21:40,541 --> 01:21:43,508
"Once he makes up his mind,
nothing can stop him."

1721
01:21:43,533 --> 01:21:45,768
"What do you think Jin Sung does
for a living?"

1722
01:21:46,886 --> 01:21:49,839
It says I should reveal my job.

1723
01:21:49,921 --> 01:21:52,228
- Your job too?
- Right away.

1724
01:21:52,388 --> 01:21:54,854
I got goosebumps.

1725
01:21:54,894 --> 01:21:57,141
My sister wrote
a nice introduction for me.

1726
01:21:57,166 --> 01:21:58,788
I'm touched.

1727
01:21:59,401 --> 01:22:01,067
What do you think he does?

1728
01:22:01,554 --> 01:22:02,781
A fencer?

1729
01:22:02,939 --> 01:22:04,806
- A fencing...
- An internship at a major company...

1730
01:22:05,040 --> 01:22:06,840
I feel like he's an athlete.

1731
01:22:07,187 --> 01:22:08,654
Judging by how his shirt fits,

1732
01:22:08,914 --> 01:22:10,647
he seemed to be in good shape.

1733
01:22:11,074 --> 01:22:13,940
If he got an internship
at a major company,

1734
01:22:14,014 --> 01:22:15,420
he does something mainly,

1735
01:22:15,454 --> 01:22:17,274
and fencing is just for fun.

1736
01:22:17,367 --> 01:22:19,027
And he's passionate about it.

1737
01:22:20,920 --> 01:22:26,320
I'm studying Materials Science
and Engineering at Korea University.

1738
01:22:27,113 --> 01:22:28,380
I'm a student.

1739
01:22:31,300 --> 01:22:35,313
I'm a senior studying Materials Science
and Engineering at Korea University.

1740
01:22:37,575 --> 01:22:41,548
I decided to pursue a career
in the semiconductor industry.

1741
01:22:42,362 --> 01:22:45,195
I'm fascinated
by how something so small...

1742
01:22:45,482 --> 01:22:48,241
could make a big difference in the world.

1743
01:22:48,282 --> 01:22:50,728
That's what made me want
to become a semiconductor engineer.

1744
01:22:52,228 --> 01:22:55,148
By using a self-aligned undercut
on the SiO2 layer...

1745
01:22:55,509 --> 01:22:58,341
We can see how efficiently it works.

1746
01:22:59,088 --> 01:23:01,968
After I graduate, I want to become
a semiconductor engineer,

1747
01:23:01,995 --> 01:23:06,308
working on improving yield
and finding the most efficient process.

1748
01:23:06,675 --> 01:23:11,201
(Jin Sung, college student)

1749
01:23:11,842 --> 01:23:13,169
Goodness.

1750
01:23:13,775 --> 01:23:16,428
I hope my sister can date him.

1751
01:23:16,474 --> 01:23:17,787
He studies semiconductors.

1752
01:23:17,812 --> 01:23:19,287
Semiconductors are a huge deal these days.

1753
01:23:19,312 --> 01:23:20,648
When the semiconductor industry
starts to slow down,

1754
01:23:20,673 --> 01:23:21,300
he could...

1755
01:23:21,362 --> 01:23:24,382
move on to other materials
or new technologies.

1756
01:23:24,462 --> 01:23:29,415
It seems like he stayed focused
and worked hard his way up.

1757
01:23:29,842 --> 01:23:32,901
I'd love to have a son like him one day.

1758
01:23:33,381 --> 01:23:34,868
He's the golden boy.

1759
01:23:38,725 --> 01:23:41,444
Let's move on to the next person.

1760
01:23:45,482 --> 01:23:47,348
- That's so cute.
- So bubbly.

1761
01:23:47,709 --> 01:23:49,479
Yu Ra.

1762
01:23:49,666 --> 01:23:50,893
Is that me?

1763
01:23:51,933 --> 01:23:53,273
Oh, dear.

1764
01:23:53,413 --> 01:23:55,693
That's obviously Yu Ra.

1765
01:23:55,718 --> 01:23:56,900
That's cute.

1766
01:23:57,066 --> 01:23:59,900
- Yu Ra.
- Yu Ra.

1767
01:24:00,266 --> 01:24:02,006
I guess that's me.

1768
01:24:02,045 --> 01:24:03,012
"I guess that's me."

1769
01:24:03,766 --> 01:24:06,160
- Does she dance?
- Does she dance?

1770
01:24:06,240 --> 01:24:08,600
- Really?
- Yu Ra, do you dance?

1771
01:24:08,733 --> 01:24:09,680
Is she in the arts?

1772
01:24:09,820 --> 01:24:11,493
She has an artsy vibe.

1773
01:24:15,216 --> 01:24:17,030
- Is that Min Seo?
- Isn't that Min Seo?

1774
01:24:17,530 --> 01:24:18,123
(Glancing)

1775
01:24:18,148 --> 01:24:20,110
Let's take another look.

1776
01:24:20,169 --> 01:24:21,229
That's me.

1777
01:24:22,123 --> 01:24:23,830
- Goodness!
- That's Min Seo!

1778
01:24:26,611 --> 01:24:29,351
(Min Seo as an adult)

1779
01:24:29,558 --> 01:24:30,865
Ballet?

1780
01:24:31,331 --> 01:24:33,071
- A dancer.
- She looks cool.

1781
01:24:33,218 --> 01:24:34,571
Isn't that just a theme?

1782
01:24:34,664 --> 01:24:36,611
Just a theme?

1783
01:24:37,418 --> 01:24:38,678
Let me read it.

1784
01:24:38,891 --> 01:24:41,537
"Min Seo is headstrong."

1785
01:24:43,529 --> 01:24:45,322
"She got into dancing one day,"

1786
01:24:45,350 --> 01:24:47,176
"and convinced our parents..."

1787
01:24:47,296 --> 01:24:49,236
"to let her go to an arts high school."

1788
01:24:49,409 --> 01:24:51,376
"She moved away from her family..."

1789
01:24:51,401 --> 01:24:54,123
"and kept pursuing what she wanted."

1790
01:24:54,196 --> 01:24:56,403
"I was so proud of her
and really admired her for it."

1791
01:24:56,443 --> 01:24:59,476
"When it comes to dating,
she takes her time opening up to someone."

1792
01:24:59,636 --> 01:25:01,950
"So, be patient
and keep knocking on that door."

1793
01:25:01,975 --> 01:25:03,582
"I hope she meets a tough guy..."

1794
01:25:03,636 --> 01:25:07,003
"who she can lean on
and feel completely comfortable around."

1795
01:25:08,923 --> 01:25:11,003
I want to say more about her.

1796
01:25:11,216 --> 01:25:13,970
I've never written an introduction
for her before.

1797
01:25:14,390 --> 01:25:16,236
We were always pretty close,

1798
01:25:16,881 --> 01:25:19,221
but not on an emotional level.

1799
01:25:19,470 --> 01:25:20,943
Now I feel like we're closer
on a deeper level.

1800
01:25:22,334 --> 01:25:25,961
"When it comes to dating,
she takes her time opening up to someone."

1801
01:25:26,174 --> 01:25:29,567
This describes me perfectly.

1802
01:25:29,721 --> 01:25:32,425
I loved the introduction. It was neat.

1803
01:25:33,565 --> 01:25:34,552
That's it.

1804
01:25:35,299 --> 01:25:36,265
A dancer.

1805
01:25:36,385 --> 01:25:37,965
I think she's a dancer.

1806
01:25:38,045 --> 01:25:41,438
She looked really good with her hair up,
so I think she's a dancer.

1807
01:25:41,652 --> 01:25:44,425
She said she liked running,

1808
01:25:44,472 --> 01:25:46,719
so I think she does Pilates or yoga.

1809
01:25:47,412 --> 01:25:48,545
My job is...

1810
01:25:48,665 --> 01:25:50,745
I pursued dance for a while,

1811
01:25:50,840 --> 01:25:52,805
but now I'm a barre instructor.

1812
01:25:53,167 --> 01:25:55,338
- Barre?
- Did you expect that?

1813
01:25:55,411 --> 01:25:57,185
I still go to barre classes!

1814
01:25:57,225 --> 01:25:59,798
- I'm not that good, though.
- It's fascinating.

1815
01:26:05,572 --> 01:26:07,412
I'm a barre instructor.

1816
01:26:17,154 --> 01:26:19,080
Push your hips back.

1817
01:26:19,134 --> 01:26:21,534
Lift it a little higher
towards the ceiling.

1818
01:26:22,585 --> 01:26:25,398
I started studying contemporary dance
in middle school...

1819
01:26:25,845 --> 01:26:28,145
and went to an arts high school.

1820
01:26:41,229 --> 01:26:45,540
I majored in dance at Dankook University
and worked as a dance instructor.

1821
01:26:45,776 --> 01:26:48,242
Then I fell in love with barre...

1822
01:26:48,296 --> 01:26:50,749
and decided to take on a new challenge.

1823
01:26:54,181 --> 01:26:57,660
(Min Seo, barre instructor)

1824
01:26:57,866 --> 01:26:59,434
Could you help me do the splits?

1825
01:27:02,188 --> 01:27:03,348
I'm serious.

1826
01:27:03,997 --> 01:27:06,470
That's why she was good at climbing.

1827
01:27:07,283 --> 01:27:08,983
(Their climbing date today)

1828
01:27:10,823 --> 01:27:12,630
We're in similar fields.

1829
01:27:12,797 --> 01:27:15,970
I was fascinated and also surprised.

1830
01:27:17,717 --> 01:27:20,102
That's really cool. A barre instructor.

1831
01:27:20,157 --> 01:27:21,150
Yes, it is.

1832
01:27:23,177 --> 01:27:24,383
Who could that be?

1833
01:27:24,604 --> 01:27:26,950
Wait. That's super cute.

1834
01:27:26,990 --> 01:27:28,204
That's adorable.

1835
01:27:28,897 --> 01:27:30,623
Based on his cheeks...

1836
01:27:30,684 --> 01:27:32,057
That's Ji Hwan for sure.

1837
01:27:32,197 --> 01:27:34,257
His eyes look like Ji Hwan's.

1838
01:27:34,424 --> 01:27:35,683
In Joong.

1839
01:27:35,708 --> 01:27:37,023
- Me?
- In Joong?

1840
01:27:37,177 --> 01:27:39,137
- His reaction!
- He looks like In Joong?

1841
01:27:39,197 --> 01:27:40,390
He's thrown off.

1842
01:27:41,534 --> 01:27:42,701
He's really cute.

1843
01:27:42,914 --> 01:27:44,683
- That's cute.
- It says Ji Hwan all over his face.

1844
01:27:44,708 --> 01:27:46,981
- Ji Hwan.
- He has the same eyes.

1845
01:27:47,386 --> 01:27:48,493
- In Joong?
- He looks like In Joong.

1846
01:27:49,260 --> 01:27:51,540
- Is that In Joong?
- In Joong!

1847
01:27:51,660 --> 01:27:53,166
This is insane.

1848
01:27:53,233 --> 01:27:55,239
All the babies look like Jin Sung to me.

1849
01:27:56,359 --> 01:27:59,157
- Jin Sung, didn't you have your turn?
- Jin Sung, I thought you were done.

1850
01:27:59,158 --> 01:28:00,246
That's me, actually.

1851
01:28:00,271 --> 01:28:02,573
- All the babies look like Jin Sung.
- Seriously.

1852
01:28:04,311 --> 01:28:06,250
That's a very straightforward photo.

1853
01:28:07,131 --> 01:28:08,771
That was In Joong.

1854
01:28:08,838 --> 01:28:10,818
- That's In Joong for sure.
- In Joong.

1855
01:28:10,844 --> 01:28:13,217
Why are you flipping in a rush?

1856
01:28:13,244 --> 01:28:14,131
Why are you in a rush?

1857
01:28:14,184 --> 01:28:15,231
I was taken aback.

1858
01:28:15,256 --> 01:28:17,317
I didn't expect to see that picture.

1859
01:28:18,218 --> 01:28:20,924
Everyone else's baby photos were
so cute and adorable,

1860
01:28:21,184 --> 01:28:24,331
and I was the only one
with a yearbook photo.

1861
01:28:25,944 --> 01:28:27,418
What is that?

1862
01:28:27,464 --> 01:28:28,951
The honor guard?

1863
01:28:29,191 --> 01:28:30,344
A military guy?

1864
01:28:30,858 --> 01:28:32,051
It's an honor guard.

1865
01:28:32,144 --> 01:28:34,491
The honor guard is an event team
that supports ceremonies.

1866
01:28:36,389 --> 01:28:37,762
He's in a hurry.

1867
01:28:37,787 --> 01:28:38,442
In there.

1868
01:28:38,467 --> 01:28:39,954
It's in the envelope.

1869
01:28:40,696 --> 01:28:41,975
(He almost ripped his introduction off.)

1870
01:28:42,129 --> 01:28:43,402
My yearbook photo caught me off guard.

1871
01:28:46,512 --> 01:28:47,978
I'm already sad.

1872
01:28:48,785 --> 01:28:51,791
"He's basically a human golden retriever."

1873
01:28:51,944 --> 01:28:53,891
"He moved schools a lot
when he was in elementary school."

1874
01:28:53,972 --> 01:28:56,552
"It must have been pretty confusing
for him at such a young age."

1875
01:28:56,585 --> 01:29:00,751
"He said he enjoyed getting attention
whenever he started at a new school."

1876
01:29:00,776 --> 01:29:02,305
"He was such a positive kid."

1877
01:29:02,358 --> 01:29:04,758
"He's super affectionate
when he's in love."

1878
01:29:04,858 --> 01:29:08,158
"When he's in a relationship, he spends
hours on the phone with his girlfriend."

1879
01:29:08,252 --> 01:29:10,771
"But this sweet guy showed..."

1880
01:29:10,825 --> 01:29:13,025
"a completely different side of himself
in the military."

1881
01:29:13,418 --> 01:29:17,878
"He became part of the honor guard
and protected the president..."

1882
01:29:17,903 --> 01:29:20,792
"and important national figures
right by their side."

1883
01:29:22,205 --> 01:29:23,372
Are you in the military?

1884
01:29:23,985 --> 01:29:24,918
A military man?

1885
01:29:25,078 --> 01:29:28,178
- That makes it harder to guess his job.
- I know.

1886
01:29:28,285 --> 01:29:30,345
I feel like his job is something
completely different.

1887
01:29:32,952 --> 01:29:34,632
I'm a college student.

1888
01:29:36,698 --> 01:29:38,192
I'm taking some time off from school.

1889
01:29:38,258 --> 01:29:40,832
I'm in charge of running...

1890
01:29:40,872 --> 01:29:43,252
a clothing brand showroom in Hannam-dong.

1891
01:29:44,885 --> 01:29:46,705
It's already tax-free.

1892
01:29:46,738 --> 01:29:48,471
The price will change.

1893
01:29:51,112 --> 01:29:52,611
I do more than just sales.

1894
01:29:52,645 --> 01:29:55,792
I help customers find styles
that suit them best.

1895
01:29:57,118 --> 01:30:01,191
(In Joong, college student
and clothing store employee)

1896
01:30:02,330 --> 01:30:04,198
I've walked past there so many times,

1897
01:30:04,733 --> 01:30:05,599
but I've never seen him.

1898
01:30:06,301 --> 01:30:07,701
What a shame.

1899
01:30:07,803 --> 01:30:09,337
No wonder that place was always packed.

1900
01:30:09,338 --> 01:30:12,406
Now I get it.
My shirt was wrinkled.

1901
01:30:12,541 --> 01:30:14,075
He showed us how to smooth them out.

1902
01:30:14,709 --> 01:30:16,243
(This morning)

1903
01:30:16,846 --> 01:30:18,545
You can get the wrinkles out
a little by doing this.

1904
01:30:18,713 --> 01:30:20,380
(An expert shared his technique.)

1905
01:30:22,517 --> 01:30:26,687
I was a little concerned too.

1906
01:30:26,688 --> 01:30:30,357
I got the impression
he was younger than me.

1907
01:30:30,625 --> 01:30:32,359
I thought he might be younger,

1908
01:30:33,461 --> 01:30:36,730
and I'd mostly dated people
in similar lines of work.

1909
01:30:36,731 --> 01:30:40,667
I'd never dated anyone
in his profession before, so...

1910
01:30:40,969 --> 01:30:44,305
I found that pretty interesting.

1911
01:30:44,940 --> 01:30:46,707
Let me turn the page.

1912
01:30:46,708 --> 01:30:49,043
(Chubby)

1913
01:30:50,479 --> 01:30:52,446
- I think she's Ye In.
- Ye In.

1914
01:30:52,747 --> 01:30:53,647
Who is it?

1915
01:30:56,284 --> 01:30:57,084
Who could it be?

1916
01:30:58,153 --> 01:30:59,921
Her cheeks are so chubby!

1917
01:30:59,922 --> 01:31:00,988
- I know.
- Right.

1918
01:31:02,458 --> 01:31:03,757
She's like a little dumpling.

1919
01:31:05,260 --> 01:31:06,193
She's cute.

1920
01:31:06,828 --> 01:31:10,130
- She suddenly grew up so much!
- She's so pretty.

1921
01:31:10,265 --> 01:31:11,165
That's me.

1922
01:31:12,934 --> 01:31:16,003
I suddenly lost a lot of weight
as I grew up.

1923
01:31:17,672 --> 01:31:19,806
She looks like a cover model!

1924
01:31:20,242 --> 01:31:21,075
She looks like an idol.

1925
01:31:21,409 --> 01:31:22,642
She's so pretty.

1926
01:31:24,613 --> 01:31:25,513
She looked so pretty.

1927
01:31:26,681 --> 01:31:28,882
He's completely smitten.

1928
01:31:28,883 --> 01:31:30,317
He's fallen for her all over again.

1929
01:31:30,318 --> 01:31:32,319
He might even take that photo home.

1930
01:31:33,021 --> 01:31:34,355
She does look amazing in that photo.

1931
01:31:34,656 --> 01:31:36,523
When Ye In was little,
she had such chubby cheeks.

1932
01:31:36,825 --> 01:31:38,058
Then, in the next photo, she looked so...

1933
01:31:38,260 --> 01:31:39,827
How should I put it?

1934
01:31:39,828 --> 01:31:40,862
I don't know. She was just so pretty.

1935
01:31:40,863 --> 01:31:42,463
I was amazed when I saw it.

1936
01:31:43,031 --> 01:31:47,334
She had a photo where she looked
really pretty in her school uniform.

1937
01:31:47,535 --> 01:31:50,137
I thought she might have been
a school uniform model.

1938
01:31:50,171 --> 01:31:52,939
I even wondered
if she was an idol trainee.

1939
01:31:54,342 --> 01:31:55,275
It's long.

1940
01:31:55,276 --> 01:31:57,544
(What did her sibling write
about her as he watched her grow up?)

1941
01:31:57,846 --> 01:32:01,048
"Ye In has always been full of talent."

1942
01:32:01,149 --> 01:32:05,052
"She loved Baek Ye Rin's songs
and wanted to sing them well,"

1943
01:32:05,153 --> 01:32:07,154
"so she signed up for vocal lessons."

1944
01:32:07,155 --> 01:32:10,257
"Then she secretly went to an audition
without telling the family."

1945
01:32:11,427 --> 01:32:13,928
"She's the kind of person who has
to try anything she gets interested in,"

1946
01:32:13,929 --> 01:32:15,663
"and she's just the same
when it comes to dating."

1947
01:32:15,897 --> 01:32:17,631
"She falls for people quickly,"

1948
01:32:17,632 --> 01:32:20,601
"and once she's sure she likes someone,"

1949
01:32:20,735 --> 01:32:23,837
"she has the courage
to go straight after him."

1950
01:32:23,838 --> 01:32:25,672
"I think that's one of her charms."

1951
01:32:26,041 --> 01:32:27,609
"She's always so sharp and put-together,"

1952
01:32:27,633 --> 01:32:29,633
"but there's one thing
that makes her let her guard down."

1953
01:32:30,045 --> 01:32:32,446
"It's delicious food."

1954
01:32:32,647 --> 01:32:36,383
"When she goes to a restaurant she loves,
she even carries digestive medicine..."

1955
01:32:36,518 --> 01:32:38,686
"because she wants to eat more."

1956
01:32:39,321 --> 01:32:41,023
"She loves Dubai chewy cookies so much..."

1957
01:32:41,024 --> 01:32:42,823
"that she buys them up
at different shops..."

1958
01:32:42,824 --> 01:32:45,059
"and taste-tests them like
she's doing research."

1959
01:32:45,560 --> 01:32:47,995
"What kind of work
do you think Ye In does?"

1960
01:32:48,663 --> 01:32:49,863
A Dubai chewy cookie researcher?

1961
01:32:53,234 --> 01:32:54,301
Could she be a pastry chef?

1962
01:32:54,302 --> 01:32:56,269
- That could be it.
- Could it be something related to that?

1963
01:32:56,270 --> 01:32:58,104
She said she loves desserts.

1964
01:32:58,306 --> 01:32:59,439
Maybe a singer-songwriter?

1965
01:32:59,841 --> 01:33:01,742
I also wondered
if she might be a flight attendant.

1966
01:33:01,743 --> 01:33:03,410
(Flight attendant?)

1967
01:33:03,411 --> 01:33:04,478
That idea just came to me.

1968
01:33:04,479 --> 01:33:05,847
Ye In has a nice voice too.

1969
01:33:05,848 --> 01:33:08,081
Maybe singing has given her
good vocal technique.

1970
01:33:08,350 --> 01:33:09,250
Maybe.

1971
01:33:09,517 --> 01:33:10,550
Maybe she's a florist.

1972
01:33:10,785 --> 01:33:11,852
Flowers really suit her.

1973
01:33:11,853 --> 01:33:14,488
I think she'd be a calm office worker.

1974
01:33:14,489 --> 01:33:16,757
She's articulate, so maybe a marketer.

1975
01:33:17,058 --> 01:33:18,291
I'm getting really nervous.

1976
01:33:19,761 --> 01:33:20,694
I'm...

1977
01:33:21,696 --> 01:33:22,896
a Korean medicine doctor.

1978
01:33:25,033 --> 01:33:26,333
A Korean medicine doctor?

1979
01:33:27,535 --> 01:33:29,636
- A Korean medicine doctor?
- A Dubai chewy cookie doctor?

1980
01:33:31,306 --> 01:33:33,174
- She had so many Dubai chewy cookies!
- It just doesn't seem to match.

1981
01:33:33,175 --> 01:33:36,143
Dubai cookies taste like herbal medicine
if they aren't made right.

1982
01:33:36,344 --> 01:33:37,911
- Seriously.
- That's true.

1983
01:33:37,912 --> 01:33:39,880
Now I see
why she got so into Dubai chewy cookies.

1984
01:33:39,881 --> 01:33:41,782
Exactly. They can taste bitter
if they're not made right.

1985
01:33:41,783 --> 01:33:43,317
- A Korean medicine doctor?
- That's amazing!

1986
01:33:44,185 --> 01:33:45,385
I'm a Korean medicine doctor.

1987
01:33:46,087 --> 01:33:47,154
- Wow.
- Sorry?

1988
01:33:47,555 --> 01:33:48,388
Wait...

1989
01:33:52,660 --> 01:33:54,828
I studied for about six years,

1990
01:33:55,297 --> 01:33:56,997
graduated from a college
of Korean medicine,

1991
01:33:56,998 --> 01:33:59,366
and now work as a Korean medicine doctor.

1992
01:33:59,701 --> 01:34:01,301
(Darae Korean Medicine)

1993
01:34:06,107 --> 01:34:07,707
I'm a Korean medicine doctor.

1994
01:34:08,510 --> 01:34:12,446
I work at a Korean medicine hospital
that specializes...

1995
01:34:12,447 --> 01:34:14,582
in traditional Korean medical treatments
and herbal prescriptions.

1996
01:34:14,583 --> 01:34:17,418
It's related to trigger points.

1997
01:34:17,419 --> 01:34:19,720
I'm going to do pharmacopuncture
and acupuncture.

1998
01:34:20,622 --> 01:34:23,857
I assess my patients' overall health...

1999
01:34:23,858 --> 01:34:27,027
and provide treatments
suited to their needs.

2000
01:34:31,766 --> 01:34:35,001
Rather than just treating their symptoms,

2001
01:34:35,002 --> 01:34:39,439
I try to identify and address
the underlying causes as well.

2002
01:34:41,408 --> 01:34:45,345
I also provide
skin-related treatments and procedures.

2003
01:34:46,381 --> 01:34:49,950
(Ye In, Korean medicine doctor)

2004
01:34:49,951 --> 01:34:51,085
Really?

2005
01:34:51,253 --> 01:34:52,452
- A Korean medicine doctor!
- That's impressive.

2006
01:34:52,453 --> 01:34:53,853
No one guessed it right.

2007
01:34:57,659 --> 01:34:58,692
(Impressed)

2008
01:35:01,863 --> 01:35:03,564
Ye In said
she was a Korean medicine doctor.

2009
01:35:03,798 --> 01:35:04,931
It's really impressive.

2010
01:35:05,333 --> 01:35:06,700
I never would've expected that.

2011
01:35:08,470 --> 01:35:10,471
Honestly, I'm quite worried.

2012
01:35:10,472 --> 01:35:11,941
It doesn't bother me,

2013
01:35:11,942 --> 01:35:15,342
but I wondered if she might be hesitant
about dating a college student...

2014
01:35:15,677 --> 01:35:17,077
when she's already working.

2015
01:35:17,612 --> 01:35:20,046
And when I heard
she's a Korean medicine doctor,

2016
01:35:20,482 --> 01:35:23,050
I did feel a little out of my league.

2017
01:35:24,385 --> 01:35:25,885
So I'm a bit worried,

2018
01:35:26,988 --> 01:35:28,221
but I'm not sure.

2019
01:35:29,725 --> 01:35:31,892
I'll just have to do my best to show her
what I've got.

2020
01:35:32,094 --> 01:35:34,695
I wonder what I could possibly offer.

2021
01:35:35,063 --> 01:35:37,297
I'm still at a stage
where I need to prepare for my future,

2022
01:35:37,298 --> 01:35:41,702
and I haven't achieved much yet.

2023
01:35:41,970 --> 01:35:43,704
I was a little envious,

2024
01:35:43,705 --> 01:35:47,641
but I also felt
there was a bit of a gap between us.

2025
01:35:47,742 --> 01:35:49,743
I know that feeling.

2026
01:35:50,411 --> 01:35:54,047
It's this strange sense
that you're falling behind.

2027
01:35:54,048 --> 01:35:55,181
- Does it make you feel intimidated?
- No.

2028
01:35:55,617 --> 01:35:57,151
If anything, it motivates me.

2029
01:35:57,452 --> 01:36:00,555
- It's one of the biggest reasons...
- Totally.

2030
01:36:00,556 --> 01:36:03,924
I tell myself I need to succeed.

2031
01:36:04,025 --> 01:36:05,559
Even when men and women are
around the same age,

2032
01:36:05,560 --> 01:36:07,795
men tend to fall a little behind
at that stage.

2033
01:36:07,796 --> 01:36:08,929
They have to serve in the military.

2034
01:36:09,130 --> 01:36:10,931
Then there must be a bit of an age gap
between her and In Joong.

2035
01:36:10,932 --> 01:36:12,532
- I think so.
- Right.

2036
01:36:12,901 --> 01:36:15,202
(Who's next?)

2037
01:36:16,137 --> 01:36:17,070
Who's this baby?

2038
01:36:18,173 --> 01:36:19,874
He kind of looks like Dong Su.

2039
01:36:20,375 --> 01:36:21,375
What a cute little face!

2040
01:36:21,976 --> 01:36:23,576
- Dong Su?
- Could it be Dong Su?

2041
01:36:24,546 --> 01:36:25,479
Me?

2042
01:36:27,549 --> 01:36:28,949
I can't believe it.
He looks like Jin Sung again!

2043
01:36:30,385 --> 01:36:31,752
- Me again?
- I must be terrible at guessing.

2044
01:36:32,353 --> 01:36:33,987
Every baby looks like Jin Sung to me.

2045
01:36:35,156 --> 01:36:36,056
Shall we turn one more page?

2046
01:36:37,258 --> 01:36:38,824
- It's Dong Su.
- Dong Su.

2047
01:36:39,360 --> 01:36:40,460
His eyes haven't changed at all.

2048
01:36:40,762 --> 01:36:41,929
That's obviously me.

2049
01:36:43,565 --> 01:36:45,099
This was taken at a kimjang event
at kindergarten.

2050
01:36:45,934 --> 01:36:46,901
Kimjang...

2051
01:36:50,405 --> 01:36:51,405
What's this?

2052
01:36:53,041 --> 01:36:54,675
(Here comes Dong Su!)

2053
01:36:54,676 --> 01:36:55,743
He's so cute.

2054
01:36:56,411 --> 01:36:58,612
Everyone else brought such nice pictures.

2055
01:36:59,214 --> 01:37:01,181
I've had LASIK now.

2056
01:37:01,382 --> 01:37:03,483
But before that, my eyesight was so bad
that I wore thick glasses.

2057
01:37:03,918 --> 01:37:04,885
They made my eyes look really small.

2058
01:37:05,853 --> 01:37:08,488
Is that even the same person?

2059
01:37:09,057 --> 01:37:10,624
It practically has Dong Su's name
written all over it.

2060
01:37:11,092 --> 01:37:12,258
That's me.

2061
01:37:12,259 --> 01:37:13,093
Oh, I see.

2062
01:37:14,262 --> 01:37:15,896
He was student vice president?

2063
01:37:19,099 --> 01:37:20,277
(Occupation: the Samsung chairman's son
and president of Samsung)

2064
01:37:20,301 --> 01:37:22,035
"Samsung Group Chairman's son?"

2065
01:37:22,570 --> 01:37:24,404
- The occupation is...
- Was that your dream job?

2066
01:37:24,405 --> 01:37:25,338
(Quite an impressive career)

2067
01:37:28,209 --> 01:37:29,142
Oh, my gosh.

2068
01:37:29,143 --> 01:37:31,444
(A reveal of Dong Su's pre-LASIK photos)

2069
01:37:31,445 --> 01:37:36,183
I think every student should
look like this.

2070
01:37:36,184 --> 01:37:37,651
- Exactly.
- I'm just building up...

2071
01:37:37,652 --> 01:37:38,952
to defend myself.

2072
01:37:38,953 --> 01:37:40,620
- You are?
- I was...

2073
01:37:40,955 --> 01:37:42,455
He seems like he was a model student.

2074
01:37:47,595 --> 01:37:48,795
Is this really the same person?

2075
01:37:51,065 --> 01:37:52,199
Is this really the same person?

2076
01:37:52,200 --> 01:37:53,800
He looks like
a completely different person.

2077
01:37:55,403 --> 01:37:57,537
I don't have those muscles anymore.

2078
01:37:58,706 --> 01:37:59,906
He looks amazing.

2079
01:38:00,408 --> 01:38:03,210
That was after I lost 35 kg.

2080
01:38:05,380 --> 01:38:07,047
Maybe he's in the fitness industry.

2081
01:38:07,749 --> 01:38:08,682
That's incredible.

2082
01:38:09,350 --> 01:38:10,450
Let me read it.

2083
01:38:13,454 --> 01:38:16,189
"Dong Su has a great personality."

2084
01:38:16,190 --> 01:38:17,791
"He's so polite..."

2085
01:38:18,059 --> 01:38:20,093
"that if he sees an older person
he knows while driving,"

2086
01:38:20,094 --> 01:38:22,396
"he'll pull over, get out and greet them."

2087
01:38:23,631 --> 01:38:26,333
"He gets up at five every morning
and starts his day."

2088
01:38:26,334 --> 01:38:29,269
"After work, he always goes running
or works out at the gym."

2089
01:38:29,270 --> 01:38:32,105
"He's very dedicated to staying in shape."

2090
01:38:32,940 --> 01:38:35,275
"I think he takes
even better care of himself than I do."

2091
01:38:36,144 --> 01:38:39,613
"He's also so thoughtful
that he checks in on me every day."

2092
01:38:39,982 --> 01:38:43,216
"But there's one thing that makes him
stop keeping in touch."

2093
01:38:43,384 --> 01:38:45,552
"It's when he gets a girlfriend."

2094
01:38:45,954 --> 01:38:49,155
"Once he's in love, his girlfriend becomes
his number one priority."

2095
01:38:49,457 --> 01:38:51,624
"I'm sure that
if he falls for someone here,"

2096
01:38:51,625 --> 01:38:55,229
"he'll go all in without holding back."

2097
01:38:55,730 --> 01:38:57,964
"Dong Su is friendly, loyal,"

2098
01:38:57,965 --> 01:38:59,399
"and serious about love."

2099
01:38:59,634 --> 01:39:01,635
"What do you think Dong Su does
for a living?"

2100
01:39:03,104 --> 01:39:04,071
- So, what do you think my job is?
- I have no idea.

2101
01:39:04,072 --> 01:39:06,306
Since he wrote "Samsung"
when he was young,

2102
01:39:07,275 --> 01:39:09,142
I think he works for a big company.

2103
01:39:09,143 --> 01:39:10,344
A fit guy at a major corporation.

2104
01:39:11,012 --> 01:39:12,012
A fit office worker?

2105
01:39:12,280 --> 01:39:13,380
- Right.
- Okay.

2106
01:39:13,381 --> 01:39:15,549
This might be too obvious,
but maybe a personal trainer?

2107
01:39:15,550 --> 01:39:16,850
I thought so too.

2108
01:39:16,984 --> 01:39:18,919
I bet his job is
something completely unexpected.

2109
01:39:19,120 --> 01:39:20,821
Maybe a web designer?

2110
01:39:20,822 --> 01:39:22,422
You seem like you'd be good in IT.

2111
01:39:22,890 --> 01:39:24,724
I get an engineering vibe from him.

2112
01:39:26,194 --> 01:39:27,160
I...

2113
01:39:28,054 --> 01:39:31,690
operate excavators and dump trucks.

2114
01:39:32,767 --> 01:39:33,734
And now,

2115
01:39:34,502 --> 01:39:35,569
I also...

2116
01:39:36,070 --> 01:39:39,606
work in agriculture and raise cattle.

2117
01:39:40,975 --> 01:39:43,476
I'm carrying on the family business.

2118
01:39:47,315 --> 01:39:48,882
I'm a heavy equipment operator.

2119
01:39:52,954 --> 01:39:54,587
I got my license...

2120
01:39:54,588 --> 01:39:57,658
and work as an excavator operator.

2121
01:39:57,659 --> 01:39:59,026
I also run my own business.

2122
01:40:04,866 --> 01:40:08,631
I mostly dig and clear land
in the early stages of construction.

2123
01:40:08,798 --> 01:40:12,940
I work all kinds of sites,
from civil engineering to landscaping.

2124
01:40:28,289 --> 01:40:31,092
On top of my main job,
I help my parents with their cattle farm.

2125
01:40:31,174 --> 01:40:33,995
We run a farm with 100 head of cattle.

2126
01:40:43,278 --> 01:40:47,485
(Dong Su, heavy equipment operator)

2127
01:40:47,984 --> 01:40:50,545
See? I knew it.
You can't do that as a hobby.

2128
01:40:50,545 --> 01:40:51,546
No, you can't.

2129
01:40:51,585 --> 01:40:52,980
First of all, it's long-distance.

2130
01:40:53,043 --> 01:40:54,315
- Yes.
- That's right.

2131
01:40:54,443 --> 01:40:56,584
- Then, long distance is a given.
- Yes.

2132
01:40:56,609 --> 01:40:57,618
Wow, that's so cool.

2133
01:40:58,549 --> 01:41:00,821
That's so cool. How many do you have?

2134
01:41:01,183 --> 01:41:01,956
Cows?

2135
01:41:02,329 --> 01:41:04,025
- Cows.
- We've got 100 right now.

2136
01:41:05,192 --> 01:41:07,128
- Wow, that's so cool.
- Whoa.

2137
01:41:07,306 --> 01:41:08,129
Wow.

2138
01:41:08,752 --> 01:41:10,752
The most surprising job? Dong Su.

2139
01:41:11,465 --> 01:41:13,868
Number one. Most shocked.

2140
01:41:14,435 --> 01:41:16,337
He was so different from what I pictured.

2141
01:41:17,371 --> 01:41:20,841
I'd never met anyone in
that line of work up close.

2142
01:41:21,019 --> 01:41:23,878
It was surprising and really cool.

2143
01:41:24,278 --> 01:41:25,813
But now that I've heard it,

2144
01:41:25,852 --> 01:41:29,572
he kind of suits a big excavator.

2145
01:41:29,784 --> 01:41:31,419
If he were sitting in one,

2146
01:41:31,686 --> 01:41:34,755
he's got a face you'd totally trust.

2147
01:41:35,245 --> 01:41:36,324
A hundred cows?

2148
01:41:37,252 --> 01:41:38,559
Wait, 100 head?
Is that how you count them?

2149
01:41:43,431 --> 01:41:44,432
I'll turn the page.

2150
01:41:47,090 --> 01:41:48,330
(A newborn appears.)

2151
01:41:48,356 --> 01:41:50,071
Who's that?

2152
01:41:50,096 --> 01:41:51,305
Ji Hwan.

2153
01:41:51,456 --> 01:41:54,141
You can tell it's me from this?

2154
01:41:54,676 --> 01:41:55,943
That baby has a lot of hair.

2155
01:41:56,616 --> 01:41:57,761
How can we...

2156
01:41:57,788 --> 01:41:59,213
I don't think it's me.

2157
01:42:01,561 --> 01:42:03,628
It's a girl. Is she upset?

2158
01:42:03,630 --> 01:42:05,541
(Clue 2: A pouty face)

2159
01:42:06,376 --> 01:42:08,756
- Jwa Hyeon? It's Jwa Hyeon.
- I can see her personality.

2160
01:42:09,210 --> 01:42:10,828
- Whoa, Jwa Hyeon.
- It's so her.

2161
01:42:10,830 --> 01:42:12,760
Your eyes look alike when you smile.

2162
01:42:14,070 --> 01:42:15,910
(One person goes quiet.)

2163
01:42:16,256 --> 01:42:17,732
Is that really Jwa Hyeon?

2164
01:42:18,616 --> 01:42:20,443
(Putting on a poker face)

2165
01:42:21,185 --> 01:42:23,292
- Wow.
- It is her.

2166
01:42:23,292 --> 01:42:24,405
Oh, wow.

2167
01:42:24,525 --> 01:42:25,706
It's Jwa Hyeon.

2168
01:42:25,805 --> 01:42:27,041
Yep, that's me.

2169
01:42:27,218 --> 01:42:29,405
But I edited this one really hard.

2170
01:42:29,578 --> 01:42:30,745
So it's not me.

2171
01:42:30,778 --> 01:42:33,614
- You look exactly the same.
- Same as now.

2172
01:42:33,872 --> 01:42:34,982
Yeah, you look the same.

2173
01:42:36,678 --> 01:42:37,532
Broadcasting?

2174
01:42:37,732 --> 01:42:38,853
Is that a soundproof booth?

2175
01:42:39,452 --> 01:42:41,452
I think she's in a booth.

2176
01:42:42,156 --> 01:42:43,090
A producer?

2177
01:42:43,430 --> 01:42:45,359
Something with sound?

2178
01:42:45,404 --> 01:42:46,494
Something in broadcasting?

2179
01:42:46,790 --> 01:42:47,928
I have no clue.

2180
01:42:49,124 --> 01:42:50,384
(Sibling intro letter)

2181
01:42:50,484 --> 01:42:52,222
I'm definitely going to cry.

2182
01:42:52,224 --> 01:42:53,234
Heads up.

2183
01:42:56,050 --> 01:42:58,105
Wow, it's long. No way.

2184
01:43:05,259 --> 01:43:08,516
Jwa Hyeon gives everything
when she loves someone.

2185
01:43:09,550 --> 01:43:12,653
I've never seen her hold back her heart
when she likes someone.

2186
01:43:13,120 --> 01:43:15,723
Once, after a breakup,

2187
01:43:15,799 --> 01:43:17,799
she cried her eyes out for a whole week.

2188
01:43:17,925 --> 01:43:19,093
Watching her...

2189
01:43:19,126 --> 01:43:21,662
my heart ached, and I was really worried.

2190
01:43:22,163 --> 01:43:23,297
I hope she meets someone...

2191
01:43:23,533 --> 01:43:26,200
who doesn't take her love for granted.

2192
01:43:26,546 --> 01:43:29,059
Someone who can share feelings
at the same warmth.

2193
01:43:29,059 --> 01:43:31,105
Someone warm.

2194
01:43:31,605 --> 01:43:33,645
With someone like that, I think...

2195
01:43:33,665 --> 01:43:36,143
she could live happily ever after.

2196
01:43:37,445 --> 01:43:41,048
Ji Hwan talks kind of slowly and briefly,

2197
01:43:41,099 --> 01:43:43,317
so he's never had the chance
to tell me this much.

2198
01:43:43,651 --> 01:43:46,187
I was watching him
from the corner of my eye.

2199
01:43:46,921 --> 01:43:49,090
He was bouncing his feet. So cute.

2200
01:43:51,799 --> 01:43:54,028
Like he was waiting for my reaction.

2201
01:43:54,517 --> 01:43:56,063
He was like a baby.

2202
01:43:57,565 --> 01:44:00,034
He feels all that.

2203
01:44:00,034 --> 01:44:01,990
But he doesn't say it, so it doesn't show.

2204
01:44:01,992 --> 01:44:03,684
Right.

2205
01:44:03,726 --> 01:44:08,042
Or maybe it takes him a while
to feel that way.

2206
01:44:09,376 --> 01:44:12,179
She studied art all through school.

2207
01:44:12,190 --> 01:44:14,248
But now she does something
totally different.

2208
01:44:14,876 --> 01:44:15,983
As an adult,

2209
01:44:15,983 --> 01:44:19,220
switching to a whole new path
couldn't have been easy.

2210
01:44:19,430 --> 01:44:21,430
But she made it through
a 1,000-to-1 audition.

2211
01:44:21,432 --> 01:44:23,758
Seeing her crush it at her job now,

2212
01:44:23,896 --> 01:44:26,761
I think she's amazing,
even if she's my sister.

2213
01:44:27,043 --> 01:44:28,829
An audition?

2214
01:44:29,864 --> 01:44:31,864
What do you think Jwa Hyeon does?

2215
01:44:32,663 --> 01:44:33,768
- Audition?
- An actress?

2216
01:44:34,101 --> 01:44:35,469
- Huh?
- A thousand to one audition?

2217
01:44:35,617 --> 01:44:36,670
A thousand to one?

2218
01:44:36,971 --> 01:44:38,339
An announcer? Broadcasting?

2219
01:44:38,606 --> 01:44:39,573
An audition?

2220
01:44:39,721 --> 01:44:41,201
(No clue)

2221
01:44:41,201 --> 01:44:42,143
A thousand to one?

2222
01:44:44,655 --> 01:44:45,479
I'm...

2223
01:44:46,814 --> 01:44:48,249
an online lecture instructor.

2224
01:44:57,525 --> 01:44:59,093
I'm an English teacher.

2225
01:45:00,394 --> 01:45:02,663
I teach English to middle schoolers...

2226
01:45:02,663 --> 01:45:05,566
on the online education
platform Visang Edu.

2227
01:45:07,234 --> 01:45:09,570
You need to go through this carefully...

2228
01:45:09,570 --> 01:45:12,355
so you don't just memorize it.

2229
01:45:12,355 --> 01:45:16,177
I also teach in-person classes
in Daechi-dong.

2230
01:45:17,077 --> 01:45:19,046
You need to check the tense,
check the voice,

2231
01:45:19,155 --> 01:45:22,516
and which modifiers to use.

2232
01:45:23,551 --> 01:45:25,686
Besides filming lectures,

2233
01:45:25,733 --> 01:45:27,288
I plan the curriculum,

2234
01:45:27,333 --> 01:45:29,590
and make textbooks
and test questions myself.

2235
01:45:33,577 --> 01:45:37,665
I create content
to help students raise their grades.

2236
01:45:39,551 --> 01:45:43,271
(Jwa Hyeon, Visang Edu English instructor)

2237
01:45:45,995 --> 01:45:47,842
- No wonder her tone.
- Yeah.

2238
01:45:48,082 --> 01:45:49,948
- Now that I think about it...
- The teacher tone...

2239
01:45:49,948 --> 01:45:51,222
made me sleepy.

2240
01:45:51,224 --> 01:45:53,708
(No wonder her voice was
so easy to listen to.)

2241
01:45:53,815 --> 01:45:55,115
At yoga today, she was like...

2242
01:45:55,382 --> 01:45:56,517
"You're doing so well."

2243
01:45:57,840 --> 01:45:59,153
It was out of habit.

2244
01:45:59,687 --> 01:46:01,255
You must say it a lot.

2245
01:46:01,613 --> 01:46:02,656
That's so cool.

2246
01:46:03,573 --> 01:46:05,159
I'll flip the page.

2247
01:46:08,271 --> 01:46:10,271
Look at those chubby cheeks.

2248
01:46:10,318 --> 01:46:12,518
- The eyes are so big.
- Yeah.

2249
01:46:13,411 --> 01:46:14,535
- It's Ji Hwan.
- Ji Hwan.

2250
01:46:18,051 --> 01:46:18,973
Is it me?

2251
01:46:21,004 --> 01:46:22,443
Oh.

2252
01:46:22,624 --> 01:46:23,457
Ji Hwan.

2253
01:46:23,498 --> 01:46:24,645
It's Ji Hwan.

2254
01:46:24,924 --> 01:46:27,937
You're just a taller version.

2255
01:46:27,939 --> 01:46:29,578
(The chubby years)

2256
01:46:29,651 --> 01:46:30,951
I think that's me.

2257
01:46:31,685 --> 01:46:34,822
You suddenly slimmed down.

2258
01:46:35,155 --> 01:46:37,291
He lost his baby fat in between.

2259
01:46:37,524 --> 01:46:38,525
Is that a pull-up bar?

2260
01:46:38,861 --> 01:46:39,860
Lat pulldown.

2261
01:46:41,822 --> 01:46:43,230
You started working out that young?

2262
01:46:43,232 --> 01:46:44,682
- That's so cool.
- How old were you?

2263
01:46:45,966 --> 01:46:48,736
I was probably about 11 here.

2264
01:46:54,269 --> 01:46:56,777
- He's a swimmer.
- A swimmer.

2265
01:46:57,029 --> 01:46:58,379
A swimmer?

2266
01:47:07,834 --> 01:47:08,989
Swimming.

2267
01:47:09,234 --> 01:47:10,224
Swimming?

2268
01:47:11,392 --> 01:47:12,734
But what's going on there?

2269
01:47:13,460 --> 01:47:14,428
Is he upside down?

2270
01:47:14,430 --> 01:47:16,363
There's a handle here.

2271
01:47:16,620 --> 01:47:18,766
The backstroke start goes backward.

2272
01:47:19,034 --> 01:47:20,734
So you jump backward.

2273
01:47:21,402 --> 01:47:22,770
That's why it looks like that.

2274
01:47:24,168 --> 01:47:26,161
So those shoulders
didn't come from nowhere.

2275
01:47:26,188 --> 01:47:27,207
So you swim.

2276
01:47:27,207 --> 01:47:28,573
- That's so cool.
- Of course.

2277
01:47:29,595 --> 01:47:31,111
It's embarrassing. Let's turn the page.

2278
01:47:35,282 --> 01:47:36,951
- Right. You said you sing.
- That's right.

2279
01:47:36,953 --> 01:47:38,855
(Ji Hwan is busking.)

2280
01:47:38,962 --> 01:47:40,287
This is Hongdae.

2281
01:47:42,269 --> 01:47:45,426
- He's around when I walk around Hongdae.
- I think I've seen him.

2282
01:47:46,402 --> 01:47:48,402
(They might've seen him there.)

2283
01:47:49,729 --> 01:47:50,731
I'll read it.

2284
01:47:58,272 --> 01:48:01,308
Ji Hwan is really clumsy at dating.

2285
01:48:01,608 --> 01:48:05,212
He's practically never dated,
so it's kind of frustrating.

2286
01:48:07,147 --> 01:48:09,950
Even if he seems clumsy and awkward,

2287
01:48:10,250 --> 01:48:12,853
I promise there's real feeling...

2288
01:48:12,867 --> 01:48:14,388
and courage behind it.

2289
01:48:15,089 --> 01:48:18,802
He needs time to decide
and time to express himself.

2290
01:48:18,822 --> 01:48:20,361
So please give him a little time.

2291
01:48:21,228 --> 01:48:25,532
Since elementary school, Ji Hwan chased
his dream of the national team.

2292
01:48:25,722 --> 01:48:28,402
But the training was so intense
and overwhelming,

2293
01:48:28,836 --> 01:48:31,772
he once ran off to the mountains alone.

2294
01:48:32,740 --> 01:48:33,474
Wow.

2295
01:48:33,982 --> 01:48:36,449
(Embarrassing past on full display)

2296
01:48:37,362 --> 01:48:39,913
The whole family panicked
and searched for him.

2297
01:48:40,314 --> 01:48:42,695
And only after a long talk
to calm him down...

2298
01:48:42,709 --> 01:48:45,486
did he come down. I still remember it.

2299
01:48:45,853 --> 01:48:48,208
How innocent do you have to be
to run away to a mountain?

2300
01:48:49,089 --> 01:48:51,425
- Most kids go to an internet cafe.
- That's right.

2301
01:48:51,759 --> 01:48:53,193
Why is she telling that story?

2302
01:48:53,894 --> 01:48:56,397
But he pushed through that hard,

2303
01:48:56,964 --> 01:49:00,167
and made the most of his time,
working harder than anyone.

2304
01:49:00,567 --> 01:49:03,637
And that's what made him
the solid Ji Hwan he is now.

2305
01:49:04,138 --> 01:49:06,774
What do you think Ji Hwan does?

2306
01:49:08,050 --> 01:49:10,163
(Q. How was the intro
your older sister wrote?)

2307
01:49:10,370 --> 01:49:11,879
I really liked... No,

2308
01:49:11,963 --> 01:49:12,946
I didn't.

2309
01:49:12,977 --> 01:49:14,281
I didn't like it.

2310
01:49:15,103 --> 01:49:16,550
To sum it up...

2311
01:49:16,657 --> 01:49:17,651
"never dated,"

2312
01:49:17,935 --> 01:49:20,054
"got caught running around a mountain,"

2313
01:49:20,287 --> 01:49:21,321
"and what's his job?"

2314
01:49:22,689 --> 01:49:25,826
I checked if there was another page.

2315
01:49:27,394 --> 01:49:29,326
That's the problem.

2316
01:49:29,393 --> 01:49:31,298
He's stuck on the first line.

2317
01:49:31,298 --> 01:49:32,931
"Never dated." Which is true.

2318
01:49:33,039 --> 01:49:34,234
But he's so hung up on that,

2319
01:49:34,359 --> 01:49:37,471
he misses the whole point.

2320
01:49:37,659 --> 01:49:39,473
Classic little brother behavior.

2321
01:49:39,940 --> 01:49:42,407
Ran off to a mountain? Never dated?

2322
01:49:42,462 --> 01:49:43,877
Hearing that,

2323
01:49:44,211 --> 01:49:47,347
I remembered how he was on our date.

2324
01:49:48,248 --> 01:49:51,318
And I thought, "So that's why."

2325
01:49:52,619 --> 01:49:55,220
(She feels like she gets
Ji Hwan a bit more.)

2326
01:49:56,515 --> 01:49:59,560
- Isn't it better that she said all that?
- Yes.

2327
01:49:59,560 --> 01:50:02,362
Ji Hwan is so quiet,
people could misread him.

2328
01:50:02,397 --> 01:50:06,137
This feels like a super useful mechanic
for My Sibling's Romance.

2329
01:50:06,162 --> 01:50:06,884
Right.

2330
01:50:06,909 --> 01:50:09,008
When you clear up a misunderstanding
you had about someone...

2331
01:50:09,032 --> 01:50:10,109
through their family,

2332
01:50:10,133 --> 01:50:13,024
you realize,
"Oh, that's why they act that way."

2333
01:50:13,287 --> 01:50:15,887
It would've been great
if Min Seo had known this before going in.

2334
01:50:15,927 --> 01:50:18,766
"What kind of work does Ji Hwan do?"

2335
01:50:19,607 --> 01:50:20,468
A swimmer?

2336
01:50:21,267 --> 01:50:23,067
Or a singer-songwriter?

2337
01:50:23,187 --> 01:50:25,367
A singer-songwriter
who's good at swimming?

2338
01:50:26,689 --> 01:50:27,717
My occupation is...

2339
01:50:29,793 --> 01:50:32,101
I'm a former swimmer, and...

2340
01:50:32,847 --> 01:50:37,141
I'm currently a college student
majoring in Physical Education...

2341
01:50:37,165 --> 01:50:39,307
at Kyung Hee University.

2342
01:50:45,715 --> 01:50:48,784
I'm studying Physical Education
at Kyung Hee University,

2343
01:50:50,756 --> 01:50:53,555
and I swam competitively
up until high school...

2344
01:50:56,065 --> 01:50:58,427
before quitting due to an injury,

2345
01:50:58,910 --> 01:51:01,342
and now I work as a swim instructor.

2346
01:51:05,993 --> 01:51:09,171
Right now, to help people
dealing with injuries like I did,

2347
01:51:09,195 --> 01:51:13,254
I'm gaining hands-on experience
at an athletic rehab center.

2348
01:51:14,184 --> 01:51:17,084
(Ji Hwan,
swim instructor, college student)

2349
01:51:17,656 --> 01:51:21,161
So are you a singer too?

2350
01:51:21,186 --> 01:51:24,531
No, that's purely just a hobby of mine.

2351
01:51:24,683 --> 01:51:28,702
I'm usually not the type to step up
and put myself out there,

2352
01:51:29,021 --> 01:51:31,806
but singing is the one thing
I step forward for.

2353
01:51:33,797 --> 01:51:34,709
Singing only.

2354
01:51:36,847 --> 01:51:38,252
It's actually pretty embarrassing,
you know?

2355
01:51:38,277 --> 01:51:40,737
Doing it in front
of a huge crowd of people.

2356
01:51:41,121 --> 01:51:46,241
Still, whether I'm up there singing
or walking off afterward,

2357
01:51:46,621 --> 01:51:51,446
just knowing I mustered up the courage
and pulled it off...

2358
01:51:51,703 --> 01:51:52,660
felt really great.

2359
01:51:53,675 --> 01:51:56,318
The parts of myself that need to change
should obviously change,

2360
01:51:56,342 --> 01:51:58,120
and I really want to change too.

2361
01:51:58,144 --> 01:52:02,224
Because I feel like I'm growing
bit by bit in front of others,

2362
01:52:02,857 --> 01:52:06,607
even now, I still go up and sing
without hesitation.

2363
01:52:09,117 --> 01:52:11,530
- People who love singing...
- I know, right? It's amazing.

2364
01:52:11,554 --> 01:52:15,237
they seem to have this drive
to just push forward.

2365
01:52:16,283 --> 01:52:18,319
- And it's fun in itself.
- Really?

2366
01:52:19,416 --> 01:52:23,912
Hearing that he loves singing
so much made me curious,

2367
01:52:23,936 --> 01:52:27,849
and since I love singing too,
having that in common...

2368
01:52:28,093 --> 01:52:30,731
made me want to talk to him more.

2369
01:52:32,103 --> 01:52:33,234
Shall we check the next one?

2370
01:52:33,431 --> 01:52:34,637
I want to hear him sing.

2371
01:52:34,698 --> 01:52:35,784
(Now only one person remains.)

2372
01:52:36,236 --> 01:52:38,415
- Yu Ra.
- It's Yu Ra.

2373
01:52:42,080 --> 01:52:42,910
It's her all right.

2374
01:52:43,911 --> 01:52:44,970
So cute.

2375
01:52:45,003 --> 01:52:46,619
(Fierce gaze)

2376
01:52:46,737 --> 01:52:47,648
Cute.

2377
01:52:47,673 --> 01:52:49,116
Why am I last?

2378
01:52:52,644 --> 01:52:54,088
Ballet?

2379
01:52:55,084 --> 01:52:56,344
She's so cute here too.

2380
01:52:56,450 --> 01:52:58,225
Well, she was little back then, so...

2381
01:52:58,726 --> 01:53:01,083
She looks like she might be a dancer.

2382
01:53:02,863 --> 01:53:03,764
Dance?

2383
01:53:06,142 --> 01:53:08,842
(This time, she's playing flute.)

2384
01:53:09,528 --> 01:53:11,271
Isn't that really hard to play?

2385
01:53:11,530 --> 01:53:13,908
It was just a school orchestra, though,

2386
01:53:14,338 --> 01:53:15,810
I was the principal first chair.

2387
01:53:16,961 --> 01:53:19,413
- Impressive.
- You must have been amazing.

2388
01:53:20,487 --> 01:53:22,482
A total prodigy.

2389
01:53:25,837 --> 01:53:27,087
Shall we flip to the next one?

2390
01:53:31,772 --> 01:53:33,393
- Oh, a lab coat?
- A lab coat?

2391
01:53:34,253 --> 01:53:36,677
(Suddenly appearing in a lab coat)

2392
01:53:37,604 --> 01:53:38,692
A doctor...

2393
01:53:38,717 --> 01:53:39,812
Looks like she's a doctor.

2394
01:53:39,836 --> 01:53:41,669
Don't tell me she's
another Korean medicine doctor.

2395
01:53:41,697 --> 01:53:42,797
Could be a research lab too.

2396
01:53:42,897 --> 01:53:45,277
Oh, it could be a lab. Right.

2397
01:53:45,369 --> 01:53:46,540
- A lab coat?
- A lab coat?

2398
01:53:50,017 --> 01:53:51,537
Maybe a pharmacist?

2399
01:53:51,977 --> 01:53:53,380
Yeah, she gives off pharmacist vibes.

2400
01:53:56,847 --> 01:53:58,552
She looks like a dentist.

2401
01:53:58,987 --> 01:54:01,547
- A pharmacist...
- I think she might be a pharmacist too.

2402
01:54:02,527 --> 01:54:03,223
Pharmacist?

2403
01:54:03,587 --> 01:54:04,358
Pharmacist!

2404
01:54:05,847 --> 01:54:07,461
She really does look like a pharmacist.

2405
01:54:09,733 --> 01:54:11,899
This is the last one.

2406
01:54:12,606 --> 01:54:15,460
(The final introduction letter
has arrived.)

2407
01:54:15,967 --> 01:54:17,104
I'll read it.

2408
01:54:17,627 --> 01:54:20,362
"Round-faced Yu Ra is someone
without a sharp edge to her,"

2409
01:54:20,386 --> 01:54:22,109
"just like her appearance."

2410
01:54:22,807 --> 01:54:25,914
"Whenever a troublemaker like me
upset our parents,"

2411
01:54:26,058 --> 01:54:29,283
"Yu Ra always kept the peace at home
with her cute antics."

2412
01:54:30,114 --> 01:54:32,174
"Even if a restaurant gets
our order wrong,"

2413
01:54:32,388 --> 01:54:35,410
"or when we're startled by a car
suddenly cutting us off,"

2414
01:54:35,723 --> 01:54:37,212
"far from getting angry,"

2415
01:54:37,236 --> 01:54:40,661
"Yu Ra puts everyone at ease
with her gentle words."

2416
01:54:41,100 --> 01:54:43,664
"The people she's drawn to
seem similar to her too."

2417
01:54:44,266 --> 01:54:46,598
"She likes bear-like guys
who are gentle and sweet..."

2418
01:54:46,622 --> 01:54:48,101
"in both looks and personality."

2419
01:54:53,745 --> 01:54:56,165
(Who best fits her type?)

2420
01:54:56,747 --> 01:54:58,112
Dong Su.

2421
01:54:59,186 --> 01:55:00,581
Doesn't he look like a bear?

2422
01:55:02,067 --> 01:55:04,827
"Ever since she was young,
Yu Ra knew exactly what she wanted to do."

2423
01:55:05,266 --> 01:55:06,921
"After watching medical dramas,"

2424
01:55:06,945 --> 01:55:09,845
"she endlessly chattered on
about life and the human body,"

2425
01:55:10,215 --> 01:55:12,341
"and eventually, after a long,
grueling period of exam prep,"

2426
01:55:12,365 --> 01:55:14,695
"she got into the major she wanted."

2427
01:55:15,573 --> 01:55:17,898
"What kind of work does Yu Ra do?"

2428
01:55:19,753 --> 01:55:21,242
(It's already been narrowed down
quite a bit.)

2429
01:55:21,267 --> 01:55:23,122
- A doctor.
- Doctor.

2430
01:55:23,147 --> 01:55:24,037
A med student?

2431
01:55:24,967 --> 01:55:27,141
Something tells me
she's still a college student.

2432
01:55:27,600 --> 01:55:29,876
I'm not a med student.

2433
01:55:30,620 --> 01:55:35,816
I'm currently in dental school.

2434
01:55:37,245 --> 01:55:38,798
(Dental School)

2435
01:55:38,823 --> 01:55:43,727
I'm a dental student
studying to become a dentist.

2436
01:55:45,920 --> 01:55:47,735
Right now in dental school,

2437
01:55:47,759 --> 01:55:50,964
starting from basic knowledge
of teeth and oral anatomy,

2438
01:55:55,410 --> 01:55:57,051
I'm learning everything...

2439
01:55:57,082 --> 01:55:59,948
from the causes and diagnosis
of various dental diseases...

2440
01:55:59,973 --> 01:56:02,777
to the clinical knowledge
needed for treatment.

2441
01:56:05,186 --> 01:56:06,214
After graduation,

2442
01:56:06,238 --> 01:56:09,905
I plan to complete an internship
and residency at a university hospital,

2443
01:56:10,061 --> 01:56:13,921
with the ultimate goal
of becoming a dental specialist.

2444
01:56:15,865 --> 01:56:19,165
(Yu Ra, college student)

2445
01:56:20,294 --> 01:56:21,262
A dentist...

2446
01:56:22,468 --> 01:56:25,307
I was shocked
that you guessed it right away.

2447
01:56:25,420 --> 01:56:27,534
We won't have to worry
about our health at all.

2448
01:56:28,023 --> 01:56:28,702
Right?

2449
01:56:28,855 --> 01:56:30,905
We've got
a Korean medicine doctor here too.

2450
01:56:34,126 --> 01:56:35,909
Which dental school do you go to?

2451
01:56:36,360 --> 01:56:37,477
Kangwon National University.

2452
01:56:42,367 --> 01:56:43,417
A college student...

2453
01:56:43,726 --> 01:56:44,718
A college student?

2454
01:56:44,793 --> 01:56:46,253
I did have that thought earlier.

2455
01:56:46,666 --> 01:56:49,337
I was hoping to meet someone
already in the workforce.

2456
01:56:51,040 --> 01:56:52,460
I'm curious about her age.

2457
01:56:52,887 --> 01:56:54,837
I think we'll need to hear how old she is.

2458
01:56:54,862 --> 01:56:56,187
I really can't get a read on it.

2459
01:56:56,307 --> 01:56:58,007
It sounds like she took
the college entrance exam a few times.

2460
01:56:58,032 --> 01:57:00,012
Plus, she's living in Gangwon-do.

2461
01:57:00,115 --> 01:57:00,935
Yu Ra...

2462
01:57:03,420 --> 01:57:05,626
Location always seems
super important to Dong Su.

2463
01:57:05,651 --> 01:57:07,474
- Right.
- Total long distance.

2464
01:57:07,774 --> 01:57:09,276
Wouldn't she be graduating soon, though?

2465
01:57:09,421 --> 01:57:10,686
It's complicated.

2466
01:57:10,711 --> 01:57:13,602
Most of them are
in that transitional stage...

2467
01:57:13,626 --> 01:57:15,570
from student to working adult,

2468
01:57:15,594 --> 01:57:19,091
so revealing their occupations
lets everyone guess their ages,

2469
01:57:19,115 --> 01:57:21,413
leaving plenty of people
overwhelmed with worry.

2470
01:57:21,437 --> 01:57:22,338
True.

2471
01:57:22,362 --> 01:57:25,091
I'm curious to see
how this will affect things.

2472
01:57:25,973 --> 01:57:27,840
(Everyone's occupations
have been revealed.)

2473
01:57:27,865 --> 01:57:29,541
I can't believe
they revealed them this early.

2474
01:57:29,565 --> 01:57:30,564
- I know, right?
- Exactly.

2475
01:57:34,895 --> 01:57:37,146
(A text message has arrived.)

2476
01:57:37,573 --> 01:57:39,819
(Day 2 in the house:
Who made your heart flutter?)

2477
01:57:39,820 --> 01:57:42,972
(Send us their name and a message,
and we will deliver it anonymously.)

2478
01:57:43,247 --> 01:57:44,511
Just like this, right away?

2479
01:57:44,610 --> 01:57:45,278
Right away?

2480
01:57:45,979 --> 01:57:46,780
Amazing.

2481
01:57:47,133 --> 01:57:48,716
I am pretty curious, though.

2482
01:57:48,741 --> 01:57:50,351
Could things have changed
that drastically?

2483
01:57:50,448 --> 01:57:51,587
Right this instant?

2484
01:57:51,667 --> 01:57:53,347
I don't think things will change
immediately.

2485
01:57:53,480 --> 01:57:56,840
These realistic concerns are starting
to sink in a little more.

2486
01:57:57,067 --> 01:57:59,427
I think there's going to be
a slight shift.

2487
01:58:00,047 --> 01:58:02,307
Won't most of the changes
come from the women's side?

2488
01:58:02,439 --> 01:58:03,663
- Rather than the men's?
- Yes.

2489
01:58:04,175 --> 01:58:07,041
(Sending their hearts for the first time
since moving in)

2490
01:58:11,197 --> 01:58:13,874
You're supposed to text the person
who made your heart flutter.

2491
01:58:14,290 --> 01:58:18,345
Having anonymity guaranteed
actually made it really hard.

2492
01:58:18,763 --> 01:58:20,480
How should I word it?

2493
01:58:22,297 --> 01:58:24,351
How bold should I be?

2494
01:58:31,633 --> 01:58:33,727
Will she send one to me? Will I get one?

2495
01:58:37,431 --> 01:58:40,769
(After careful thought,
they send their texts one by one.)

2496
01:58:41,588 --> 01:58:44,089
(Everyone's feelings have been delivered.)

2497
01:58:45,747 --> 01:58:48,742
My shoulder actually feels worse
after doing yoga today.

2498
01:58:49,289 --> 01:58:52,452
Then she should treat you right away.

2499
01:58:52,476 --> 01:58:54,348
I should've brought
my acupuncture needles.

2500
01:58:55,167 --> 01:58:56,917
- I could've given you acupuncture.
- That's so cool.

2501
01:58:57,146 --> 01:59:00,587
Honestly, if you took
a yoga class today...

2502
01:59:01,348 --> 01:59:05,935
(Let's make Dubai chewy cookies together.
Great job today.)

2503
01:59:06,753 --> 01:59:08,184
I sent mine straight to Ye In.

2504
01:59:08,209 --> 01:59:09,706
I didn't even have to think twice.

2505
01:59:09,731 --> 01:59:12,032
I just figured, let's send it fast
and get out of here fast.

2506
01:59:12,341 --> 01:59:14,034
- "Get out of here?"
- Where are you flying off to?

2507
01:59:14,307 --> 01:59:16,103
In Joong is always fast, no matter what.

2508
01:59:16,967 --> 01:59:18,672
I literally just fired it off right away.

2509
01:59:19,597 --> 01:59:22,050
(In Joong was the fastest
to send his text.)

2510
01:59:22,673 --> 01:59:24,193
I regretted it a little
right after sending it.

2511
01:59:24,218 --> 01:59:25,679
It feels way too casual, doesn't it?

2512
01:59:25,993 --> 01:59:29,427
I wish I had written,
"It was fun today," instead.

2513
01:59:29,946 --> 01:59:33,167
Saying "Great job today"
feels a bit lacking.

2514
01:59:33,266 --> 01:59:34,709
I told myself that next time,

2515
01:59:34,733 --> 01:59:36,890
I need to take things a little slower
when sending a text.

2516
01:59:41,835 --> 01:59:43,318
(Thanks to you,
I lost track of time today.)

2517
01:59:43,342 --> 01:59:45,158
(I'll listen to the song
you recommended next time!)

2518
01:59:45,573 --> 01:59:48,001
The second I saw that,
I couldn't hide my smile.

2519
01:59:48,907 --> 01:59:49,927
It just felt amazing.

2520
01:59:49,952 --> 01:59:51,805
It felt really great, but...

2521
01:59:52,613 --> 01:59:54,863
I did find myself wondering
whether she texted me...

2522
01:59:54,888 --> 01:59:56,599
simply because we spent time
together today,

2523
01:59:56,977 --> 02:00:00,514
or if she's genuinely interested in me.

2524
02:00:01,822 --> 02:00:05,447
(In Joong and Ye In chose each other.)

2525
02:00:05,820 --> 02:00:08,255
I'm practically ready to start
learning yoga right now.

2526
02:00:09,896 --> 02:00:12,325
- You must've been really impressed.
- I know, right?

2527
02:00:17,404 --> 02:00:19,417
(It's nice seeing you smile all the time!)

2528
02:00:19,441 --> 02:00:23,801
(I'd love to spend some time together
if we get the chance.)

2529
02:00:24,319 --> 02:00:26,419
Is this from Ji Hwan?

2530
02:00:27,080 --> 02:00:28,430
Even though it's anonymous,

2531
02:00:28,454 --> 02:00:31,420
I wanted to express my feelings
to Min Seo a bit,

2532
02:00:31,640 --> 02:00:34,040
so I wrote that right away
with that in mind.

2533
02:00:35,069 --> 02:00:37,784
Min Seo laughs really easily.

2534
02:00:38,652 --> 02:00:41,938
(Min Seo, who laughed a lot
throughout their date)

2535
02:00:43,226 --> 02:00:45,025
She's super bright.

2536
02:00:46,706 --> 02:00:50,597
Bit by bit, my fondness for her
kept growing.

2537
02:00:53,360 --> 02:00:55,769
I thought about it really hard.

2538
02:00:56,014 --> 02:00:57,525
Because for me,

2539
02:00:57,549 --> 02:01:00,628
having the same sense of humor
and good conversation is a must.

2540
02:01:00,652 --> 02:01:02,642
Do you like octopus?

2541
02:01:04,951 --> 02:01:06,179
Yeah.

2542
02:01:07,276 --> 02:01:09,082
Oh...

2543
02:01:09,347 --> 02:01:10,183
Seriously.

2544
02:01:11,017 --> 02:01:12,219
This tone is...

2545
02:01:12,676 --> 02:01:15,915
If that were me,
I would've bolted outside crying.

2546
02:01:16,831 --> 02:01:18,158
Crying like this.

2547
02:01:18,687 --> 02:01:20,227
- Because my feelings were so hurt.
- Right.

2548
02:01:21,027 --> 02:01:22,763
Do you like octopus?

2549
02:01:25,322 --> 02:01:26,099
Yeah.

2550
02:01:35,896 --> 02:01:38,465
If it's like this,
isn't that a bit awkward?

2551
02:01:38,510 --> 02:01:39,472
This is tricky.

2552
02:01:39,916 --> 02:01:42,435
Isn't this the definition
of being on different pages?

2553
02:01:43,110 --> 02:01:45,278
One person had a rough time,
and the other says he had a great time.

2554
02:01:45,711 --> 02:01:47,413
Then on the other hand,
earlier that morning,

2555
02:01:47,438 --> 02:01:50,585
Jin Sung even gave me vitamins.

2556
02:01:50,615 --> 02:01:51,823
(This morning)

2557
02:01:51,848 --> 02:01:53,737
Min Seo, would you like some vitamins?

2558
02:01:53,977 --> 02:01:55,295
Vitamins? Oh, sure!

2559
02:01:55,660 --> 02:01:58,306
(Vitamins he gave only to Min Seo)

2560
02:01:59,412 --> 02:02:03,391
That suddenly popped back into my head,

2561
02:02:03,971 --> 02:02:07,722
so I typed Jin Sung's name in my phone,
then typed Ji Hwan's name,

2562
02:02:08,266 --> 02:02:10,176
and went back and forth over it
quite a bit.

2563
02:02:17,230 --> 02:02:21,154
(Make sure to stretch your arms well
before going to sleep.)

2564
02:02:22,795 --> 02:02:24,835
(Smile)

2565
02:02:26,069 --> 02:02:27,293
It's from Min Seo.

2566
02:02:29,397 --> 02:02:31,298
Ji Hwan is hilarious.

2567
02:02:32,763 --> 02:02:34,467
He's oblivious to how she's feeling.

2568
02:02:34,958 --> 02:02:36,837
- He's super into her.
- I know, right?

2569
02:02:38,643 --> 02:02:41,081
We stretched our arms out together.

2570
02:02:43,038 --> 02:02:45,013
I sent mine to Ji Hwan.

2571
02:02:45,038 --> 02:02:46,879
(After deliberating,
Min Seo sent her text to Ji Hwan.)

2572
02:02:47,157 --> 02:02:51,051
He's someone I have my eye on,

2573
02:02:54,583 --> 02:02:56,778
and we had a fun day together today,

2574
02:02:56,802 --> 02:03:00,127
so I wanted to drop a subtle hint
that it was me when I sent it.

2575
02:03:00,961 --> 02:03:04,352
Right after something ends,
I always think, "What did I mess up?"

2576
02:03:04,376 --> 02:03:07,601
I was hoping I'd get a text
that would stop those thoughts.

2577
02:03:07,857 --> 02:03:10,437
So it felt like a bit of a relief.

2578
02:03:11,484 --> 02:03:14,188
(Min Seo and Ji Hwan chose each other.)

2579
02:03:14,847 --> 02:03:17,419
(One person chose your sibling.)

2580
02:03:19,138 --> 02:03:22,303
I'm pretty sure it's Min Seo,
since we went rock climbing together.

2581
02:03:22,768 --> 02:03:25,018
Thank you so much for sending it.

2582
02:03:30,507 --> 02:03:31,946
I received a text saying,

2583
02:03:31,970 --> 02:03:34,060
"Thank you for making
unforgettable memories with me."

2584
02:03:34,393 --> 02:03:36,329
I think Yu Ra sent this.

2585
02:03:36,475 --> 02:03:40,054
I felt like we had a fun day
together today,

2586
02:03:40,163 --> 02:03:44,325
and Jin Sung took such sweet care of me,

2587
02:03:44,712 --> 02:03:46,594
so I sent mine to Jin Sung,

2588
02:03:46,618 --> 02:03:50,336
who went surfing and ate meat with me
even though it was tough.

2589
02:03:54,308 --> 02:03:58,087
Most people end up texting their date
after going out.

2590
02:03:58,112 --> 02:04:00,220
That good impression usually
lasts through that day.

2591
02:04:00,400 --> 02:04:02,289
I went to Korea University.

2592
02:04:02,587 --> 02:04:03,587
Really?

2593
02:04:05,207 --> 02:04:06,767
May I ask what your original major was?

2594
02:04:06,792 --> 02:04:08,161
Division of Life Sciences.

2595
02:04:09,833 --> 02:04:12,098
- So it's kind of a similar field.
- Yes.

2596
02:04:12,123 --> 02:04:15,590
Along that natural sciences,
life sciences track.

2597
02:04:18,263 --> 02:04:22,475
We talked really comfortably
while on my date with Yu Ra.

2598
02:04:22,710 --> 02:04:24,444
Our tastes seem to match well too.

2599
02:04:24,794 --> 02:04:29,270
Still, I hadn't gotten the chance
to talk much with Min Seo,

2600
02:04:29,566 --> 02:04:32,819
so I agonized over who to send my text to.

2601
02:04:41,109 --> 02:04:44,587
(Let's go running next time.)

2602
02:04:44,635 --> 02:04:45,398
Oh!

2603
02:04:47,863 --> 02:04:49,223
Seriously?

2604
02:04:49,681 --> 02:04:51,657
Things are about to get confusing.

2605
02:04:51,684 --> 02:04:53,083
(Jin Sung didn't text Yu Ra,
whom he went on a date with.)

2606
02:04:53,727 --> 02:04:54,874
Jin Sung?

2607
02:04:55,747 --> 02:04:59,479
Wait, Jin Sung went on a date
with Yu Ra today,

2608
02:04:59,874 --> 02:05:01,681
yet he sent a text to me?

2609
02:05:02,433 --> 02:05:05,418
I think I felt both puzzled and fluttery.
Half and half.

2610
02:05:06,506 --> 02:05:08,154
I sent mine to Min Seo.

2611
02:05:09,409 --> 02:05:12,880
My interest in Min Seo is stronger,

2612
02:05:12,904 --> 02:05:15,783
and I wanted to get to know her better,

2613
02:05:15,807 --> 02:05:18,831
so I casually suggested
going for a run together.

2614
02:05:21,901 --> 02:05:24,568
(Two people chose your sibling.)

2615
02:05:24,593 --> 02:05:25,553
What is this?

2616
02:05:26,500 --> 02:05:28,374
My sibling got two votes.

2617
02:05:29,809 --> 02:05:31,194
(Chuckles)

2618
02:05:31,753 --> 02:05:35,937
I figured one text was from Ji Hwan
since they went on a date,

2619
02:05:36,551 --> 02:05:37,690
and since there were two votes,

2620
02:05:37,714 --> 02:05:39,753
I naturally assumed
the other was from Jin Sung.

2621
02:05:40,621 --> 02:05:44,396
(Min Seo was chosen by two people.)

2622
02:05:44,616 --> 02:05:46,239
Did you manage to catch a wave
on your own?

2623
02:05:46,264 --> 02:05:47,928
- For about one second?
- Really?

2624
02:05:47,953 --> 02:05:49,733
Honestly, surfing was
what I envied the most.

2625
02:05:49,878 --> 02:05:51,664
- It was really hard.
- You fall right off.

2626
02:05:54,087 --> 02:05:58,065
(Getting lamb chops together
would be amazing too.)

2627
02:05:58,313 --> 02:06:00,540
Lamb skewers had come up
during our conversation.

2628
02:06:00,827 --> 02:06:02,008
Any kind of meat works.

2629
02:06:02,167 --> 02:06:03,307
I love lamb.

2630
02:06:03,835 --> 02:06:04,778
Lamb skewers...

2631
02:06:04,967 --> 02:06:06,647
- I really, truly love them.
- I love them too.

2632
02:06:06,979 --> 02:06:09,085
I love lamb paired with kaoliang liquor.

2633
02:06:09,110 --> 02:06:10,850
With a splash of beer mixed right in...

2634
02:06:11,062 --> 02:06:12,549
If we get the chance next time,

2635
02:06:12,573 --> 02:06:15,270
I'd love for us to have lamb chops
and lamb skewers.

2636
02:06:15,600 --> 02:06:17,090
We're both totally into it.

2637
02:06:17,187 --> 02:06:19,487
I hope there comes a day
we can eat it together.

2638
02:06:19,532 --> 02:06:21,561
If the opportunity comes up,

2639
02:06:21,606 --> 02:06:23,827
I want to go on another date with Dong Su,

2640
02:06:23,851 --> 02:06:25,799
so that's why I sent that.

2641
02:06:27,900 --> 02:06:30,270
I'm probably the very last person
to send mine.

2642
02:06:30,713 --> 02:06:31,771
Why did he wait so long?

2643
02:06:31,796 --> 02:06:32,942
Did he do that on purpose?

2644
02:06:32,967 --> 02:06:35,975
No, maybe he was torn
between her and Yu Ra.

2645
02:06:36,000 --> 02:06:38,480
I'm probably the very last person
to send mine.

2646
02:06:39,214 --> 02:06:40,279
I kind of...

2647
02:06:41,920 --> 02:06:45,900
Between the person I spent today with
and my first-impression pick,

2648
02:06:48,483 --> 02:06:50,056
I deliberated quite a bit.

2649
02:06:51,520 --> 02:06:54,167
The person my heart leans toward?

2650
02:06:57,456 --> 02:06:59,726
(Jwa Hyeon, with whom he shared
a romantic day)

2651
02:07:01,434 --> 02:07:04,478
(Yu Ra, with whom he spent the night
at the Love Hideout)

2652
02:07:04,804 --> 02:07:08,186
(Where does Dong Su's heart point?)

2653
02:07:17,771 --> 02:07:20,105
(Thank you for boosting my confidence
today.)

2654
02:07:20,800 --> 02:07:23,101
(Dong Su chose Jwa Hyeon.)

2655
02:07:23,126 --> 02:07:24,271
Today really wasn't...

2656
02:07:24,302 --> 02:07:26,347
"Thank you for boosting my confidence
today."

2657
02:07:26,373 --> 02:07:27,325
Did she boost his confidence?

2658
02:07:27,326 --> 02:07:30,144
She did that patting thing today,
going, "Good job, such a good job,"

2659
02:07:30,175 --> 02:07:31,764
and he must have really liked that.

2660
02:07:32,712 --> 02:07:36,503
(Thank you for boosting my confidence
today.)

2661
02:07:37,107 --> 02:07:39,439
Dong Su sent it to me.

2662
02:07:40,903 --> 02:07:42,175
I sent mine to Jwa Hyeon.

2663
02:07:42,633 --> 02:07:46,734
Since today was such a wonderful day
spent with Jwa Hyeon,

2664
02:07:47,371 --> 02:07:49,082
I sent mine to her.

2665
02:07:49,107 --> 02:07:50,867
(Dong Su and Jwa Hyeon chose each other.)

2666
02:07:51,357 --> 02:07:55,363
(One person chose your sibling.)

2667
02:08:00,863 --> 02:08:04,457
I literally jumped up and down inside.

2668
02:08:05,303 --> 02:08:07,234
She didn't get any the first time around.

2669
02:08:07,689 --> 02:08:11,325
Seeing my sister like that broke my heart,

2670
02:08:11,931 --> 02:08:13,753
so knowing how thrilled she must be,

2671
02:08:14,404 --> 02:08:16,285
I was genuinely so happy.

2672
02:08:18,104 --> 02:08:20,947
(One person chose your sibling.)

2673
02:08:21,256 --> 02:08:22,281
It's Jwa Hyeon!

2674
02:08:22,507 --> 02:08:24,172
Since they spent time together,

2675
02:08:24,196 --> 02:08:26,620
Jwa Hyeon must have given hers
to my brother.

2676
02:08:34,492 --> 02:08:37,975
(No one chose you.)

2677
02:08:38,865 --> 02:08:40,333
Oh no.

2678
02:08:41,770 --> 02:08:44,297
- It was just one date, though.
- Right.

2679
02:08:44,504 --> 02:08:47,073
(No one chose you.)

2680
02:08:49,127 --> 02:08:52,107
I did expect it to some extent.

2681
02:08:53,841 --> 02:08:57,638
Dong Su came back from doing yoga
with Jwa Hyeon...

2682
02:08:57,913 --> 02:09:00,074
looking super happy,

2683
02:09:01,233 --> 02:09:03,356
and we barely had any chance to talk.

2684
02:09:03,936 --> 02:09:09,083
And while Jin Sung and I had
a fun time together today,

2685
02:09:09,676 --> 02:09:13,225
it felt like our conversation was purely
just lighthearted fun.

2686
02:09:14,193 --> 02:09:16,502
So I figured he might not send it to me.

2687
02:09:21,313 --> 02:09:25,900
Still, actually seeing
"No one chose you." on my screen...

2688
02:09:27,056 --> 02:09:28,915
didn't feel very good.

2689
02:09:33,212 --> 02:09:34,554
I felt a little hurt.

2690
02:09:38,187 --> 02:09:41,628
It was a moment where it really hit me...

2691
02:09:41,652 --> 02:09:43,696
just how huge each individual date is.

2692
02:09:45,766 --> 02:09:51,106
I'm dying to know
what Dong Su thinks of me right now.

2693
02:09:51,346 --> 02:09:52,705
I'm so, so curious.

2694
02:09:54,147 --> 02:09:57,854
(A second night where excitement
and disappointment cross paths)

2695
02:09:57,987 --> 02:09:59,712
This is tough.

2696
02:10:00,547 --> 02:10:02,482
Things are going to get super tangled up.

2697
02:10:03,213 --> 02:10:06,752
How did things get so complicated
in just two days?

2698
02:10:06,785 --> 02:10:08,154
This has turned into a complete pretzel.

2699
02:10:08,179 --> 02:10:10,690
Usually, things stay pretty steady
through the first two days.

2700
02:10:13,427 --> 02:10:15,775
(Yu Ra comes up to the room.)

2701
02:10:27,346 --> 02:10:30,084
(She opens her notebook...)

2702
02:10:33,052 --> 02:10:36,728
(and quietly begins
writing something down.)

2703
02:10:44,223 --> 02:10:46,594
(Day 2: Is this some kind of payback?)

2704
02:10:46,618 --> 02:10:50,176
(I'm feeling more unsettled
than I thought.)

2705
02:10:51,584 --> 02:10:54,288
When I saw "No one chose you,"

2706
02:10:55,065 --> 02:10:57,277
Dong Su was the very first person
who came to mind.

2707
02:10:57,302 --> 02:10:58,237
Because...

2708
02:10:59,944 --> 02:11:02,144
when we went
to the first-impression cabin,

2709
02:11:02,175 --> 02:11:03,776
Dong Su chose me,

2710
02:11:04,704 --> 02:11:06,662
(Dong Su's first-impression pick, Yu Ra)

2711
02:11:06,857 --> 02:11:11,184
and when it was the women's turn
to choose, I picked Ji Hwan.

2712
02:11:16,842 --> 02:11:18,325
This calls for a drink.

2713
02:11:20,303 --> 02:11:23,673
And then after that,
I called Dong Su to the hideout.

2714
02:11:23,697 --> 02:11:25,966
Could you please send Dong Su in?

2715
02:11:26,446 --> 02:11:29,001
(Yu Ra called Dong Su
to the Love Hideout.)

2716
02:11:29,193 --> 02:11:32,193
So him choosing someone other than me...

2717
02:11:32,548 --> 02:11:34,979
was that kind of payback?

2718
02:11:52,720 --> 02:11:53,793
It's the Death Note.

2719
02:11:54,840 --> 02:11:58,677
I feel like Yu Ra is suddenly going
to awaken a whole new side.

2720
02:11:58,744 --> 02:12:00,323
Isn't she about to turn to the dark side?

2721
02:12:00,348 --> 02:12:03,236
What kind of villain arc would Yu Ra have?

2722
02:12:03,261 --> 02:12:04,788
Next time, we'll hear that drill buzzing.

2723
02:12:05,507 --> 02:12:07,549
- Who's going to do what to whom?
- Yu Ra is...

2724
02:12:07,589 --> 02:12:10,776
Dong Su wakes up from a nap
and doesn't have a single tooth left!

2725
02:12:11,344 --> 02:12:13,038
(Why didn't you text me?)

2726
02:12:13,063 --> 02:12:15,081
While Ye In is over there
sticking acupuncture needles!

2727
02:12:16,147 --> 02:12:17,984
"I'm sorry!"

2728
02:12:18,370 --> 02:12:19,419
I apologize.

2729
02:12:34,717 --> 02:12:36,216
Christmas on a midsummer night!

2730
02:12:37,023 --> 02:12:38,612
I love this!

2731
02:12:38,732 --> 02:12:42,191
(The siblings are invited
to a Christmas party.)

2732
02:12:42,216 --> 02:12:43,476
Great job, everyone.

2733
02:12:43,697 --> 02:12:46,817
- Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas.

2734
02:12:46,997 --> 02:12:48,661
"Hand-deliver a Christmas gift..."

2735
02:12:48,685 --> 02:12:50,877
"to the person you want
to go on a date with."

2736
02:12:51,196 --> 02:12:52,651
How could they make us do this?

2737
02:12:52,717 --> 02:12:54,397
Everyone can literally see
who gives it to whom.

2738
02:12:54,422 --> 02:12:55,988
I was seriously so nervous back then.

2739
02:12:56,150 --> 02:12:58,857
Will Yu Ra give hers to me?

2740
02:12:58,858 --> 02:13:00,917
She didn't get a text from Dong Su.

2741
02:13:00,942 --> 02:13:03,362
Do I need to refocus my heart a bit now?

2742
02:13:03,387 --> 02:13:05,932
She wouldn't suddenly want
to give hers to Ji Hwan, would she?

2743
02:13:05,957 --> 02:13:07,467
Deep down, I had my hopes up.

2744
02:13:07,570 --> 02:13:10,436
This might be my only chance right now.

2745
02:13:10,797 --> 02:13:12,004
Did you give it to them?

2746
02:13:13,506 --> 02:13:17,210
(Feelings beginning to show
right before their eyes)

2747
02:13:17,235 --> 02:13:18,611
You have to seize the opportunity.

2748
02:13:18,846 --> 02:13:19,972
I don't think
there's anything wrong with that.

2749
02:13:20,004 --> 02:13:21,427
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
